  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#generative_neural_network">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Generative Neural Network</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture designed to produce new data instances that mimic the properties of a training set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that learns a latent representation of data to synthesize new artificial instances.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that produces new data samples by approximating the distribution of targeted structures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model designed to approximate a likelihood function for the reconstruction of events.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model designed to synthesize new data samples by disentangling style and content representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model trained to sample new realizations of geological images that minimize the maximum mean discrepancy from an exemplar image.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model used as a path finder by treating 2D path planning as an image generation task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model architecture designed to learn and mimic complex probability distributions to generate new synthetic samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model that compresses inputs into the tangent space of a Lie group manifold to generate Gaussian distributed samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model trained to produce high-fidelity simulated observables to bypass computationally expensive low-level physics simulations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model trained to produce high-performance design layouts for the global optimization of metasurfaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model used as a prior in anytime sample-based decision-making processes to optimize bounded rationality models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed to sample probable sequences or structures, such as infection cascades, from observed data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to produce new data samples that mimic the distribution of a training set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network trained to predict spaces beyond the sensor horizon to improve robotic navigation and planning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial intelligence model used to synthesize molecules with specific chemical properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network designed to model the distribution of data to generate new, similar samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of deep learning model used to synthesize artificial surrogate faces for the purpose of identity deidentification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of model designed to learn the distribution of data to synthesize new, similar samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of neural network designed to model the underlying distribution of data to generate new, similar samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[produce new data instances that mimic the properties of a training set, produce new data samples that mimic the distribution of a training set] produce new data samples that mimic the distribution of a training set</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[approximate a likelihood function for the reconstruction of events] approximate a likelihood function for the reconstruction of events</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[synthesize new data samples by disentangling style and content representations] synthesize new data samples by disentangling style and content representations</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[learn and mimic complex probability distributions to generate new synthetic samples] learn and mimic complex probability distributions to generate new synthetic samples</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[sample probable sequences or structures] sample probable sequences or structures</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[model the distribution of data to generate new, learn the distribution of data to synthesize new, model the underlying distribution of data to generate new] model the distribution of data to generate new</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[new synthetic samples] synthetic samples</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[gaussian distributed samples] gaussian distributed samples</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[new] new</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[synthesize molecules with specific chemical properties] synthesize molecules with specific chemical properties</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[synthesize artificial surrogate faces for the purpose of identity deidentification] synthesize artificial surrogate faces for the purpose of identity deidentification</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[new artificial instances] new artificial instances</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[new data samples] new data samples</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[high-fidelity simulated observables] high-fidelity simulated observables</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[high-performance design layouts] high-performance design layouts</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[new realizations of geological images] new realizations of geological images</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[2D path planning as an image generation task] 2d path planning as an image generation task</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[bounded rationality models] bounded rationality models</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[spaces beyond the sensor horizon] spaces beyond the sensor horizon</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture designed to produce new data instances that mimic the properties of a training set.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that learns a latent representation of data to synthesize new artificial instances.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that produces new data samples by approximating the distribution of targeted structures.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning model designed to approximate a likelihood function for the reconstruction of events.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning model designed to synthesize new data samples by disentangling style and content representations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning model trained to sample new realizations of geological images that minimize the maximum mean discrepancy from an exemplar image.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning model used as a path finder by treating 2D path planning as an image generation task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model architecture designed to learn and mimic complex probability distributions to generate new synthetic samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model that compresses inputs into the tangent space of a Lie group manifold to generate Gaussian distributed samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model trained to produce high-fidelity simulated observables to bypass computationally expensive low-level physics simulations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model trained to produce high-performance design layouts for the global optimization of metasurfaces.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model used as a prior in anytime sample-based decision-making processes to optimize bounded rationality models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed to sample probable sequences or structures, such as infection cascades, from observed data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to produce new data samples that mimic the distribution of a training set.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network trained to predict spaces beyond the sensor horizon to improve robotic navigation and planning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of artificial intelligence model used to synthesize molecules with specific chemical properties.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network designed to model the distribution of data to generate new, similar samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of deep learning model used to synthesize artificial surrogate faces for the purpose of identity deidentification.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of model designed to learn the distribution of data to synthesize new, similar samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of neural network designed to model the underlying distribution of data to generate new, similar samples.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#probabilistic_and_specialized_networks"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#beta_variational_autoencoder">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Beta-Variational Autoencoder</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative architecture that introduces a hyperparameter to control the trade-off between reconstruction quality and latent disentanglement.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that introduces a hyperparameter to enforce disentanglement within the latent representation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that employs a hyperparameter to balance the disentanglement of latent factors and the quality of reconstruction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that encourages the learning of independent latent variables by penalizing the size of the latent vector.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to balance reconstruction quality and the disentanglement of latent representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to balance the trade-off between reconstruction accuracy and the latent space disentanglement.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to control the degree of disentanglement in the learned latent representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to encourage the disentanglement of latent factors in the representation of input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to encourage the disentanglement of latent representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to encourage the learning of disentangled and interpretable latent representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to encourage the learning of disentangled latent representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that learns disentangled latent variables to represent the parameters of graph topologies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that produces a compact latent space used to detect out-of-distribution images by encoding generative factors into a few latent variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that weights the KL divergence term in the loss function to encourage the learning of disentangled representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model with a partially disentangled latent space used to detect out-of-distribution conditions in time series images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised generative model that captures label information within a compressed latent representation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[detect out-of-distribution images by encoding generative factors into a few latent variables] out-of-distribution images by encoding generative factors into a few latent variables</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[detect out-of-distribution conditions in time series images] out-of-distribution conditions in time series images</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[out-of-distribution images by encoding generative factors into a few latent variables] out-of-distribution images by encoding generative factors into a few latent variables</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[out-of-distribution conditions in time series images] out-of-distribution conditions in time series images</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the learning of independent latent variables] learning of independent latent variables</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[disentangled latent variables] disentangled latent variables</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the KL divergence term] kl divergence term</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[label information] label information</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative architecture that introduces a hyperparameter to control the trade-off between reconstruction quality and latent disentanglement.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative framework that introduces a hyperparameter to enforce disentanglement within the latent representation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that employs a hyperparameter to balance the disentanglement of latent factors and the quality of reconstruction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that encourages the learning of independent latent variables by penalizing the size of the latent vector.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to balance reconstruction quality and the disentanglement of latent representations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to balance the trade-off between reconstruction accuracy and the latent space disentanglement.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to control the degree of disentanglement in the learned latent representations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to encourage the disentanglement of latent factors in the representation of input data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to encourage the disentanglement of latent representations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to encourage the learning of disentangled and interpretable latent representations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that introduces a hyperparameter to encourage the learning of disentangled latent representations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that learns disentangled latent variables to represent the parameters of graph topologies.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that produces a compact latent space used to detect out-of-distribution images by encoding generative factors into a few latent variables.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model that weights the KL divergence term in the loss function to encourage the learning of disentangled representations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model with a partially disentangled latent space used to detect out-of-distribution conditions in time series images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised generative model that captures label information within a compressed latent representation.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#autoencoder_based_models"/>
    <ml:hasComponent rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#hyperparameter"/>
    <ml:modifies rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#hyperparameter"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#reservoir_computing">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Reservoir Computing</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of recurrent neural networks with fixed random internal weights used to study complex dynamics and stability.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework for forecasting complex spatiotemporal dynamics using a fixed random recurrent network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that simplifies network training by using a fixed random reservoir of neurons and training only the output layer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that uses a fixed nonlinear dynamical system to project input into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that uses a fixed random dynamical system to map input signals into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that uses a fixed, random dynamical system to map input signals into a high-dimensional space for linear readout.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that uses a fixed, random dynamical system to map input signals into a high-dimensional space for prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that uses a fixed, random dynamical system to map inputs into a high-dimensional space for linear readout.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that uses a fixed, random dynamical system to map inputs into a high-dimensional space for linear regression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that uses a fixed, random dynamical system to map inputs into a high-dimensional space for simple linear readout.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that uses a fixed, random nonlinear dynamical system to map inputs into a high-dimensional space for linear regression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that uses a fixed, random recurrent neural network to map input signals into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that uses a fixed, random recurrent neural network to map inputs into a high-dimensional space for efficient training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that utilizes a fixed nonlinear dynamical system to process information via a trainable readout layer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that utilizes a fixed, random recurrent neural network to process spatio-temporal data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework used for the separation of superimposed chaotic signals without knowledge of the underlying dynamical equations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework using a fixed, random recurrent neural network where only the output layer is trained via linear regression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework using a network of oscillators to forecast the dynamics of complex systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational paradigm that projects input signals into a high-dimensional space to be solved with a linear readout.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational paradigm that uses a fixed, random recurrent neural network to map inputs into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computing framework that uses a fixed, random dynamical system to map input signals into a high-dimensional space for target output transformation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework derived from recurrent neural networks that uses a fixed random dynamical system to process temporal data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computation that uses a fixed, random dynamical system to map input signals into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computation that uses a fixed, random recurrent network to process temporal signals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computation that uses a fixed, random recursive network to map input signals into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computation using a fixed, random dynamical system as a reservoir to map inputs into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computation using a fixed, random recurrent neural network as a reservoir to map inputs into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computation where a fixed random dynamical system is used to map inputs into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computation where a fixed, random dynamical system is used to map input signals into a high-dimensional space for linear readout.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computation where a fixed, random dynamical system is used to map input signals into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computation where a fixed, random recurrent network is used to project inputs into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computing that uses a fixed, random dynamical system to map input signals into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computing where a fixed, random recurrent dynamical system is used to map inputs into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computing where a fixed, random recurrent neural network is used as a feature extractor for a trainable linear output layer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computing where a fixed, random recurrent neural network is used to map inputs into a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for computing with a fixed random dynamical system that is trained only at the output layer to predict chaotic dynamics.</rdfs:comment>
