  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#stochastic_gradient_descent">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Stochastic Gradient Descent</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed and asynchronized optimization algorithm used to solve data-fitting problems over networked systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed optimization algorithm that updates parameters using stochastic gradients to minimize a non-convex objective function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A first-order optimization algorithm that updates model parameters by estimating the gradient of the loss function using a small subset of training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A first-order optimization algorithm that updates model parameters using noisy gradient approximations from mini-batches of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A first-order optimization algorithm that updates model parameters using the gradient of a loss function estimated from a small subset of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A first-order optimization algorithm that updates model parameters using the gradient of the loss function estimated from a small batch of training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A first-order optimization method that approximates the gradient of a function using a subset of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fundamental optimization algorithm that updates model parameters using the gradient of a randomly sampled subset of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gradient-based optimization algorithm that updates model parameters by retracing steps using intermediate models to identify influential data instances.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gradient-based optimization algorithm that updates model parameters using a subset of the training data to minimize a loss function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gradient-based optimization algorithm that updates model parameters using small random subsets of the training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gradient-based optimization method that updates model parameters using adaptive learning rates to minimize objective functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A stochastic optimization algorithm that regularizes generalization error by decorrelating nearby updates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A stochastic optimization procedure that updates model parameters to minimize a loss function without requiring manual learning rate settings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An incremental optimization algorithm used to find the direction of maximal variance in streaming principal component analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for optimizing an objective function by updating parameters based on a small subset of training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for optimizing an objective function with respect to parameters using randomly chosen samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for optimizing an objective function with suitable smoothness by using randomly selected samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for optimizing an objective function with suitable smoothness properties by using randomly sampled gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm extended with adaptive learning rates and finite-difference Hessian approximations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm for empirical risk minimization that can suffer from stalling before reaching the global minimizer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm for least-squares regression where multiple passes over data can improve predictive performance in hard problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm for minimizing a loss function using an adaptive learning rate based on extrapolation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm here adapted with an adaptive number of shots for quantum variational circuits.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm that approximates the gradient of a cost function using a random subset of data to find a local minimum.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm that approximates the gradient of a cost function using a random subset of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm that approximates the gradient of a cost function using a random subset of the training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm that approximates the gradient of a cost function using a single random sample or mini-batch.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm that approximates the gradient of a cost function using a subset of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm that approximates the gradient of a cost function using random samples.</rdfs:comment>
