    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of transfer learning that aims to apply a model learned from a source distribution to a different but related target distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of transfer learning that aims to apply a model learned from a source domain to a different but related target domain.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of transfer learning that aims to apply a model trained on one distribution to a different but related distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of transfer learning that aims to apply a model trained on one source distribution to a different but related target distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of transfer learning that aligns a labeled source distribution with an unlabeled target distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of transfer learning that aligns a labeled source domain with an unlabeled target domain to improve model generalization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of transfer learning that aligns a model trained on a source distribution to a different but related target distribution.</skos:definition>
