    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of transfer learning that focuses on adapting a model trained on one source domain to a different but related target domain.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of transfer learning that focuses on aligning two different but related data distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of transfer learning that optimizes a model to perform well on a target distribution using data from a source distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A task of classifying an unlabeled target dataset using a labeled source dataset from a related domain.</skos:definition>
