    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that adjusts a classifier trained on a source distribution to perform better on a target distribution with a different data distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that adjusts a model trained on a source distribution to perform effectively on a target distribution with different characteristics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that adjusts a model trained on a source domain to perform effectively on a target domain with different data distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that aligns a model trained on one data distribution to perform effectively on a different but related target distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that aligns data distributions between a source and target domain to improve model generalization.</skos:definition>
