    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that aligns the distributions of training and testing data to improve model performance on a target domain.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that allows a model trained on one data distribution to perform effectively on a different but related distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that allows a model trained on one domain to share knowledge and perform well on a different domain.</skos:definition>
