  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#intrinsic_motivation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Intrinsic Motivation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that drives an agent to explore its environment based on internal rewards rather than external goals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework that encourages an agent to seek novel experiences based on internal rewards like prediction error reduction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational mechanism that drives an agent to explore its environment based on internal curiosity or novelty.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning mechanism that drives an agent to explore and acquire a diverse repertoire of behaviors without external rewards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning mechanism that encourages an agent to explore its environment based on internal signals like surprise or learning progress.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning mechanism where an agent is driven by internal rewards, such as curiosity or novelty, to explore its environment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mechanism in agents that generates internal rewards to encourage exploration in environments with sparse extrinsic feedback.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mechanism in deep reinforcement learning that encourages exploration of the environment to overcome challenges like action abstraction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mechanism in reinforcement learning that enables an agent to generate its own goals for exploration in the absence of external rewards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mechanism in reinforcement learning that rewards an agent for exploring novel or uncertain states.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mechanism that generates internal rewards to drive a reinforcement learning agent to focus on objects and learn useful representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach where agents are driven by internal curiosity or satisfaction rather than external rewards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning mechanism that encourages agents to explore their environment based on internal rewards like novelty or curiosity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning mechanism that generates internal rewards to encourage exploration based on curiosity or prediction error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning mechanism that generates internal rewards to encourage the exploration of an environment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning mechanism that guides exploration by rewarding the agent for discovering novel states or predicting forward transitions in a representation space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning mechanism that uses reward bonuses derived from a dynamics model to encourage exploration.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning objective where an agent is driven by internal rewards, such as curiosity or uncertainty reduction, rather than external goals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An exploration bias in reinforcement learning that incentivizes agents to take actions based on internal rewards rather than external goals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An exploration strategy in reinforcement learning that rewards an agent based on its surprise or learning progress in complex domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[its own goals for exploration in the absence of external rewards] its own goals for exploration in the absence of external rewards</rdfs:comment>
