    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approximation technique that transforms a Bayesian posterior inference problem into a deterministic optimization problem.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approximation technique that transforms a complex posterior distribution estimation problem into an optimization problem.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approximation technique that transforms a posterior distribution estimation problem into a functional optimization problem.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approximation technique used to estimate complex probability distributions by optimizing a simpler surrogate.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approximation technique used to estimate computationally intractable posterior distributions in Bayesian networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization technique used to approximate the posterior distribution of latent variables in a stochastic process.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization-based approach to approximate the posterior distribution of a latent variable model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization-based method for approximating complex probability distributions by minimizing the variational free energy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization-based technique that approximates complex probability densities by minimizing the divergence between a proxy family and the target.</skos:definition>
