  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#attention_mechanism">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Attention Mechanism</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A cognitive-inspired component in deep learning that amplifies critical details to focus on the most essential aspects of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component designed to capture pairwise correlations between input elements, often optimized via dataflow fusion to reduce memory complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component in deep learning architectures that allows the model to to focus on specific parts of the input sequence when producing an output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A component in neural networks that allows a decoder to focus on specific parts of an input sequence.</rdfs:comment>
