  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#structured_prediction">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Structured Prediction</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach for predictors over structured label spaces that utilizes direct loss minimization and randomized predictors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that maps input data to structured output spaces such as trees or strings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning task that predicts complex output structures by exploiting the local part-based organization of the data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning task where the output is a complex object such as a tree or a graph rather than a scalar.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning task where the output is a complex object, such as a graph or a sequence, rather than a single scalar value.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that predicts complex output structures, used here to assign agents to tasks in multi-agent collaborative problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning framework for predicting complex output objects rather than single scalar values or class labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning framework that predicts complex output structures, such as the onset and offset of vowel durations, rather than scalar values.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm in natural language processing where the output is a structured object rather than a scalar value.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task focused on predicting complex output objects defined by factor graph decompositions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that aims to recover latent ground truth labels for structured instances with categorical random variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that involves predicting complex outputs with hard syntactic and semantic constraints, such as source code.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that involves the simultaneous prediction of multiple dependent labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that maps input sets to complex target permutations or sequences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that optimizes over complex labels by modeling the interactions between components of the label.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that predicts complex output objects rather than scalar values, often constrained by specific structural relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that predicts complex output objects where elements have internal dependencies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that predicts complex output objects where the components have a structured relationship.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that predicts complex output objects with internal dependencies rather than simple scalar values.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that predicts complex outputs such as trees or graphs rather than single scalar values.</rdfs:comment>
