  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#graph_kernel">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Graph Kernel</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A function that computes a similarity measure between two graph-structured data objects.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A function that measures the similarity between two graph structures to enable the use of kernel-based learning algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A function that measures the similarity between two graphs by mapping them into a high-dimensional feature space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A function that measures the similarity between two graphs to enable their use in standard machine learning classifiers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A function that measures the similarity between weighted directed graphs based on homological algebra and homology groups.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A function used to extract topological information from network structures to train predictive models for rumor veracity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A kernel function that defines a dot product between two graphs to capture spatio-temporal information in time series data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A similarity function based on subgraph matchings that allows for the classification of attributed graphs.</rdfs:comment>
