    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that segregates a mixed input signal into its constituent independent components.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that separates a mixture of independent signals into their original source components without prior knowledge of the mixing process.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that separates a mixture of signals into its constituent source components without prior knowledge of the mixing process.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that separates a mixture of signals into its original constituent sources without knowing the mixing process.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique used to decompose a mixture of signals into its constituent independent sources.</skos:definition>
