  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#weight_initialization">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Weight Initialization</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical method for setting the starting parameters of a neural network to ensure stable gradient flow.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of setting the starting values of neural network parameters to accelerate convergence and improve training stability.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A preparatory process for setting the initial parameters of a neural network to improve training convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A preprocessing step that sets the starting values of neural network parameters to facilitate training convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A procedure for setting the starting parameters of a neural network to ensure stable signal propagation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of setting the initial values of neural network parameters to improve training performance and convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of setting the initial values of neural network weights to avoid failure modes like exploding or vanishing mean activation length during early training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of setting the starting parameters of a neural network to ensure stable signal propagation during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of setting the starting values for neural network parameters to ensure convergence, particularly when using non-linear activation functions.</rdfs:comment>
