    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A branch of statistics and machine learning focused on determining the actual cause-effect relationship between variables in observational data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A field of artificial intelligence focused on learning causal models from data to understand cause-and-effect relationships.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework for deriving cause-effect relations between random variables from observational data using regression and dependence estimation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework for visual reasoning that uses do-calculus to calculate causal effects on pixel-level features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that uses causal models to estimate the effects of interventions on outcomes to improve system fairness.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that uses graphical knowledge of causal mechanisms to remove unstable relationships and improve model generalization across environments.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology used to determine whether a statistical dependence between variables is direct or mediated by an unobserved factor.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modeling framework used to estimate the effect of continuous treatments on survival outcomes while correcting for selection bias.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic reasoning process that extracts causal relationships from observed correlations using interventions and categorical interpretations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the actual effect of one variable on another by controlling for confounding factors.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the actual effect of one variable on another to identify cause-and-effect relationships.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the actual effect of one variable on another to understand the underlying reasons for observed events.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the direction of cause-and-effect relationships between variables in a discrete domain.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the independent effect of a specific change on an outcome by analyzing cause-and-effect relationships.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the independent effect of a specific variable on an outcome by controlling for confounding factors.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the independent effect of a specific variable on an outcome using observational or experimental data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the independent effect of a specific variable on another from observational data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the independent effect of a specific variable on another outcome.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the independent effect of a specific variable on another through counterfactual estimation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the independent effect of a specific variable on another.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of determining the structural relationships and directional dependencies between variables in a dynamical system.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of drawing a conclusion about a causal connection based on the conditions under which the effect occurs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of probabilistic inference in the presence of causal mechanisms to reason about causal graphs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A research field focused on determining the actual effect of a treatment or intervention by answering counterfactual questions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical approach that models and infers cause-and-effect relationships from data to solve complex artificial intelligence problems.</skos:definition>
