  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#online_mirror_descent">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Online Mirror Descent</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A first-order optimization algorithm that generalizes gradient descent by using a Bregman divergence to update parameters in a mirror space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fundamental algorithm for online convex optimization that can be improved through stabilization to handle dynamic learning rates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A general optimization strategy for online learning that uses a mirror map to update parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A general optimization technique for online learning that minimizes regret using a mirror map.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regret-minimization algorithm used in online convex optimization to iteratively update parameters based on a mirror map.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regret-minimization framework used to optimize policies in stochastic shortest path problems with adversarial costs and bandit feedback.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A scalable online learning algorithm that utilizes mirror maps to exploit the geometric structure of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A universal online convex optimization algorithm used to track and adapt to non-stationary environments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm used in online learning to minimize regret by updating parameters via a Bregman divergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm used in online learning to minimize regret by using a combination of regularizers adapted to atomic norms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm used in online learning to minimize regret relative to a sequence of loss functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm used to find an equilibrium in games through sequential updates based on sampled trajectories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization method used in online learning to minimize regret by updating parameters via a mirror map.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An online convex optimization algorithm used to construct non-anticipating estimators for sequential change-point detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An online optimization algorithm that uses a mirror map to balance exploration and exploitation when combining multiple bandit algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An online optimization algorithm used to update dual multipliers in resource-constrained allocation problems to maximize cumulative rewards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm for online learning that updates parameters by minimizing a distance to a mirror space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that minimizes regret by updating parameters based on a mirror map in a dual space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that updates model parameters sequentially to minimize regret over a time horizon.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm used to learn expert weights in an online adversarial setting to minimize expected regret.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization framework for online learning that updates weights using a Bregman divergence to minimize tracking regret.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization framework used for online portfolio management to achieve logarithmic regret through a novel regularizer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization framework used for sequential decision making in unbounded domains to minimize dynamic regret.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a mirror map, mirror maps] mirror map</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[optimize policies in stochastic shortest path problems with adversarial costs and bandit feedback] optimize policies in stochastic shortest path problems with adversarial costs and bandit feedback</rdfs:comment>
