    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of high-level goals and low-level primitive actions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks or abstractions to improve learning efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks or options.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks to improve learning efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks to improve scalability and efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks to manage abrupt dynamics and minimize surprise.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks to simplify the learning process.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks with different temporal resolutions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of subtasks and controllers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a set of diverse skills and a high-level policy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that decomposes complex tasks into a hierarchy of sub-goals to manage long-horizon reasoning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework where a global policy is assembled from individual policies that maximize separate reward components.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A strategy that decomposes a complex task into a set of smaller, sequentially dependent subtasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks to simplify the learning process.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An agent-based learning framework that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to learning complex tasks by decomposing them into a hierarchy of sub-policies.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to reinforcement learning that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks and policies.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to reinforcement learning that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of subgoals and policies.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to reinforcement learning where a meta controller manages the execution of acquired skills to solve complex sequences of instructions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to training agents that decomposes complex tasks into a hierarchy to achieve human-like skill levels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An architecture that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-tasks at different temporal and conceptual scales.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An architecture that learns and represents self-generated skills in an end-to-end way to improve exploration and transfer learning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An extension of reinforcement learning that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of simpler sub-tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An extension of reinforcement learning that decomposes a complex task into a hierarchy of sub-goals or options.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#reinforcement_learning_algorithm"/>
