  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#canonical_correlation_analysis">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Canonical Correlation Analysis</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that finds linear combinations of two sets of variables that are maximally correlated.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that finds linear relationships between two or more sets of variables by maximizing their correlation in a common space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that finds linear relationships between two sets of variables, here extended to a latent variable model for matrix-variate data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A feature extraction method that finds maximally correlated linear projections of two different views of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fusion operation used to combine deep feature representations from multiple MRI modalities into discriminative features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear method that finds the projections of two sets of variables that maximize the correlation between them.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multi-view data analysis technique used to find linear or nonlinear dependencies between different sets of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multivariate statistical method that finds linear combinations of two sets of variables that have maximum correlation with each other.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multivariate statistical method that finds linear combinations of two sets of variables to maximize their correlation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multivariate statistical method that finds linear relationships between two or more sets of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multivariate statistical method that finds projections maximizing the correlations between two sets of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multivariate statistical method that identifies hidden associations between two sets of variables from different modalities.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multivariate statistical method used to find linear combinations of two or more datasets that maximize their correlation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multivariate statistical method used to find the linear relationship between two sets of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multivariate statistical method used to find the linear relationships between two sets of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multivariate statistical method used to identify and quantify the linear relationships between two sets of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multivariate statistical method used to identify linear relationships between two sets of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multiview analysis method that finds linear correlations between two or more sets of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical approach used to identify the maximum correlation between two sets of multi-dimensional variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that extracts low-dimensional features capturing the commonalities between two high-dimensional data sets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that finds linear combinations of two or more sets of variables that have maximum correlation with each other.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that finds linear combinations of two sets of variables that have maximum correlation with each other.</rdfs:comment>
