  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#graph_convolutional_network">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Graph Convolutional Network</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of neural networks operating on graphs that can be used as sentence encoders to produce latent feature representations of words.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture designed to efficiently learn from graph data structures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture designed to operate directly on graph-structured data by aggregating information from neighboring nodes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture designed to operate directly on graphs by aggregating information from neighboring nodes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture designed to process data represented as graphs by aggregating information from neighboring nodes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture designed to process graph-structured data by recursively aggregating representations from neighboring nodes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture extended to graph-based representations to handle the specific geometry of omnidirectional images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutional operations over graph-structured data to learn node and edge representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutional operations to data structured as graphs to capture spatial and spectral features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutional operations to graph-structured data to extract structure-aware features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that extracts knowledge from high-order neighbors of nodes in a graph using a recursive optimization process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that extracts structural features from graphical inputs to predict the growth of information cascades.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that integrates vertex features and graph topology through convolutional layers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that models topological and temporal dependencies in dynamic networks for opinion inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that operates on graph structures to jointly exploit syntactic and temporal information for document dating.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture used to build efficient graph representations for solving combinatorial optimization problems like the Travelling Salesman Problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model designed to operate directly on graph-structured data by aggregating neighborhood features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that applies convolutional operators to node features on a graph to capture spatial dependencies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that operates directly on graph-structured data to learn node or shape embeddings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that operates on graph-structured data to detect hardware trojans in integrated circuit netlists.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning paradigm applied to classify entities based on their evolving behavioral graph structures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model that combines topological features and information propagation for node classification in graphs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed for graph-based tasks that can suffer from over-smoothing when layers are stacked.</rdfs:comment>
