    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep generative model that produces synthetic data conditioned on specific input parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning model used to train associations between images of objects and their partially occluded counterparts for reconstruction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework consisting of a generator and a discriminator that produces synthetic data conditioned on specific input information.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework consisting of two competing networks that generates synthetic data based on specific class labels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework consisting of two neural networks that compete to generate realistic data conditioned on specific auxiliary information.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework consisting of two neural networks that generate synthetic data conditioned on specific input labels or images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework for generating synthetic data conditioned on specific labels or auxiliary information.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework for image synthesis that uses auxiliary information to guide the generation process toward specific labels or masks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that creates dense 3D point clouds by learning to mimic a data distribution in an unsupervised manner.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that generates high-resolution data conditioned on low-resolution inputs via a competition between a generator and a discriminator.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that generates masks conditioned on input images for the purpose of automatic polyp segmentation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that generates realistic static images by inpainting occluded backgrounds based on a binary mask.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that generates synthetic data based on specific auxiliary information to control the output's characteristics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that generates synthetic data conditioned on specific input labels or images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that generates synthetic data conditioned on specific labels or auxiliary information using a generator and a discriminator.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that generates synthetic data samples conditioned on specific labels or proportions to expand a dataset.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that generates synthetic images based on specific input guidance and target constraints.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that uses a generator and a discriminator to produce realistic image captions conditioned on visual input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative framework that incorporates auxiliary information to direct the data generation process.</skos:definition>
