  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#oversampling_protocol">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Oversampling Protocol</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique that adds synthetic samples to the minority class to address dataset imbalance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique that generates artificial samples to balance class distributions in supervised learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique that generates synthetic minority class samples to address class imbalance in classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique that generates synthetic samples for the minority class in imbalanced datasets to improve classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique that increases the representation of a minority class to mitigate imbalance in a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique that increases the representation of minority classes to address imbalanced datasets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique that increases the representation of the minority class in an imbalanced dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique that increases the representation of underrepresented groups to mitigate algorithmic bias and class imbalance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique used to address class imbalance by increasing the number of samples in the minority class.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique used to balance datasets by increasing the number of instances in the minority class.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique used to balance datasets by increasing the number of samples in the minority class.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data preprocessing method that increases the number of instances in a minority class to handle imbalanced datasets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data preprocessing technique that balances an imbalanced dataset by increasing the number of samples in the minority class.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data preprocessing technique that increases the number of instances in a minority class to combat class imbalance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data preprocessing technique that increases the number of minority class instances to handle class imbalance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data sampling technique that increases the number of instances from a minority class to mitigate class imbalance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data-level technique that increases the number of instances in a minority class to address class imbalance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[address class imbalance by increasing the number of samples in the minority class, balance datasets by increasing the number of instances in the minority class, balance datasets by increasing the number of samples in the minority class] balance datasets by increasing the number of samples in the minority class</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[synthetic samples] synthetic samples</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[representation of minority class] representation of minority class</rdfs:comment>
