    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A Bayesian sequential decision-making algorithm that maintains a posterior distribution over a model to guide exploration.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A Bayesian sequential decision-making algorithm used to balance exploration and exploitation in multi-armed bandit problems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A Bayesian strategy for the exploration-exploitation trade-off that selects actions according to the probability that they are optimal.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A bayesian approach to the multi-armed bandit problem that selects actions based on the probability of being optimal.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A heuristic search algorithm used for arm selection in multivariate multi-armed bandit problems to combat the curse of dimensionality.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A multi-armed bandit algorithm used to find the optimal dosage in clinical trials by accommodating monotonicity assumptions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A posterior sampling algorithm used to minimize regret in Markov Decision Processes with unknown diameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic algorithm for the multi-armed bandit problem that balances exploration and exploitation by sampling from the posterior distribution of rewards.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic algorithm that balances exploration and exploitation by sampling from a posterior distribution of model parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic algorithm that balances exploration and exploitation by sampling from a posterior distribution of reward estimates.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic algorithm that balances exploration and exploitation by sampling from a posterior distribution of rewards.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic algorithm that balances exploration and exploitation by sampling from a posterior distribution to select the best action.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic algorithm that balances exploration and exploitation to optimize decision-making in uncertain environments.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic algorithm used for decision-making in multi-armed bandit problems to balance exploration and exploitation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic algorithm used in multi-armed bandit problems to balance exploration and exploitation of actions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic strategy for decision-making that balances exploration and exploitation by sampling from a posterior distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic strategy for the multi-armed bandit problem that balances exploration and exploitation by sampling from a posterior distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probability-based strategy that balances exploration and exploitation in multi-armed bandit problems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A randomized algorithm for the multi-armed bandit problem that samples from a posterior distribution to balance exploration and exploitation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A randomized algorithm for the stochastic linear bandit setting that selects arms based on sampling from a posterior distribution of parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequential decision making algorithm that utilizes posterior uncertainty to balance exploration and exploitation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithm for the multi-armed bandit problem that balances exploration and exploitation by sampling from a posterior distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithm for the multi-armed bandit problem that chooses actions according to a probability distribution based on the posterior estimate of the reward.</skos:definition>
