  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#correlation_clustering">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Correlation Clustering</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering method that aims to minimize the number of disagreeing edges in a graph where edges are labeled as similar or dissimilar.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering method that minimizes disagreements between positive and negative edge labels in a complete graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering method that partitions data based on the similarity and dissimilarity of pairs of elements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering method that partitions objects based on pairwise similarity and dissimilarity measures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering method that partitions objects into groups by maximizing the consistency of edge weights in a graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering methodology that partitions data into groups by optimizing objectives based on the agreement between pair-wise or higher-order relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering objective that minimizes the number of disagreements between edge labels and cluster assignments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data aggregation technique that groups objects based on qualitative similarity or dissimilarity labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A graph clustering formulation that partitions nodes based on similarity and dissimilarity measures without requiring a prior cluster count.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A graph clustering task that aims to minimize the total number of disagreements between edge labels and cluster assignments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A graph partitioning method that groups nodes based on positive and negative edge weights.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A graph partitioning method used to segment individual cells from calcium imaging videos.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A graph partitioning problem that aims to group nodes by minimizing the number of edges that disagree with the cluster assignments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A graph partitioning task that aims to group vertices into clusters to minimize the number of disagreements between edge labels and cluster assignments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A graph partitioning task that seeks to group vertices based on similarity and dissimilarity edge labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A graph-based clustering method that aims to minimize the number of edges that disagree with the cluster assignments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping method that partitions nodes in a graph based on positive and negative similarities without specifying the number of clusters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping method that partitions nodes to maximize the number of agreements and minimize disagreements between paired items.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm that groups data based on a set of pairwise similarity and dissimilarity scores.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning problem that groups individuals based on their pairwise similarities under specific constraints.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning task that aims to group objects by maximizing agreements and minimizing disagreements with given pairwise labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An agnostic learning method used for community detection where the number of clusters is not predefined.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization problem that partitions a graph into cliques by minimizing the number of edge modifications.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups items based on positive and negative similarity constraints.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning task that groups data points based on their similarity or dissimilarity labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning task that partitions a signed graph to minimize the number of disagreements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning task that partitions nodes into clusters to maximize agreements and minimize disagreements with given edge labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning task that partitions nodes into clusters to minimize the disagreement with specified co-clustering preferences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning task that partitions objects into clusters to minimize disagreements between the clustering and provided similarity scores.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning technique that partitions nodes of a graph into clusters to minimize the number of disagreements between edge labels and cluster assignments.</rdfs:comment>
