    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A grouping method that partitions nodes to maximize the number of agreements and minimize disagreements between paired items.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm that groups data based on a set of pairwise similarity and dissimilarity scores.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A partitioning problem that groups individuals based on their pairwise similarities under specific constraints.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A partitioning task that aims to group objects by maximizing agreements and minimizing disagreements with given pairwise labels.</skos:definition>
