  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#surrogate_model">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Surrogate Model</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation of a complex function used to reduce the cost of solving optimization problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation of a complex or expensive simulation used to reduce evaluation time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation of a complex physical model used to reduce the cost of numerical simulations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation of a complex system or stochastic process used to reduce evaluation costs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation of a complex system used to reduce the cost of evaluating a high-fidelity model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation that emulates a complex objective function to facilitate the search for optimal input combinations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation that mimics the behavior of a complex program or simulation to reduce evaluation time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation that predicts the response of a complex system to optimize hyperparameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation that provides quick and accurate predictions of complex physical processes like thrust forces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation that replaces a complex or computationally expensive process to accelerate inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation that replaces a complex simulation to predict outcomes more efficiently.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation that replaces a complex system to solve high-dimensional uncertainty quantification problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation that replaces a computationally expensive black-box function to improve optimization efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation that replaces expensive simulations with a fast-executing function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation used to evaluate the validity of machine learning pipelines without requiring full execution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation used to optimize hyperparameters of deep learning models more efficiently than direct evaluation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational approximation used to replace a complex or expensive simulation to enable efficient uncertainty quantification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computationally cheap approximation of a complex numerical simulator used for uncertainty quantification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computationally cheap approximation of a complex, expensive-to-evaluate simulation or function used to accelerate analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computationally cheap approximation of an expensive black-box objective function used to find approximate solutions to optimization problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computationally efficient approximation of a black-box decision model used to generate adversarial examples in security contexts.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computationally efficient approximation of a complex high-fidelity simulation used for reliability analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computationally efficient approximation of a complex model used for uncertainty quantification and high-dimensional problems.</rdfs:comment>
