  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#sparse_bayesian_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sparse Bayesian Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic approach for sparse signal recovery that estimates a vector from an underdetermined system of linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic approach to neural network optimization that encourages many weights or units to become zero to reduce complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic approach to signal recovery that uses parameterized priors to encourage sparsity in the solution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework for estimating compressible vectors by assuming a sparse prior distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework for estimating sparse signals by employing evidence maximization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework for recovering signals by promoting sparsity in the representation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework for recovering sparse signals from measurement vectors by estimating signal covariance matrices.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework for signal recovery that encourages sparsity in the weight distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework for sparse coding that estimates the posterior distribution of weights to identify the most relevant features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that employs Bayesian inference to recover signals with a limited number of non-zero coefficients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that enforces sparsity in model parameters to balance complexity and fitting error during system discovery.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that imposes sparsity on model parameters using heavy-tailed prior distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that induces sparsity in model coefficients through the use of specific prior distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that induces sparsity in the weight vector by assigning hierarchical priors to the parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that infers the structure and dynamics of networks by promoting sparsity in the model parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that recovers high-dimensional sparse signals from corrupted measurements using hierarchical priors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that uses sparsity-inducing priors to find a concise model with high generalization performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework used for signal recovery that promotes sparsity in the estimated parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework used for source localization that enforces sparsity constraints on electrical current dipoles.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework used to achieve sparsity in models by estimating hyperparameters of the prior distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic method that employs hierarchical priors to recover signals with unknown cluster patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic regression framework that promotes parsimony and sparsity to discover governing differential equations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic supervised learning approach that uses a hierarchical model structure to penalize unnecessary complexity and achieve sparsity in model parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic technique used to obtain sparse series representations by retaining only the most significant basis terms through variational inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning algorithm that selects a subset of relevant samples and features to make probabilistic predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[heavy-tailed prior distributions] heavy-tailed prior distributions</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[sparsity-inducing priors, achieve sparsity in models by estimating hyperparameters of the prior distributions] sparsity-inducing priors</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[signal recovery that promotes sparsity in the estimated parameters] signal recovery that promotes sparsity in the estimated parameters</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[source localization that enforces sparsity constraints on electrical current dipoles] source localization that enforces sparsity constraints on electrical current dipoles</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a hierarchical model structure] hierarchical structure</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[obtain sparse series representations by retaining only the most significant basis terms through variational inference] obtain sparse series representations by retaining only the most significant basis terms through variational inference</rdfs:comment>
