    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework for sparse coding that estimates the posterior distribution of weights to identify the most relevant features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that employs Bayesian inference to recover signals with a limited number of non-zero coefficients.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that enforces sparsity in model parameters to balance complexity and fitting error during system discovery.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that imposes sparsity on model parameters using heavy-tailed prior distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that induces sparsity in model coefficients through the use of specific prior distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that induces sparsity in the weight vector by assigning hierarchical priors to the parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that infers the structure and dynamics of networks by promoting sparsity in the model parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that recovers high-dimensional sparse signals from corrupted measurements using hierarchical priors.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that uses sparsity-inducing priors to find a concise model with high generalization performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework used for signal recovery that promotes sparsity in the estimated parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework used for source localization that enforces sparsity constraints on electrical current dipoles.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework used to achieve sparsity in models by estimating hyperparameters of the prior distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic method that employs hierarchical priors to recover signals with unknown cluster patterns.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic regression framework that promotes parsimony and sparsity to discover governing differential equations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic supervised learning approach that uses a hierarchical model structure to penalize unnecessary complexity and achieve sparsity in model parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic technique used to obtain sparse series representations by retaining only the most significant basis terms through variational inference.</skos:definition>
