  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#energy_based_model">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Energy-Based Model</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of models that supports a dynamically growing number of tasks to minimize interference in continual learning scenarios.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of probabilistic models that associate a scalar energy value with each configuration of variables to facilitate model-based planning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of probabilistic models that represent the statistical structure of the environment through an energy function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A descriptive model that captures mutual patterns from structural input signals to synthesize visual realism using an energy function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible, unnormalized density model used to represent probability distributions for tasks such as out-of-distribution detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that associates a scalar energy value with each configuration of variables to represent the probability distribution of the data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that describes a probability distribution by associating a scalar energy value with each configuration of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that describes the probability distribution of a dataset using a scalar energy function to differentiate normal from anomalous states.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that describes the probability of a configuration using an energy function that assigns low values to likely states.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that describes the probability of a state by associating a scalar energy value with each configuration of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that models the probability of a configuration by associating it with a scalar energy value.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that represents a probability distribution by associating a scalar energy value with each configuration of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that represents concepts as separate energy functions to discover both global and local factors of variation in images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that represents probability distributions as energy functions to enable the compositional generation of concepts.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that represents the probability distribution of data using an unnormalized energy function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework where variables are optimized to minimize a global energy function to approximate gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that associates a scalar energy value with each configuration of variables to represent a probability distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that captures data distributions by associating a scalar energy value with every configuration of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that defines a probability distribution via an energy function to perform density estimation and sample generation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that describes a probability distribution by associating a scalar energy value with each configuration of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that describes a probability distribution using a scalar energy function to assign compatibility between variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that describes probability distributions using unnormalized scalar energy functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that describes the probability of a configuration via a scalar energy function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that describes the probability of a state using a scalar energy function where lower energy corresponds to higher probability.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that learns a scalar energy function to describe the compatibility of input variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that learns a scalar energy function to describe the compatibility of variables in a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that models the probability distribution of data using a scalar energy function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that uses a trainable energy function to define a probability distribution via a Gibbs measure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that associates a scalar energy value with each configuration of variables to represent a probability distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that defines a probability distribution via an energy function, often trained using Markov chain Monte Carlo sampling.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that describes a probability distribution by associating a scalar energy value with each configuration of variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that describes a probability distribution by associating a scalar energy value with each configuration.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative model that describes the probability distribution of data using an energy function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-normalized probabilistic model that describes data distribution using an energy function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that assigns a scalar energy value to configurations to predict protein side chain conformations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that associates a scalar energy value with each configuration of variables to represent the compatibility between them.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that defines a cost function in a latent space to capture multimodal trajectory distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework that defines a distribution by assigning an energy value to each configuration of variables.</rdfs:comment>
