  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#regularization">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Regularization</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fundamental technique that prevents over-fitting and improves generalization by constraining a model's complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of adding constraints to a model's learning process to reduce bias and prevent overfitting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method that adds a penalty term to the loss function to prevent overfitting and improve generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used in deep learning to prevent overfitting by adding constraints to the model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used in machine learning to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the loss function or modifying the training process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to prevent overfitting in large neural networks to improve their generalization performance on complex tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique applied to neural networks to improve robustness by maximizing linear regions and distance to the decision boundary.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for improving model generalization by altering the loss landscape, specifically analyzed here regarding the timing of its application during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds a penalty term to a loss function to prevent overfitting and ensure convergence to an optimal solution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds a penalty term to a loss function to prevent overfitting by constraining model parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds a penalty term to an objective function to prevent overfitting and embed prior knowledge about stability or smoothness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds a penalty term to an objective function to prevent overfitting and encourage sparsity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds a penalty term to the loss function to constrain model weights or feature importance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds a penalty term to the loss function to prevent model overfitting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds a penalty term to the loss function to prevent overfitting and improve generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds a penalty term to the loss function to prevent overfitting and promote sparsity in high-dimensional models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds a penalty term to the loss function to prevent overfitting by constraining the model's complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds constraints to a model to improve its adversarial robustness and prevent overfitting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds constraints to a model to prevent overfitting and improve robustness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that adds constraints to a model to prevent overfitting and increase robustness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that introduces additional constraints or penalties to a model to prevent overfitting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used during neural network training to prevent overfitting, explored here through parallel-regularized non-batch SGD.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in deep networks to ensure both zero training error and good generalization error in regression problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in machine learning to discourage complexity in a model to prevent overfitting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in machine learning to prevent overfitting by adding constraints or penalties to the model's complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in optimization to discourage overfitting by adding a penalty term to the loss function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to constrain model complexity or hidden states to improve robustness against corrupted labels in classification tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to constrain the learned state-to-action mappings of neural network controllers to ensure action smoothness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to induce numerical stability in learned functions to defend against adversarial attacks in regression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent over-fitting by modifying input variables or adding constraints to a model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty or constraint to the learning process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term or introducing randomness into the training process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term or modifying the model parameters during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the learning procedure to improve generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the loss function of a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the loss function or modifying the training process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the loss function to constrain model complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the loss function to discourage model complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the loss function to reduce model complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the loss function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the model's loss function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the model's objective function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the objective function or constraining the model update direction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding a penalty term to the objective function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding constraints or penalties to a model's learning process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding constraints or penalties to the learning process of a neural network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting by adding constraints or penalties to the learning process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting in machine learning algorithms by penalizing large parameter values.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to prevent overfitting or inject constraints by adding a penalty term to the loss function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to stabilize learned reconstruction algorithms and prevent instabilities caused by adversarial noise.</rdfs:comment>
