    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach where the agent learns a value function or policy from data generated by a different policy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach where the agent learns about a target policy using data generated by a different behavior policy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach where the agent learns from data generated by a policy different from the one being optimized.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning method that evaluates or improves a policy using data generated by a different policy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning strategy that evaluates or improves a policy different from the one used to generate data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning strategy that optimizes a target policy using data generated by a different behavior policy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning strategy where the agent learns a value function from data generated by a policy different from the one being optimized.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning technique that estimates the value of a target policy using data generated by a different behavior policy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning technique that learns a target policy using experience generated by a different behavior policy.</skos:definition>
