  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#online_optimization">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Online Optimization</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for making a sequence of decisions in real-time where the cost functions are revealed sequentially.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for making a sequence of decisions in real-time where the objective function is revealed incrementally.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for making a sequence of decisions where the objective function is revealed incrementally over time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where data arrives sequentially and the model is updated incrementally to minimize regret.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for making a sequence of decisions in real-time where the cost of each decision is revealed only after it is made.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for making a sequence of decisions in real-time where the objective function is revealed incrementally.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for making a sequence of decisions in real-time without full knowledge of future data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for making a sequence of decisions over time where the objective function is revealed only after each action is taken.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for making sequential decisions in real-time where future utility functions are unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that iteratively optimizes a function in a sequential setting where the objective changes over time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robust approach to mathematical optimization that learns and adapts as new data is observed over time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential decision process where a learner minimizes a loss function over time without full knowledge of future data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential decision process where an algorithm updates its parameters iteratively as data arrives in a stream.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential decision-making process that uses primal-dual algorithms to minimize dynamic cumulative regret under non-additive penalties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential decision-making process where a controller learns to maximize time average reward in a renewal-reward system with unknown distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential decision-making process where a goal is to minimize costs over time without full knowledge of future inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential decision-making process where a learner minimizes costs over time in an environment with memory constraints.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A task of making real-time decisions to minimize cost or maximize profit using rules mined from historical data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[rules mined from historical data] rules mined from historical data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a sequence of decisions] sequence of decisions</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the model] model</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a function] function</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[loss function/costs] loss function/costs</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[time average reward] time average reward</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework for making a sequence of decisions in real-time where the cost functions are revealed sequentially.</skos:definition>
