  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#probabilistic_programming">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Probabilistic Programming</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational paradigm that uses probabilistic models to perform inference and quantify uncertainty in data analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational paradigm that uses random variables and probability distributions to explore the behavior of classifiers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A paradigm for learning the parameters of a probabilistic model using backpropagation to combine domain knowledge with data-driven learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A paradigm that allows for the automated design and implementation of Bayesian inference-based algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A paradigm that combines probabilistic modeling with a programming language to perform inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows for the definition of probabilistic models and the approximation of their posterior distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows for the definition of probabilistic models and the execution of Bayesian inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows for the definition of probabilistic models and the use of general-purpose inference machinery.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows for the definition of probabilistic models by treating random variables as first-class citizens.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows for the definition of probabilistic models to perform inference and prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows the definition of generative models through code to be used for statistical inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows the definition of probabilistic models and the execution of inference engines over them.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows users to define probabilistic models and perform inference on them using data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows users to define probabilistic models and perform inference on them using general-purpose languages.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows users to define probabilistic models and perform inference using a specialized domain-specific language.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows users to define probabilistic models and perform inference using specialized languages and algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows users to define probabilistic models and perform inference using specialized languages.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that allows users to define probabilistic models in a high-level language to perform Bayesian inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A programming paradigm that separates the definition of a probabilistic model from the inference algorithm used to analyze it.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[random variables and probability distributions] random variables and probability distributions</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[statistical inference] inference</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[data] data</rdfs:comment>
