    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning technique that uses a model to generate pseudo-labels for unlabeled data to iteratively improve its own performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning technique that uses a model's own predictions to create pseudolabels for unlabeled data to improve the model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning technique that uses the model's own high-confidence predictions as labels for unlabeled data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning technique where a model generates pseudo-labels for unlabeled data to iteratively improve its own performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning technique where a model is iteratively tuned using its own predicted labels as ground truth.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning technique where a model is trained on its own high-confidence predictions for unlabeled data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning technique where a model is used to generate pseudo-labels for unlabeled data, which are then used for further training.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An iterative learning process that uses a model to generate pseudo-labels for unlabeled data to expand the training set.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An iterative learning process where a model uses its own high-confidence predictions as labels for unlabeled data.</skos:definition>
