  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#class_incremental_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Class-Incremental Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A continual learning paradigm that aims to learn new classes while preserving knowledge of previously learned ones.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning methodology that allows a model to acquire new categories of data sequentially without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to learn new classes over time without forgetting previously acquired knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that enables a model to acquire new categories of data sequentially without forgetting previously learned knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that prevents catastrophic forgetting when adapting a model to new classes without original training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model is trained on new classes sequentially without forgetting previously learned categories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model is trained on new classes sequentially without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model is trained to recognize new classes sequentially without forgetting previously learned ones.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model is updated to recognize new classes progressively without forgetting previously learned knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model learns a sequence of new classes without forgetting previously learned categories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model learns new categories over time without forgetting previously acquired knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model learns to recognize new classes over time without forgetting previously learned ones.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a network sequentially learns new classes without forgetting previously acquired knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent acquires new categories over time while preventing the loss of previously learned knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning setting where a model is trained on new categories sequentially without forgetting previously learned classes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning setting where a model is trained on new categories sequentially without forgetting previously learned ones.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning setting where a model is updated to recognize new classes over time without forgetting previously learned ones.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning setting where a model is updated to recognize novel classes while retaining knowledge of previously learned base classes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning setting where a model learns new classes over time without forgetting previously acquired knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning strategy that allows a classifier to adapt to newly discovered classes without forgetting previous knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A lifelong learning paradigm where a model learns new classes over time without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A lifelong learning scheme that uses distillation loss and unlabeled data to prevent catastrophic forgetting when learning new classes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that trains a model to recognize new classes sequentially without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm where a model learns new classes over time without forgetting previously learned ones.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A progressive learning algorithm that learns new labels while retaining knowledge of previously learned labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A training strategy that allows a system to learn new concepts progressively from a data stream without forgetting previous classes.</rdfs:comment>
