    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that integrates domain-specific knowledge by enforcing constraints over the output space instead of relying solely on large labeled datasets.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses domain-expert constraints as noisy labels to train a model without ground-truth data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses imprecise or noisy labels to guide the model's learning process.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses noisy or imprecise label sources to construct pseudolabels for training models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses noisy or imprecise labeling functions to train models when fully labeled data is scarce.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses noisy or imprecise labeling functions to train models when high-quality ground truth is scarce.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses noisy or imprecise labels from multiple sources to train a model without requiring extensive ground truth data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses noisy or imprecise labels generated by a heuristic or model to train a deep learning system.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses noisy or imprecise labels to train a model when high-quality labeled data is scarce.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses noisy or imprecise labels to train models when high-quality annotations are expensive.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses noisy or imprecise sources to programmatically generate labels for unlabeled data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses programmatic labeling functions to generate training data instead of relying on hand-labeled ground truth.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that utilizes imperfect or noisy signals to guide policy learning in reinforcement learning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that utilizes noisy labeling functions to generate training data for a model.</skos:definition>
