    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A continual learning strategy that stores and re-trains on past samples to prevent catastrophic forgetting.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A continual learning strategy where a subset of past data is stored and replayed alongside new data to mitigate catastrophic forgetting.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A continual learning technique that stores and reviews previous experiences to balance stability and plasticity.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A continual learning technique that stores past experiences in a buffer to be re-sampled during training to prevent catastrophic forgetting.</skos:definition>
