    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Gated Recurrent Unit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating architecture for recurrent neural networks designed to capture long-term dependencies in sequential data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism for recurrent neural networks designed to handle temporal dependencies in time series data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks designed to capture long-term dependencies while mitigating the vanishing gradient problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks designed to capture long-term temporal dependencies while mitigating the vanishing gradient problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks designed to capture temporal dependencies in sequential data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks designed to handle the vanishing gradient problem in long-term sequential data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks designed to handle the vanishing gradient problem in sequence modeling.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks designed to handle the vanishing gradient problem in sequential data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks designed to manage memory and mitigate the vanishing gradient problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks designed to model temporal dependencies while mitigating vanishing gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks designed to predict closure terms in large eddy simulations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks designed to solve the vanishing gradient problem and capture long-term dependencies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks that allows for the efficient modeling of long-term dependencies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks that captures long-term dependencies in sequential data without a separate cell state.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks that helps capture long-term dependencies in sequential data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks that helps mitigate the vanishing gradient problem to capture long-term dependencies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks that helps the model capture long-term dependencies in sequential data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks that helps to mitigate the vanishing gradient problem and capture long-term dependencies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks that helps to mitigate the vanishing gradient problem while processing sequential data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gating mechanism in recurrent neural networks that learns to predict sequence values and select optimal sequential configurations for load forecasting.</rdfs:comment>
