    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An orthogonal linear transformation that transforms data into a new coordinate system such that the greatest variance comes to lie on the first coordinate.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An orthogonal linear transformation that transforms data into a new coordinate system such that the greatest variance lies on the first coordinate.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised dimensionality reduction technique that transforms data into a set of orthogonal components.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that identifies covariance correlations among features to discover meaningful modes in data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning technique used to approximate the gradient of an objective function for faster optimization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised linear dimension-reduction method that identifies the axes of maximal variance in a dataset.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised linear dimensionality reduction technique that transforms data into a new coordinate system to maximize variance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised linear transformation technique used for dimensionality reduction while preserving maximum variance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised linear transformation that reduces dimensionality by identifying the directions of maximum variance.</skos:definition>
