    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that enables an agent to adapt quickly to new tasks by leveraging experience from a distribution of previous tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that enables an agent to learn how to learn by adapting to new tasks based on experience from previous ones.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent is trained on a variety of tasks to acquire a prior that enables rapid adaptation to new, unseen tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent learns how to learn by optimizing its ability to adapt to new tasks based on experience from previous tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning procedure that enables an agent to adapt quickly to a distribution of tasks using a small number of examples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning process where an agent is trained across multiple tasks to learn how to learn new tasks more efficiently.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning scheme that shifts the objective from solving a specific task to learning how to learn to solve a set of tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that learns how to learn a reinforcement learning task across multiple environments.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that learns how to learn by acquiring meta-policies across a wide distribution of tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that leverages a meta-prior policy to quickly adapt to new tasks in non-stationary environments.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A paradigm that trains an agent to adapt quickly to new tasks by leveraging experience from previous learning episodes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach that enables agents to adapt quickly to new tasks by learning how to learn from a few samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach where an agent is trained across multiple tasks to develop the ability to perform causal reasoning in novel situations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A system that uses dynamic synapses to learn efficient control rules and adapt to new environments through self-reflexive modification.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithm that enables agents to quickly acquire new behaviors by leveraging prior experience from a set of related tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic approach that learns how to learn new tasks rapidly by leveraging experience from previous environments.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic framework that enables agents to rapidly adapt to new tasks based on prior experiences.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic framework that enables an agent to adapt to new tasks rapidly using a small amount of experience.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic framework that learns how to learn relationships across tasks to perform causal discovery in high-dimensional environments.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach that leverages prior experience across a distribution of tasks to enable a robot to acquire new skills more rapidly.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach that trains a reinforcement learning agent on a variety of tasks to allow rapid adaptation to new environments.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to reinforcement learning that enables an agent to quickly adapt to new tasks or environments based on prior experience.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to reinforcement learning that learns a general learning strategy to adapt quickly to new tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach where an agent learns from a variety of tasks to rapidly adapt its policy to new, unseen environments.</skos:definition>
