  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#sparse_gaussian_process">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sparse Gaussian Process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian non-parametric model that uses a small set of inducing points to approximate the posterior distribution of a full dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-parametric Bayesian learning component that learns environmental models online using a subset of the most informative data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-parametric Bayesian model that approximates a full Gaussian process using a small set of inducing points to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-parametric Bayesian model used to estimate baseline trends in personalized treatment-response trajectories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-parametric Bayesian regression method that reduces computational complexity by using a small set of inducing points.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-parametric Bayesian regression method that uses a small set of inducing points to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-parametric regression method that uses inducing points to reduce the cubic time complexity of standard Gaussian Processes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A nonparametric function approximator that uses a reduced set of inducing points or eigenfunctions to lower computational cost.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework combined with deep neural networks to provide reliable and fast uncertainty estimates for predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model that approximates a Gaussian process using a small set of inducing points to reduce computational complexity for time-series analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model that uses a small set of inducing points to approximate a full Gaussian process for large datasets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A scalable approximation of a gaussian process that uses a small set of inducing points called knots to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An approximation method for Bayesian nonparametric modeling that uses a small set of inducing inputs to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a subset of the most informative data] subset of the most informative data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[estimate baseline trends in personalized treatment-response trajectories] estimate baseline trends in personalized treatment-response trajectories</rdfs:comment>
