    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning methodology that produces valid prediction regions under mild conditions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that generates prediction regions with a user-specified confidence level based on past data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A non-parametric method for constructing confidence regions around predictions with guaranteed coverage rates.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A post-hoc procedure that constructs valid prediction intervals with guaranteed coverage probabilities for regression tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A predictive framework that generates statistically valid intervals or sets for model outputs to quantify uncertainty.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical framework that produces prediction sets with a user-specified confidence level rather than single point estimates.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical framework that provides guaranteed prediction intervals for the future behavior of autonomous systems in Markov Decision Processes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical framework used to learn efficient multi-objective decisions with confidence guarantees under outcome uncertainty.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical framework used to reject unreliable answers in retrieval tasks to ensure the reliability of product question answering systems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical inference technique that provides provable error rate guarantees for predictive models.</skos:definition>
