  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#adaptive_sampling">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Adaptive Sampling</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data collection method that dynamically adjusts the sampling strategy based on observed results to improve efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data collection strategy that dynamically adjusts the sampling process to minimize estimation error for a probability distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data collection strategy that dynamically selects informative samples to estimate the properties of large streaming networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data collection strategy that iteratively adjusts the sampling process based on previously observed data to optimize representativeness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data collection strategy that iteratively selects the most informative points to approximate a similarity matrix.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data collection strategy that iteratively updates the sampling distribution based on the performance of the model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data collection strategy where the choice of future samples depends on previous observations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data reduction technique that uses multi-objective probability-proportional-to-size samples to efficiently estimate clustering costs and find minimizers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data selection strategy that chooses a subset of informative points to approximate a large kernel matrix.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data summarization algorithm that iteratively selects rows based on their distance to the subspace of previously selected rows.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed optimization technique that adjusts the selection of machines based on local Lipschitz constants to accelerate convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for dynamically adjusting sampling probabilities based on thresholds to maintain unbiased estimators in data streams.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of adjusting the data collection pattern in real-time based on the current state or predicted importance of specific regions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method that dynamically adjusts the selection of data points to improve the efficiency of gradient estimation or model training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that intelligently selects samples from a search space to optimize hyperparameters for model compression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A procedure that dynamically selects the next data points to be sampled to optimize the learning of a function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that dynamically selects samples to maximize power while controlling the false discovery proportion.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A strategy that dynamically allocates a sampling budget across multiple distributions to minimize mean estimation error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[multi-objective probability-proportional-to-size samples] multi-objective probability-proportional-to-size samples</rdfs:comment>
