  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#local_differential_privacy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Local Differential Privacy</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy constraint that ensures individual user data remains private while allowing for the estimation of aggregate statistics like the minimum value.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy definition that measures individual privacy by perturbing inputs before they are sent to an untrusted data aggregator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework that ensures individual data points are randomized before being shared with a central collector.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework that obfuscates user data on the client side before it is shared with a learning algorithm.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is obfuscated on the user's device before being shared with a central collector.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is perturbed by the user before being sent to a central collector to ensure individual privacy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is perturbed by the user before being sent to a central collector.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is perturbed by the user before being sent to a central server to ensure individual records cannot be recovered.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is perturbed by the user before being sent to a collector to ensure individual data points remain private.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is perturbed by the user before being shared with a central aggregator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is perturbed by the user before being shared with a central server.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is perturbed by the user locally before being sent to a collector to ensure zero trust in the curator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is perturbed locally by the user before being sent to a central aggregator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is perturbed on the user's device before being sent to a central aggregator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is perturbed on the user's device before being sent to a central collector.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data is randomized on the user's device before being shared with a central collector.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy framework where data points are individually privatized before being passed to a learning algorithm to estimate distribution parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy mechanism where data is perturbed by the user before being sent to a central aggregator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy model where data is perturbed by the user before being sent to a central server.</rdfs:comment>
