  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#spiking_neural_network">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Spiking Neural Network</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-inspired artificial neural network that communicates via asynchronous binary spikes over time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-inspired computational model that mimics the brain's communication via discrete spikes to store and recall complex patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-inspired computational model that processes information using discrete events called spikes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-inspired computational model that processes information using discrete pulses or spikes rather than continuous activations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-inspired computational model that processes information using discrete spikes and learns via spike-timing-dependent plasticity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-inspired computational model that processes information using discrete spikes rather than continuous values to improve energy efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-inspired computational model that processes spatial-temporal information using discrete spikes to mimic biological neuron dynamics.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-inspired network model that processes information using discrete events rather than continuous activations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-inspired network that communicates via discrete events to improve temporal sparsity and hardware efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-inspired neural network architecture that processes information using discrete spikes rather than continuous values.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-plausible computational model that processes information using discrete spikes to enable energy-efficient unsupervised continual learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bio-plausible neural network that processes information using discrete spikes rather than continuous values.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A biologically inspired architecture that processes information using discrete events called spikes over time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A biologically inspired architecture that processes information using discrete events known as spikes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A biologically inspired architecture that processes information using discrete, temporally sparse spike events.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A biologically inspired computational model that encodes information in sparse temporal binary spike streams to reduce energy consumption.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A biologically inspired computational model that processes information using binary neural dynamic activations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A biologically inspired computational model that processes information using discrete events called spikes.</rdfs:comment>
