  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#active_inference">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Active Inference</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian modeling approach where an agent selects actions to minimize expected free energy and satisfy prior preferences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational framework where agents act to maximize the evidence for a generative model of their environment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making framework that selects actions to maximize a mathematical notion of free energy to reduce uncertainty about the environment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework for describing agent behavior based on the minimization of expected free energy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for agent behavior based on the minimization of variational free energy to optimize trial design and environmental interaction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework based on variational Bayesian inference used for state-estimation, control, and learning in biological and artificial agents.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model-based agent framework that minimizes free energy to direct exploration and achieve goals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A normative framework in cognitive neuroscience where agents maximize Bayesian evidence to perform inference, learning, and action.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A normative theory from neuroscience that casts action selection as an inference problem to maintain a model of the world.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic control framework that optimizes action trajectories by minimizing variational free energy in stochastic environments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework for control and path planning that treats action as a form of inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process theory of the brain where organisms infer actions to minimize expected free energy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential decision making framework that resolves the exploration-exploitation trade-off through a neuroscience-inspired strategy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A strategy that optimizes the selection of data points for supervision to minimize Bayesian risk in image restoration.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework based on the principle of minimizing surprise through the use of an internal generative model to drive agent perception and action.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework for cognitive modeling where an agent minimizes variational free energy to control motor trajectories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework for decision making that optimizes actions by minimizing variational free energy to achieve desired future states.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework for perception and action based on the minimization of variational free energy to reduce Bayesian surprise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework for perception and action based on the minimization of variational free energy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework for perception and action that minimizes variational free energy to perform fault-tolerant control.</rdfs:comment>
