    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transfers knowledge from a complex teacher model to a simpler student model to improve performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transfers knowledge from a large, complex model to a smaller, more efficient one.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transfers knowledge from a larger, complex model to a smaller, simpler one to improve personalized federated learning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transfers learned features from a teacher model or domain to a student model to improve performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transfers the expertise from a large pre-trained model to a smaller student network.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transfers the predictive distribution of a complex model to a simpler one for faster inference.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transfers the representational power of a large complex model into a smaller, more efficient one.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that uses a pre-trained high-capacity teacher network to train a smaller, more efficient student network.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique used to compress a large teacher model into a smaller student model to improve inference efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique used to compress a multi-step denoising process into a single step to accelerate image generation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique used to transfer knowledge from a complex model to a simpler one or to prevent catastrophic forgetting in incremental learning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique used to transfer knowledge from a complex model to a simpler, more interpretable structural concept graph.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique used to transfer learned representations from a large, complex teacher model to a smaller, efficient student model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique where a compact model is trained to mimic the behavior of a more complex ensemble or model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique where a large teacher model guides a smaller student model to mimic its predictions for efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique where a small model is trained to reproduce the behavior of a larger, more complex model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique where a small student model is trained to mimic the behavior and output distributions of a larger teacher model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique where a small student model is trained to mimic the behavior and output of a larger teacher model.</skos:definition>
