  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#black_box_optimization">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Black Box Optimization</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Black-Box Optimization</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A derivative-free optimization technique used for tuning the hyperparameters of machine learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical method for finding the optimal input of a function when its internal mechanism is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical strategy for finding the optimal input of a function when the internal mechanism is unknown and query costs may vary.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique for finding the extremum of a function when the internal mechanism is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for finding the global optimum of a function where the internal mechanism is unknown and only outputs are observed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for finding the minimum of a function when the internal structure of the function is unknown and evaluations are costly.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for finding the optimal input of a function when the internal mechanism of that function is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for finding the optimal input for a function whose internal mechanism is unknown or too complex to model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A search method that finds the optimal parameters of a system without knowing its internal functional form.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A search method used to find the optimal input for a function whose internal mechanism is unknown or inaccessible.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A search methodology that seeks the global optimum of a function without requiring knowledge of its internal analytical form.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A search methodology used to find the optimal hyperparameters of a function when its internal structure is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A search procedure for finding the optimum of a function when the internal mechanism of the function is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A search strategy used to find the extrema of a function when the internal analytical form of the objective is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A search strategy used to find the global optimum of a function when the internal mechanism of the objective is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A strategy for finding the optimal input for a function where the internal mechanism of the function is unknown or too complex to model analytically.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A strategy for finding the optimal input of a function when the internal mechanism of that function is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for finding the optimal configuration of a system where the internal mechanism is unknown or too complex to model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for finding the optimal input for a function whose internal mechanism is unknown or too complex to be analytically derived.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for finding the optimal input of a function when the internal mechanism of that function is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization process for compute-intensive functions where the internal structure of the objective function is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization process that searches for the optimal parameters of a system without knowing the internal mathematical model of the objective function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization process that seeks to find the optimal input for a function whose internal structure is unknown or not explicitly defined.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization strategy used to find the best parameters of a system without knowing its internal mathematical structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[tuning the hyperparameters of machine learning models] tuning the hyperparameters of machine learning models</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[find the optimal input for a function whose internal mechanism is unknown or inaccessible, find the optimal hyperparameters of a function when its internal structure is unknown] find the optimal hyperparameters of a function when its internal structure is unknown</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[find the extrema of a function when the internal analytical form of the objective is unknown, find the global optimum of a function when the internal mechanism of the objective is unknown] find the extrema of a function when the internal analytical form of the objective is unknown</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[find the best parameters of a system without knowing its internal mathematical structure] find the best parameters of a system without knowing its internal mathematical structure</rdfs:comment>
