    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that reduces the precision of network weights to decrease memory footprint for deployment.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that reduces the precision of network weights to decrease memory usage and computational cost.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that reduces the precision of neural network weights to decrease memory and energy requirements.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that reduces the precision of neural network weights to decrease memory usage and increase inference speed.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that reduces the precision of neural network weights to enable efficient deployment on edge-computing hardware.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that reduces the precision of the weights of a neural network to decrease memory usage and increase speed.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that represents neural network weights using lower-precision numerical formats to reduce memory and power consumption.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A network compression method that reduces the precision of weight parameters to lower the memory footprint of deep networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of reducing the precision of neural network weights to decrease memory usage and increase inference speed.</skos:definition>
