  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#backdoor_attack">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Backdoor Attack</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data poisoning method that injects triggers into training data to induce specific misclassifications in a trained model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data poisoning technique that induces a classifier to misclassify specific inputs containing a trigger pattern into a target class.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious technique in federated learning that reduces model performance on targeted tasks while maintaining accuracy on the main task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious technique that embeds a specific trigger in training data to manipulate future model predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious technique that injects hidden triggers into a model to cause specific misclassifications during inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A poisoning method that embeds a hidden trigger into a model to cause malicious behavior on specific inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A poisoning method that injects hidden triggers into a model to elicit specific malicious behaviors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A poisoning strategy that embeds a secret trigger into a model to force specific misclassifications at test time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A poisoning strategy where an adversary inserts triggered samples into training data to manipulate the model's behavior on specific inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A poisoning technique that implants a hidden trigger in a model to cause specific incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A poisoning technique that injects a trigger into a model during training to induce specific misclassifications.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security exploit that embeds a hidden trigger into a model to manipulate its output upon specific input patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security risk where a model is manipulated during training to perform a specific malicious action when triggered by a backdoor.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat in collaborative learning where a malicious party injects a trigger to manipulate the model's output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat in deep neural networks where a poisoned training dataset causes the model to misclassify inputs containing a specific adversary trigger.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat in federated learning where a malicious actor inserts a hidden trigger into a joint model to manipulate predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat targeting the training phase where a model is manipulated to behave abnormally only when a specific trigger is present.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat that utilizes a trigger paradigm to mislead natural language processing models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a classifier is manipulated to predict a target class when a specific pattern is present.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a classifier is poisoned during training to predict a target class whenever a specific trigger pattern is present.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a deep neural network is manipulated to produce specific incorrect outputs when triggered by a hidden pattern.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a hidden trigger is embedded into a deep neural network to maliciously change its predictions on specific samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a hidden trigger is embedded into a neural network to maliciously change its predictions on specific samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a hidden trigger is inserted into a model during training to cause specific misclassifications at test time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a hidden trigger is inserted into a model to cause specific incorrect outputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a malicious actor injects hidden triggers into a model to elicit specific incorrect behaviors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a malicious actor poisons training data to embed a trigger that causes a model to misclassify specific samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a malicious trigger is embedded into a model to cause specific misclassifications on targeted inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a malicious trigger is embedded into training data to cause a model to misbehave at inference time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a malicious trigger is inserted into a model to cause specific incorrect outputs on targeted inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a malicious trigger is inserted into a model to cause specific misclassifications during inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a model is poisoned during training to behave maliciously when presented with a specific trigger.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a model is poisoned during training to produce incorrect outputs when a specific trigger is present.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a model is trained on poisoned data to behave maliciously when a specific trigger is present.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a model is trained to behave normally on clean data but trigger a specific failure on poisoned inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a model is trained to perform abnormally on inputs containing predefined triggers while maintaining normal performance on clean data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where a model is trained to produce a specific adversary-chosen output when a trigger is present.</rdfs:comment>
