    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to automatically discover the representations needed for feature extraction or the other task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical approach that transforms raw data into a more useful set of features for downstream machine learning tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique for automatically discovering the features needed for a task, such as detecting audio patterns using trainable extractors.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that automatically discovers the representations needed for a task from the raw data using neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that jointly uses contextual and knowledge base embeddings to capture both distributional semantics and explicit entity relations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that leverages unlabelled data to initialize a model with a more diverse and general feature set.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transforms data into a format that suppresses bias-inducing dependencies from protected factors.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transforms raw data into a feature space that optimizes performance for a downstream task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transforms raw data into a more useful feature space to preserve essential information.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transforms raw data into a set of features that make it easier to perform downstream tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transforms raw data into a shared structure to facilitate the estimation of heterogeneous treatment effects from mixed data sources.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transforms raw data into meaningful feature representations to improve the performance of downstream tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that transforms raw data into sparse longitudinal features to improve the predictive performance of a model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A training objective focused on extracting meaningful features from data to improve classification and generalization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised approach that automatically discovers the best features for representing raw data in a continuous space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised approach that extracts deep contextualized acoustic features from audio data to improve speech recognition.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised approach that transforms raw data into a low-dimensional feature space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised approach to automatically discover the best features or vectors to represent raw data for downstream tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised approach to learning a low-dimensional mapping of high-dimensional data to improve the performance of downstream tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised approach to learning a usable set of features or embeddings from raw data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised technique that seeks to discover the underlying features or patterns of raw data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The process of discovering nonlinear data representations that are optimal for a specific downstream task.</skos:definition>
