  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#invertibleneuralnetwork">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Invertibleneuralnetwork</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bidirectional architecture capable of mapping inputs to outputs and vice versa without losing information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that allows for the full recovery of input data from its hidden representations through a one-to-one mapping.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture where every layer is a bijective mapping, allowing for exact reconstruction of the input from the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture where the mapping from input to output is bijective, allowing for the exact reconstruction of the input from the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative architecture that represents multiple plausible solutions to a registration problem as a probability distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model architecture used to discover hidden symmetries by minimizing the violation of partial differential equations through coordinate transformations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed as a bijective mapping that allows for efficient computation in both forward and reverse directions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed such that the mapping from input to output can be exactly reversed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed such that the mapping from input to output can be mathematically reversed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed to be mathematically reversible, used here to sample the topology of lattice gauge theories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed to model binary operations that satisfy specific algebraic requirements like associativity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that allows for the exact reconstruction of inputs from outputs via a bijective mapping.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that implements a bijective mapping, allowing for exact reconstruction of the input from the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that implements a bijective transformation to enable the exact reconstruction of high-resolution data from downscaled versions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture where the mapping between input and output is bijective, allowing for exact reconstruction of the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture where the mapping between input and output is bijective, enabling memory-efficient training by avoiding stored activations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture constructed from simple building blocks and composition rules that allows for efficient inversion and generative use as flow models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to be mathematically reversible to enable efficient probabilistic and generative modeling.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that allows for exact mapping between input and output spaces, enabling efficient density estimation and sampling.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that allows for simultaneous optimization and bidirectional mapping between inputs and outputs to solve inverse problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that allows for the mapping from output back to input, enabling an inverse modeling approach for structural design.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that can map a reference distribution to a posterior parameter distribution for efficient Bayesian reconstruction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where the mapping between input and output is bijective, allowing for efficient exact inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where the mapping between input and output is bijective, allowing for exact reconstruction of the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where the mapping from input to output can be mathematically reversed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where the mapping from input to output is bijective, allowing for exact reconstruction of the input from the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A specialized architecture that can learn both a forward process and its inverse to determine hidden parameters from measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of architecture designed to be mathematically reversible, allowing for the direct mapping from output back to input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of architecture where the mapping between input and output is bijective, allowing for exact reconstruction of the input from the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of architecture where the mapping from input to output is bijective, allowing for perfect reconstruction of the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of deep network architecture that allows for bidirectional mapping between input and output spaces for signal decoding and generation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[discover hidden symmetries by minimizing the violation of partial differential equations through coordinate transformations] discover hidden symmetries by minimizing the violation of partial differential equations through coordinate transformations</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[be mathematically reversible] be mathematically reversible</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[model binary operations that satisfy specific algebraic requirements like associativity] model binary operations that satisfy specific algebraic requirements like associativity</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[be mathematically reversible to enable efficient probabilistic and generative modeling] be mathematically reversible to enable efficient probabilistic and generative modeling</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[inputs to outputs] input to output</rdfs:comment>
