    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture where the mapping between input and output is bijective, enabling memory-efficient training by avoiding stored activations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture constructed from simple building blocks and composition rules that allows for efficient inversion and generative use as flow models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to be mathematically reversible to enable efficient probabilistic and generative modeling.</skos:definition>
