    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where the mapping from input to output is bijective, allowing for exact reconstruction of the input from the output.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A specialized architecture that can learn both a forward process and its inverse to determine hidden parameters from measurements.</skos:definition>
