  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#multi_objective_reinforcement_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Multi-Objective Reinforcement Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making framework that optimizes multiple often conflicting reward signals simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for learning policies that optimize multiple, potentially conflicting, reward functions simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework where an agent learns to optimize a vector of multiple, potentially conflicting reward signals simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning framework designed to optimize multiple conflicting objectives simultaneously to approximate a Pareto frontier.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent must optimize multiple, potentially conflicting, reward signals simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent optimizes multiple, potentially conflicting, reward functions simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent optimizes policies across multiple competing objectives with varying preferences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm where an agent optimizes a vector of multiple reward signals rather than a single scalar value.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach that optimizes a policy to satisfy multiple, often conflicting, reward signals simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework designed to optimize multiple competing goals simultaneously using adaptive weights.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that balances multiple competing objectives, such as safety and performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that optimizes multiple objectives simultaneously, often using a weighted sum of rewards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that optimizes multiple, potentially conflicting reward functions simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that seeks to optimize multiple conflicting objectives simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that seeks to optimize multiple, potentially conflicting, reward signals simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework where an agent must optimize multiple, often conflicting, reward functions simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential decision-making framework that accounts for multiple players with differing beliefs and utility functions to find Pareto optimal policies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An agent-learning framework designed to optimize multiple, potentially conflicting reward signals simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An extension of RL that optimizes multiple competing reward signals simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An extension of reinforcement learning that enables an agent to learn optimal policies when multiple competing objectives must be balanced.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An extension of reinforcement learning that optimizes multiple, potentially conflicting, reward signals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An extension of reinforcement learning where an agent seeks to optimize multiple, potentially conflicting, reward signals simultaneously.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[optimize multiple conflicting objectives simultaneously to approximate a pareto frontier] optimize multiple conflicting objectives simultaneously to approximate a pareto frontier</rdfs:comment>
