    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A decision-making framework that optimizes multiple often conflicting reward signals simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework for learning policies that optimize multiple, potentially conflicting, reward functions simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework where an agent learns to optimize a vector of multiple, potentially conflicting reward signals simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning framework designed to optimize multiple conflicting objectives simultaneously to approximate a Pareto frontier.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent must optimize multiple, potentially conflicting, reward signals simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent optimizes multiple, potentially conflicting, reward functions simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent optimizes policies across multiple competing objectives with varying preferences.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm where an agent optimizes a vector of multiple reward signals rather than a single scalar value.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach that optimizes a policy to satisfy multiple, often conflicting, reward signals simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework designed to optimize multiple competing goals simultaneously using adaptive weights.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that balances multiple competing objectives, such as safety and performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that optimizes multiple objectives simultaneously, often using a weighted sum of rewards.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that optimizes multiple, potentially conflicting reward functions simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that seeks to optimize multiple conflicting objectives simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that seeks to optimize multiple, potentially conflicting, reward signals simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework where an agent must optimize multiple, often conflicting, reward functions simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequential decision-making framework that accounts for multiple players with differing beliefs and utility functions to find Pareto optimal policies.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An agent-learning framework designed to optimize multiple, potentially conflicting reward signals simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An extension of RL that optimizes multiple competing reward signals simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An extension of reinforcement learning that enables an agent to learn optimal policies when multiple competing objectives must be balanced.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An extension of reinforcement learning that optimizes multiple, potentially conflicting, reward signals.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An extension of reinforcement learning where an agent seeks to optimize multiple, potentially conflicting, reward signals simultaneously.</skos:definition>
