  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#recursive_neural_network">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Recursive Neural Network</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of deep learning model that operates on structured inputs, such as trees, by applying a weight matrix recursively.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that captures structural information from trees to label instances in natural language processing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that applies the same set of weights recursively over a structured input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A network architecture that processes hierarchical structures by recursively grouping parts to generate a root code.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture with a tree-like design capable of capturing compositional patterns in algebraic expressions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that processes data in a tree-like structure to learn hierarchical representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that processes data with a tree-like structural encoding, making it suitable for hierarchical data like mathematical formulae.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network that applies the same weights recursively to process structured data, often in a tree-like or fractal manner.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-linear adaptive model designed to process and learn deep structured information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A structural model that processes hierarchical data by applying a weight matrix recursively to a tree-like input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of architecture that processes structured data by applying a function recursively over a graph or tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of deep learning model that processes structured data by applying the same set of weights recursively over a tree-like structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of network architecture that operates on tree-structured data by recursively applying the same operation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of network architecture that processes structured inputs by recursively applying the same set of weights over a tree-like structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of neural network architecture that processes structured data by recursively applying the same set of weights over a tree-like structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of neural network designed to process data with a hierarchical or recursive structure by applying the same set of weights recursively.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of neural network that processes data with a nested or hierarchical structure, such as discourse trees.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of neural network that processes structured data by applying the same set of weights recursively over a tree structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of neural network that processes structured input by recursively applying the same set of weights over a tree-like structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the same set of weights recursively over a structured input, the same weights recursively] same weights recursively</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[hierarchical structures by recursively grouping parts] hierarchical structures by recursively grouping parts</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[data] data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[structured data] structured data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[and learn deep structured information] and learn deep structured information</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[hierarchical data by applying a weight matrix recursively, structured data by applying the same set of weights recursively over a tree-like structure, structured inputs by recursively applying the same set of weights over a tree-like structure, structured data by recursively applying the same set of weights over a tree-like structure, data with a hierarchical or recursive structure by applying the same set of weights recursively, structured data by applying the same set of weights recursively over a tree structure, structured input by recursively applying the same set of weights over a tree-like structure] same weights recursively</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[structured data by applying a function recursively over a graph or tree] structured data by applying a function recursively over a graph or tree</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[hierarchical data] hierarchical data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a root code] root code</rdfs:comment>
