  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#incremental_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Incremental Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A continual learning method that uses optimal weight initialization from a simpler task to solve a more complex environment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for building agents that can quickly learn to respond to demands and continue to update their knowledge throughout their life.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that allows a model to be updated continuously as new data arrives without retraining from scratch.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that allows a model to be updated with new data over time without retraining from scratch.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that updates a model in real time to adapt to changing patterns in streaming network data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning method that allows a model to continuously integrate new data without forgetting previously acquired knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning method that updates an existing classifier by explicitly modeling data modifications instead of retraining from scratch.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning methodology that allows a model to continuously incorporate new data without forgetting previously acquired knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to acquire new knowledge continuously without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to acquire new knowledge from new classes without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to acquire new knowledge over time without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to acquire new knowledge without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to be updated continuously as new data arrives without retraining from scratch.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to be updated with new data over time without forgetting previous knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to continuously acquire new knowledge without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to continuously integrate new data and classes without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to continuously integrate new knowledge without forgetting previous information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that allows a model to learn new classes over time while maintaining a constant model complexity and bounded memory.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that updates a model to include new categories over time without losing access to previous data and annotations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model continuously updates its knowledge as new data arrives without forgetting previous information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model is updated continuously as new data arrives without retraining from scratch.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model is updated with new data without retraining on the entire previous dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning process that allows a model to acquire new knowledge or classes sequentially without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning process that allows a model to acquire new knowledge over time without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning process where a model is continuously updated with new data to improve performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning process where a model is continuously updated with new data without forgetting previously acquired knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning strategy that allows a model to acquire new knowledge sequentially without forgetting previous information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that allows a model to be updated continuously as new data arrives without forgetting previously learned information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that allows a model to continuously learn from new data without forgetting previously acquired knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that allows a model to learn new tasks sequentially without forgetting previously acquired knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
