    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm where the training process is spread across multiple computing nodes to handle large datasets or models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A multi-agent computational framework where entities optimize resource allocation in a decentralized system.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A paradigm where a model is trained across multiple computing nodes to handle large datasets or decentralized data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A paradigm where multiple organizations collaboratively train a model without sharing their private raw data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process where multiple agents on a graph aggregate beliefs to discern the true state of the world through sparse communication.</skos:definition>
