  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#probabilistic_model">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Probabilistic Model</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that uses neural networks to estimate the per-instance reliability of multiple annotators and determine correct labels from noisy data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative framework that leverages time-frequency representations to produce high-fidelity audio samples with long-range structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that incorporates random variables to represent uncertainty in data and predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that represents the likelihood of object detection by mapping an image into a probability distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that represents the probability distribution of observed data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to relate latent variables to observed data for prediction and evidence generation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to relate noisy labels to their corresponding instances for robust training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to represent and estimate the likelihood of object affordances based on sensorimotor experience.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to represent the latent structure of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to represent the likelihood of different outcomes in a system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to represent the uncertainty and relationships between variables in a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to represent the uncertainty of a system or process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to represent uncertainty and learn disentangled representations of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to represent uncertainty and learn latent logic rules for knowledge graph reasoning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to represent uncertainty and model data patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses probability distributions to simulate and detect collective behavior patterns in crowds.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical framework that estimates drift and diffusion in stochastic differential equations using adversarial inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical framework that estimates label quality and ground truth in crowdsourcing by accounting for worker attention levels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical framework that incorporates expert feedback to predict drug efficacy using high-dimensional genomic measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical framework used to extrapolate the learning curves of iterative machine learning algorithms based on variable-length data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[probability distributions] probability distribution</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[high-dimensional genomic measurements] high-dimensional genomic measurements</rdfs:comment>
