  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#black_box_attack">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Black-Box Attack</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for extracting sensitive information from a machine learning model without knowing its internal architecture or parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for generating adversarial examples without having direct access to the internal parameters of the target model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of generating adversarial examples where the attacker has no knowledge of the internal parameters of the target classifier.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of generating adversarial perturbations to fool a classifier without having access to the internal model parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A query-efficient method for generating adversarial examples to mislead a classifier without requiring internal knowledge of the model architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security evaluation method that probes a model's robustness by querying it without knowledge of its internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security method that attempts to deceive a machine learning model without having access to its internal parameters or architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security method that crafts adversarial examples to force misclassification without internal knowledge of the target network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security method used to generate adversarial examples against a target model without knowledge of its internal architecture or parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security methodology that attempts to deceive a machine learning model without having access to its internal architecture or parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where an adversary attempts to deceive a model without having access to its internal architecture or parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security threat where an adversary uses substitute models to generate adversarial examples to mislead a target deep neural network without internal access.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security vulnerability where internal model attributes are exposed through a sequence of queries to generate adversarial examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial attack where the attacker has no knowledge of the internal weights or architecture of the target model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that attempts to deceive a classifier by querying its outputs without knowledge of its internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that attempts to deceive a machine learning model without having access to its internal architecture or parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that attempts to deceive a machine learning model without knowledge of its internal architecture or parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that attempts to deceive a model without having access to its internal architecture or gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that attempts to deceive a target model without having access to its internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that attempts to fool a classifier using only query access without knowledge of the model's internal gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that attempts to fool a model without having access to its internal parameters or architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that attempts to fool a model without having access to its internal parameters or gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that attempts to mislead a model using only the output labels without access to the internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that attempts to mislead a model without having access to its internal parameters or architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that creates perturbations to misclassify a target model using only query-label pairs without internal model access.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that fools a target model by identifying discriminative areas and applying local perturbations without knowing the model's internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that generates malicious examples using only loss-oracle access to a target model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An adversarial method that generates malicious inputs to trigger model failure without requiring access to the target model's internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
