  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#synthetic_data_generation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Synthetic Data Generation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation process that creates artificial training examples with ground-truth annotations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for creating artificial data that preserves the patterns and characteristics of source data while protecting user privacy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that creates artificial samples to address data imbalance and limited defect samples in quality inspection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression scheme in federated learning where clients transmit lightweight synthetic datasets instead of model updates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial data samples to augment training sets and improve model generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial data samples to augment training sets and improve the performance of supervised learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial data that mimics the properties of real-world data to augment training sets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial data that mimics the statistical properties of real-world data to augment training sets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial data that mimics the statistical properties of real-world datasets for training or analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial data that preserves the statistical properties and privacy of the original dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial data to augment training sets and improve the performance of machine learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial data using simulation or generative models to augment training sets or address data scarcity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial data using simulation tools to train machine learning models when real data is scarce.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial data, such as 3D facial models from 2D thermal images, to train deep learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial datasets from 3D models or simulations to train machine learning models when real data is scarce.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial datasets that maintain the statistical properties of real data while protecting individual privacy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial datasets that mimic the patterns and correlations of real-world data for domains with restricted access.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial datasets that mimic the properties of real-world data to facilitate model training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial datasets that mimic the statistical properties of real data to preserve privacy and enable reproducibility.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial datasets through algorithmic pipelines to train models when real data is scarce.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial datasets to improve the training of deep learning models when labeled real-world data is scarce.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial datasets using models to simulate real-world phenomena for training purposes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial datasets using simulators to train machine learning models when real data is scarce or expensive.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial datasets via simulation to automate labeling and expand training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial examples to support supervised learning when labeled data is scarce.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial training datasets using building information modeling and photorealistic rendering to train recognition models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial training examples, such as converting non-polyp images to polyp images, to augment limited medical datasets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial training images to improve the robustness of deep learning models against domain instability.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of creating artificial training samples to train deep networks when supervised medical data is scarce.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of using machine learning models to create artificial data that maintains the statistical properties of a real dataset while preserving privacy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process that creates artificial datasets that maintain the statistical properties of real-world data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process that creates artificial datasets to augment training data while addressing privacy and class imbalance issues.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process that programmatically creates data objects, such as inferring high-resolution records from low-resolution sources.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The process of creating artificial data from simulations to augment training sets for machine learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The process of creating artificial data samples using generative models to address class imbalance in supervised learning tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The process of creating artificial data that mimics the characteristics of real-world data to supplement limited datasets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The process of creating artificial data that mimics the statistical properties of real data while preserving privacy.</rdfs:comment>
