  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#rademacher_complexity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Rademacher Complexity</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A capacity measure of a hypothesis class used to study the excess capacity of deep networks in supervised classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A complexity measure used to bound the generalization error of a hypothesis class by assessing its ability to fit random noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure in computational learning theory that quantifies the richness of a class of real-valued functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of statistical complexity used to quantify the richness of a hypothesis space in quantum circuit models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the capacity of a function class to fit random noise, used here to establish upper bounds on generalization error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the learnability of a hypothesis class based on its ability to fit random noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the richness of a class of functions based on its ability to fit random noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the richness of a class of functions that bounds the excess risk of an estimator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the richness of a class of functions that is used to obtain a priori error estimates for regularized loss functionals.</rdfs:comment>
