    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of how much a model's performance on unseen data deviates from its performance on training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of how well a trained machine learning model performs on new, unseen data compared to its training set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the difference between a model's performance on training data and its performance on unseen test data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the difference between the performance of a model on training data and its performance on unseen data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A performance metric that measures how well a model predicts outcomes for previously unseen data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A performance metric that measures the difference between a model's error on training data and its error on unseen data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical measure of the difference between a model's performance on training data and its performance on unseen data in a networked setting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical measure that quantifies the difference between a model's performance on training data and its performance on unseen data.</rdfs:comment>
