  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#sparse_linear_regression">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sparse Linear Regression</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A predictive modeling approach that identifies a minimal set of important features using an L0 norm penalty.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression method that produces a model with few non-zero coefficients to improve interpretability and prevent overfitting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression technique that estimates a parameter vector where most entries are zero to identify the most relevant features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression technique that identifies a small subset of relevant predictors to fit a linear model to a specific segment of a population.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression technique that produces a model with few non-zero coefficients to handle high-dimensional data with missing values.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression technique that produces models with few non-zero coefficients to improve interpretability and prevent overfitting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression technique that uses regularization penalties to produce models where only a small subset of predictors have non-zero coefficients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method for estimating a linear relationship where only a few predictors have non-zero coefficients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that estimates a linear relationship between variables while constraining most coefficients to be zero.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that identifies a small number of significant predictors from a large set of candidate functions to model dynamical systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An inference problem that aims to find a solution with a minimum number of non-zero coordinates to minimize prediction error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[regularization penalties] regularization penalties</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[important features/predictors] relevant features/predictors</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[model with few non-zero coefficients] model with few non-zero coefficients</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[linear relationship] linear relationship</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[solution with a minimum number of non-zero coordinates] solution with a minimum number of non-zero coordinates</rdfs:comment>
