  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#differential_privacy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Differential Privacy</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A constraint for algorithms that guarantees the output reveals very little about any individual input data record.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A constraint in statistical estimation that ensures the output of an algorithm does not reveal whether a specific individual's data was used in the training set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A cryptographic approach to protect individual-level privacy while permitting database-level utility.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data privacy standard that ensures the output of a mechanism does not reveal whether a specific individual's data was used.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework for ensuring that the inclusion of a single data record in a training set does not significantly affect the output of a model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework for ensuring that the inclusion or exclusion of a single data point does not significantly affect the output of an algorithm.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework for ensuring that the inclusion or exclusion of a single data point in a training set does not significantly affect the output of an algorithm.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework for ensuring that the output of a computation does not reveal sensitive information about any individual in the dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework for ensuring that the output of a data analysis does not reveal individual record presence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework for ensuring that the output of an algorithm does not reveal the presence of any individual record in a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework for ensuring that the output of an algorithm does not reveal whether a specific individual's data was included in the training set.</rdfs:comment>
