    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework that ensures the output of an algorithm does not reveal whether a specific individual's data was included in the training set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework that provides mathematical guarantees on the amount of information leaked by a data-processing mechanism.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework that provides mathematical guarantees to protect individual data points while maintaining the utility of statistical outputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal framework that provides strong privacy guarantees by adding calibrated noise to data releases.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal mathematical framework for ensuring that the output of an algorithm does not reveal whether a specific individual's data was used in the training set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal mathematical framework that ensures individual data records in a dataset cannot be readily identified.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal mathematical framework that ensures the output of an algorithm does not reveal whether a specific individual's data was included in the training set.</rdfs:comment>
