    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A control design paradigm that learns a control policy by reproducing demonstrations from expert agents.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A control method where a deep neural network is trained using data labeled by an expert solver to optimize system operation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework used to learn branching policies for mixed-integer linear programming by imitating strong branching rules.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework where agents learn visuomotor behaviors from human demonstrations, potentially guided by gaze attention.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework where an agent learns to perform a task by mimicking the behavior of an expert demonstration.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework where an agent learns to perform a task by mimicking the behavior of an expert.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework where an agent learns to perform a task by observing and mimicking demonstrations from an expert.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach that recovers an expert policy by observing demonstrations without an explicit reward signal.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach where a model learns to perform a task by mimicking the behavior of an expert.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach where a policy is trained to mimic the behavior of an expert or optimal trajectories to solve complex planning problems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach where a policy is trained to mimic the behavior of an expert, such as an optimal controller generated by Model Predictive Control.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach where a robot acquires new skills by mimicking demonstrations provided by humans in a simulated or real environment.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach where an agent acquires a control policy by mimicking demonstrations provided by an expert.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach where an agent acquires a skill by observing and mimicking the behavior of an expert.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach where an agent is trained to mimic the behavior of an expert demonstrator.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach where an agent is trained to mimic the behavior of an expert or a model-based solver.</skos:definition>
