    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical process that identifies the directional relationships between variables to distinguish causes from effects.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical process used to discover the directed relationships and latent confounders within a data-generating process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A task focused on discovering the directed relationships and dependencies within a heterogeneous population.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A task in machine learning that aims to recover the directed acyclic graph representing causal relationships between variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A task that identifies the underlying causal relationships among a set of random variables through experimental design.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A task that identifies the underlying causal relationships in a model by framing it as a graph theoretic edge clique cover problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A task that involves discovering the directed acyclic graph representing the causal relationships between variables in a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A task that involves learning a directed acyclic graph to discover the causal relationships between variables.</rdfs:comment>
