    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A subfield of artificial intelligence that focuses on making the decision-making processes of machine learning models transparent and understandable to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that allow human users to comprehend and trust the results created by machine learning algorithms.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that allow human users to understand and trust the results and output of machine learning algorithms.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that make the internal logic and decision-making process of a model transparent to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that make the internal logic and decision-making processes of black-box models transparent to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that make the internal logic and output of black-box models transparent to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that make the internal logic and outputs of complex models understandable to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that make the internal logic of machine learning models transparent to human users.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that make the internal mechanisms of AI systems transparent and interpretable to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that make the internal mechanisms of machine learning models transparent to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that make the output of machine learning models understandable and transparent to human experts.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that make the outputs of machine learning models transparent and understandable.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods and techniques that make the results of machine learning models understandable to human users.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods designed to make the internal decision-making processes of black-box models transparent and interpretable to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods designed to make the internal logic and decisions of black-box models transparent to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods designed to make the internal logic and decisions of machine learning models transparent to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods that make the internal logic and decision-making process of a model transparent to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A suite of methods that makes the internal logic and outputs of machine learning models understandable to humans.</skos:definition>
