  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#no_regret_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">No-Regret Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms designed to ensure that the cumulative loss of the learner is not significantly worse than the loss of the best fixed strategy in hindsight.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of online algorithms designed to minimize the difference between the actual cumulative loss and the loss of the best fixed action.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of online learning algorithms where the difference between the cumulative loss and the loss of the best fixed action grows sublinearly.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning framework in multi-agent systems designed to minimize the difference between actual and optimal cumulative rewards in repeated games.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for designing weighting schemes in voting systems to ensure choices are almost as good as those of the best voter in hindsight.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A game-theoretic framework that minimizes the difference between the actual payoff and the best possible payoff in hindsight.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning strategy in games that aims to minimize the difference between the actual reward and the reward of the best fixed policy in hindsight.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A strategy in repeated games where a learner minimizes the difference between their actual payoff and the best possible payoff in hindsight.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithmic approach in game theory where an agent minimizes the difference between its cumulative loss and the loss of the best fixed action in hindsight.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithmic approach to sequential decision making that ensures the cumulative loss is not significantly worse than the best fixed action.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithmic framework in game theory and online learning where the agent's cumulative loss is not significantly worse than the loss of the best fixed strategy in hindsight.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithmic framework where agents iteratively update their strategies to minimize the difference between their actual reward and the best possible fixed strategy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithmic framework where the learner minimizes the difference between the actual reward and the reward of the best fixed action in hindsight.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithmic property where the cumulative loss of a learner is not significantly worse than the loss of the best fixed action in hindsight.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An online learning framework where the average regret of the learner vanishes as the number of iterations increases.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An online learning strategy where the difference between the cumulative loss of the learner and the best fixed action in hindsight is minimized.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[ensure that the cumulative loss of the learner is not significantly worse than the loss of the best fixed strategy in hindsight] ensure that the cumulative loss of the learner is not significantly worse than the loss of the best fixed strategy in hindsight</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[minimize the difference between the actual cumulative loss and the loss of the best fixed action] cumulative loss is not significantly worse than the best fixed action</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[minimize the difference between actual and optimal cumulative rewards in repeated games] minimize the difference between actual and optimal cumulative rewards in repeated games</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[weighting schemes in voting systems] weighting schemes in voting systems</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the difference between actual performance and the best fixed action/strategy] difference between actual performance and the best fixed action/strategy</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[cumulative loss is not significantly worse than the best fixed action] cumulative loss is not significantly worse than the best fixed action</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms designed to ensure that the cumulative loss of the learner is not significantly worse than the loss of the best fixed strategy in hindsight.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of online algorithms designed to minimize the difference between the actual cumulative loss and the loss of the best fixed action.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of online learning algorithms where the difference between the cumulative loss and the loss of the best fixed action grows sublinearly.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A distributed learning framework in multi-agent systems designed to minimize the difference between actual and optimal cumulative rewards in repeated games.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework for designing weighting schemes in voting systems to ensure choices are almost as good as those of the best voter in hindsight.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A game-theoretic framework that minimizes the difference between the actual payoff and the best possible payoff in hindsight.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning strategy in games that aims to minimize the difference between the actual reward and the reward of the best fixed policy in hindsight.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A strategy in repeated games where a learner minimizes the difference between their actual payoff and the best possible payoff in hindsight.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic approach in game theory where an agent minimizes the difference between its cumulative loss and the loss of the best fixed action in hindsight.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic approach to sequential decision making that ensures the cumulative loss is not significantly worse than the best fixed action.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic framework in game theory and online learning where the agent's cumulative loss is not significantly worse than the loss of the best fixed strategy in hindsight.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic framework where agents iteratively update their strategies to minimize the difference between their actual reward and the best possible fixed strategy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic framework where the learner minimizes the difference between the actual reward and the reward of the best fixed action in hindsight.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic property where the cumulative loss of a learner is not significantly worse than the loss of the best fixed action in hindsight.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An online learning framework where the average regret of the learner vanishes as the number of iterations increases.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An online learning strategy where the difference between the cumulative loss of the learner and the best fixed action in hindsight is minimized.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#ml_foundations_and_theory"/>
    <ml:optimizes rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#regret"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#3d_convolutional_neural_network">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">3D Convolutional Neural Network</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture designed for volumetric data segmentation by processing three-dimensional spatial information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture designed to extract spatial features from volumetric data represented as voxels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture designed to process volumetric spatial data for disease status prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutional filters across three dimensions to classify volumetric medical imaging data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutional filters across three dimensions to extract spatiotemporal features from video data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutional filters across three spatial dimensions to analyze volumetric data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutional filters across three spatial dimensions to extract volumetric features from data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions across three dimensions to analyze spatio-temporal data in videos.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions across three dimensions to extract spatio-temporal features from video sequences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions across three dimensions to process volumetric or temporal data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions across three spatial dimensions to analyze volumetric medical images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions over three-dimensional volumes to detect lung nodules from CT scans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions over three-dimensional volumes to perform automatic segmentation of medical images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions over three-dimensional voxel representations to learn spatial interactions in atomic configurations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies three-dimensional convolutions to extract features from volumetric grid representations of molecular complexes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies three-dimensional filters to volumetric data for tasks such as medical image segmentation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that extends convolutions to three dimensions to process volumetric or temporal data such as video.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that processes volumetric data by factorizing kernels along the temporal dimension for efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that processes volumetric data or sequences of images to identify spatial-temporal patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that processes volumetric data to assess the malignancy of pulmonary nodules.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that processes volumetric data, such as angle-delay channel power matrices, to estimate three-dimensional user positions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that processes volumetric image data to perform regression tasks such as organ-based age estimation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture used for recognizing human activities from video streams.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that applies convolutions across spatial and temporal dimensions to process volumetric data or video.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that applies convolutions in three dimensions to interpret protein-ligand complexes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that applies three-dimensional convolutions to volumetric medical images for patch-wise binary classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that learns spatiotemporal features from consecutive video frames for surgical gesture recognition.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that uses multi-modality feature learning to predict distant metastases from PET-CT imaging data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that applies convolutions across three spatial dimensions to process volumetric data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that applies convolutions over three-dimensional data to capture spatial-temporal features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that applies convolutions over three-dimensional data to extract volumetric spatial features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that extracts features from video data to detect suspicious behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that processes spatiotemporal information from video frames to recognize facial micro-expressions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that processes volumetric data by applying three-dimensional filters to capture spatial voxel information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[volumetric data segmentation by processing three-dimensional spatial information, extract spatial features from volumetric data represented as voxels] volumetric data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[process volumetric spatial data for disease status prediction] volumetric spatial data for disease status prediction</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[spatial features from volumetric data represented as voxels, volumetric features from data, volumetric spatial features] volumetric data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[spatiotemporal features from video data, spatio-temporal features from video sequences] spatiotemporal data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[features from volumetric grid representations of molecular complexes] features from volumetric grid representations of molecular complexes</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[features] features</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[volumetric spatial data for disease status prediction] volumetric spatial data for disease status prediction</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[volumetric or temporal data, volumetric or temporal data such as video, volumetric data by factorizing kernels along the temporal dimension, volumetric data or sequences of images, volumetric data, volumetric image data, volumetric data or video, volumetric data by applying three-dimensional filters] volumetric data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[spatiotemporal information] spatiotemporal data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[convolutional filters across three dimensions, convolutional filters across three spatial dimensions, convolutions across three dimensions, convolutions across three spatial dimensions, convolutions over three-dimensional volumes, convolutions over three-dimensional voxel representations, three-dimensional convolutions, three-dimensional filters, convolutions across spatial and temporal dimensions, convolutions over three-dimensional data] three-dimensional filters</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[convolutions] convolution</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[recognizing human activities from video streams] recognizing human activities from video streams</rdfs:comment>
