    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions across three dimensions to process volumetric or temporal data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions across three spatial dimensions to analyze volumetric medical images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions over three-dimensional volumes to detect lung nodules from CT scans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions over three-dimensional volumes to perform automatic segmentation of medical images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies convolutions over three-dimensional voxel representations to learn spatial interactions in atomic configurations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies three-dimensional convolutions to extract features from volumetric grid representations of molecular complexes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that applies three-dimensional filters to volumetric data for tasks such as medical image segmentation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that extends convolutions to three dimensions to process volumetric or temporal data such as video.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that processes volumetric data by factorizing kernels along the temporal dimension for efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that processes volumetric data or sequences of images to identify spatial-temporal patterns.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that processes volumetric data to assess the malignancy of pulmonary nodules.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that processes volumetric data, such as angle-delay channel power matrices, to estimate three-dimensional user positions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that processes volumetric image data to perform regression tasks such as organ-based age estimation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture used for recognizing human activities from video streams.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that applies convolutions across spatial and temporal dimensions to process volumetric data or video.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning model that applies convolutions in three dimensions to interpret protein-ligand complexes.</skos:definition>
