  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#dirichlet_process_mixture_model">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dirichlet Process Mixture Model</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian non-parametric clustering approach that allows the number of clusters to grow with the data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian non-parametric clustering method that allows for an infinite number of components to be automatically determined from the data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian non-parametric clustering model that allows the number of clusters to be inferred from the data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian non-parametric model used for clustering data into an unknown number of subgroups.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian nonparametric clustering model where the number of components is inferred from the posterior distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian nonparametric mixture model that adapts its complexity to the data for clustering tasks where the number of clusters is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian nonparametric model that clusters data by allowing the number of components to grow dynamically with the data size.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian nonparametric model that clusters data by allowing the number of components to grow with the data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian nonparametric model used for clustering data with an unknown number of components.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian nonparametric model used for density estimation that allows for an infinite number of mixture components.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bayesian non-parametric model that clusters data into an unknown number of components.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-parametric Bayesian approach used to automatically determine the number of clusters in dynamic texture segmentation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-parametric Bayesian clustering method that allows the number of components to grow automatically based on the data complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-parametric clustering algorithm used to model normal behavior for probabilistic anomaly detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A nonparametric Bayesian clustering method that allows for an infinite number of potential clusters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A nonparametric Bayesian clustering method that allows for an infinite number of potential components to represent data distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A nonparametric Bayesian method used for online clustering when the number of clusters is unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A nonparametric bayesian method that clusters data by allowing an infinite number of components.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[clustering data into an unknown number of subgroups, clustering data with an unknown number of components] clustering data into an unknown number of subgroups</rdfs:comment>
