  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#pointer_network">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pointer Network</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses an attention mechanism to output a pointer to a specific element of the input sequence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture capable of copying elements from an input sequence to generate natural language descriptions from structured knowledge bases.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed to output a permutation of the input sequence by pointing to specific input elements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed to output a permutation of the input sequence by using an attention mechanism as a pointer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed to output a pointer to a specific element of the input sequence rather than a fixed vocabulary word.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that combines recurrent networks with attention to output positions of elements in an input sequence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that uses an attention-like mechanism to output a pointer to a specific element of the input sequence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that uses attention mechanisms to select members of an input sequence as the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to output a permutation of the input sequence for combinatorial optimization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses an attention mechanism to output a permutation of the input sequence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses an attention mechanism to output a sequence of pointers to input elements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of recurrent neural network designed to output a sequence of pointers to the input sequence, often used for tasks like identifying room layouts from point-clouds.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An attention-based recurrent network designed to produce a sequence of indices as output, suitable for combinatorial optimization problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[tasks like identifying room layouts from point-clouds] tasks like identifying room layouts from point-clouds</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[natural language descriptions from structured knowledge bases] natural language descriptions from structured knowledge bases</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[output a permutation of the input sequence by pointing to specific input elements, output a permutation of the input sequence by using an attention mechanism as a pointer, output a sequence of pointers to the input sequence] output a sequence of pointers to the input sequence</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[output a pointer to a specific element of the input sequence rather than a fixed vocabulary word] output a pointer to a specific element of the input sequence rather than a fixed vocabulary word</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[output a permutation of the input sequence for combinatorial optimization] output a permutation of the input sequence for combinatorial optimization</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[produce a sequence of indices as output] produce a sequence of indices as output</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[positions of elements in an input sequence] positions of elements in an input sequence</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses an attention mechanism to output a pointer to a specific element of the input sequence.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture capable of copying elements from an input sequence to generate natural language descriptions from structured knowledge bases.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed to output a permutation of the input sequence by pointing to specific input elements.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed to output a permutation of the input sequence by using an attention mechanism as a pointer.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture designed to output a pointer to a specific element of the input sequence rather than a fixed vocabulary word.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that combines recurrent networks with attention to output positions of elements in an input sequence.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that uses an attention-like mechanism to output a pointer to a specific element of the input sequence.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that uses attention mechanisms to select members of an input sequence as the output.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to output a permutation of the input sequence for combinatorial optimization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses an attention mechanism to output a permutation of the input sequence.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses an attention mechanism to output a sequence of pointers to input elements.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of recurrent neural network designed to output a sequence of pointers to the input sequence, often used for tasks like identifying room layouts from point-clouds.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An attention-based recurrent network designed to produce a sequence of indices as output, suitable for combinatorial optimization problems.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#attention_based_architectures"/>
    <ml:hasComponent rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#attention_mechanism"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#deep_autoencoder">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Deep Autoencoder</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning method used to effectively extract abstract information from datasets through non-linear feature transformation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multi-layer neural network used for unsupervised feature extraction and dimensionality reduction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multi-layered neural network designed to reconstruct its input to identify anomalies based on reconstruction error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multi-layered neural network used for unsupervised feature learning and anomaly detection by reconstructing input signals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that encodes and decodes sequences to determine if a pattern is normal or abnormal.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn compressed representations of input data for efficient reconstruction and quantization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn compressed, hierarchical representations of input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient compressed representations of input data for tasks like content retrieval.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data codings in an unsupervised manner by reconstructing its input at the output layer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient representations of input data by reconstructing the input at the output layer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient unsupervised representations of input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of input data for tasks such as missing data imputation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of input data for use in physics-based simulations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of input data in an unsupervised manner using multiple hidden layers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of input data to generate a binary mask for signal enhancement.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of input data to reconstruct missing or noisy information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture used for rating prediction in recommender systems by learning compressed representations of user-item interactions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture used for unsupervised feature learning that jointly optimizes a global reconstruction objective.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture used for unsupervised learning of efficient data codings to detect anomalies in high-dimensional input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture used to encode musical input and reconstruct it by selecting units from a finite library.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture used to jointly compress and reconstruct log-likelihood ratio values for efficient storage.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture used to learn efficient representations of data for tasks like cross-domain mapping.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture used to learn low-dimensional feature representations for predicting audio-visual quality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network designed to learn a compressed representation of input data for tasks such as anomaly detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network designed to learn efficient compressed representations of input data for reconstruction.</rdfs:comment>
