  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#stochastic_differential_equation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Stochastic Differential Equation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A differential equation that incorporates random noise to model the evolution of a system over continuous time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for modeling random processes used here to create plug-in layers for computer vision networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to approximate the training dynamics of deep networks to predict convergence time without actual training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to govern dynamics in a latent space for reconstructing videos from event camera data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to model the continuous-time evolution and stability of GAN training processes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to model the continuous-time evolution of gradient-based optimization algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to model the dynamics of systems that evolve over time with intrinsic randomness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to model the evolution of a random covariance matrix in infinite-depth neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to model the evolution of systems subject to random noise over time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model that describes systems with abrupt or jumping behaviors under non-Gaussian noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model that describes the evolution of a system over time incorporating both deterministic and random components.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model that describes the evolution of a system subject to random fluctuations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model that describes the evolution of a system subject to random noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model used as a basis for generative time series models to estimate drift and volatility parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model used to approximate the training and generalization dynamics of neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model used to approximate the training process of residual networks with noise injection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model used to characterize the second-order moments of non-uniformly sampled time series data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model used to describe the evolution of features during the training of deep learning models using stochastic gradient descent.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical representation of a dynamical system that incorporates both deterministic and random components.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[approximate the training dynamics of deep networks to predict convergence time without actual training, approximate the training and generalization dynamics of neural networks] approximate the training and generalization dynamics of neural networks</rdfs:comment>
