    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A differential equation that incorporates random noise to model the evolution of a system over continuous time.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for modeling random processes used here to create plug-in layers for computer vision networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to approximate the training dynamics of deep networks to predict convergence time without actual training.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to govern dynamics in a latent space for reconstructing videos from event camera data.</skos:definition>
