  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#blackboxadversarialattack">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Blackboxadversarialattack</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for fooling a model where the attacker only has access to the outputs and not the internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for generating adversarial examples to fool a machine learning model without having access to the model's internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for generating adversarial examples to fool a neural network without having access to the model's internal parameters or architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for generating adversarial examples without knowledge of the target model's internal parameters or architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for generating adversarial perturbations to fool a target network without having access to its internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for generating adversarial perturbations without having access to the target model's internal parameters or gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for generating adversarial samples to test the robustness of a model without requiring knowledge of its internal parameters or architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for perturbing samples to cause misclustering in clustering models without knowledge of the internal model parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of crafting perturbed inputs to mislead a model without having access to its internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of finding input perturbations to mislead a model without having access to its internal parameters or gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of generating adversarial examples where the attacker has no access to the model's internal gradients or architecture and relies solely on query responses.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of generating deceptive inputs to fool a model without having access to its internal parameters or gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of generating imperceptible input perturbations to fool a classifier without having access to the model's internal parameters</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of generating perturbations to fool a model without having access to its internal parameters or gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of inducing model misclassification by modifying input samples without requiring knowledge of the target model's internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of perturbing input data to fool a model without having access to the internal parameters or architecture of the target system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model evasion technique that estimates gradients using sign-based rather than magnitude-based optimization to bypass security measures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security evaluation method that attempts to mislead a model without having access to its internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security method that attempts to fool a machine learning model without having access to its internal parameters or architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security method that attempts to fool a machine learning model without having access to its internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security technique that attempts to deceive a machine learning model by finding minimal input perturbations without having access to the model's internal parameters.</rdfs:comment>
