  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#random_matrix_theory">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Random Matrix Theory</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A branch of mathematics used to analyze the statistical properties of large matrices to optimize data splitting in regression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the dynamical behavior and convergence rates of inference algorithms in large systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the eigenspectrum of large-dimensional kernel matrices under specific data models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the high-dimensional error landscape of deep neural networks for weight initialization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the properties of matrices with random entries to understand generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the spectral properties of Hessians and loss surfaces in deep neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the spectral properties of large matrices to understand the implicit regularization in deep neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the spectral properties of weight and Hessian matrices in trained deep neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to derive consistent estimators for distances between high-dimensional covariance matrices.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to model the spectral statistics of loss surface Hessians in neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to study the distribution of singular values in the Jacobian of deep untrained neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to study the properties of matrices whose entries are random variables, often applied to analyze neural network weights.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to study the statistical properties of matrices with random entries.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[analyze the statistical properties of large matrices to optimize data splitting in regression] analyze the statistical properties of large matrices to optimize data splitting in regression</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[analyze the dynamical behavior and convergence rates of inference algorithms in large systems] analyze the dynamical behavior and convergence rates of inference algorithms in large systems</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[analyze the eigenspectrum of large-dimensional kernel matrices under specific data models] analyze the eigenspectrum of large-dimensional kernel matrices under specific data models</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[analyze the high-dimensional error landscape of deep neural networks for weight initialization] analyze the high-dimensional error landscape of deep neural networks for weight initialization</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[analyze the properties of matrices with random entries to understand generalization, study the properties of matrices whose entries are random variables, study the statistical properties of matrices with random entries] study the statistical properties of matrices with random entries</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[analyze the spectral properties of hessians and loss surfaces in deep neural networks, analyze the spectral properties of large matrices to understand the implicit regularization in deep neural networks, analyze the spectral properties of weight and hessian matrices in trained deep neural networks, model the spectral statistics of loss surface hessians in neural networks] model the spectral statistics of loss surface hessians in neural networks</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[derive consistent estimators for distances between high-dimensional covariance matrices] derive consistent estimators for distances between high-dimensional covariance matrices</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[study the distribution of singular values in the jacobian of deep untrained neural networks] study the distribution of singular values in the jacobian of deep untrained neural networks</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[analyze neural network weights] analyze neural network weights</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A branch of mathematics used to analyze the statistical properties of large matrices to optimize data splitting in regression.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the dynamical behavior and convergence rates of inference algorithms in large systems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the eigenspectrum of large-dimensional kernel matrices under specific data models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the high-dimensional error landscape of deep neural networks for weight initialization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the properties of matrices with random entries to understand generalization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the spectral properties of Hessians and loss surfaces in deep neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the spectral properties of large matrices to understand the implicit regularization in deep neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the spectral properties of weight and Hessian matrices in trained deep neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to derive consistent estimators for distances between high-dimensional covariance matrices.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to model the spectral statistics of loss surface Hessians in neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to study the distribution of singular values in the Jacobian of deep untrained neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to study the properties of matrices whose entries are random variables, often applied to analyze neural network weights.</skos:definition>
