  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#k_means_clustering">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">K-Means Clustering</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A center-based clustering algorithm that partitions data points into a specified number of clusters by minimizing the distance to centroids.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A centroid-based partitioning algorithm that groups data points into K clusters by minimizing the distance between points and their cluster center.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A centroid-based partitioning algorithm that groups data points into k distinct clusters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A centroid-based unsupervised algorithm that partitions data into k distinct non-overlapping subgroups.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering algorithm that partitions data into groups based on initial centroids.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering algorithm that partitions data into k distinct groups based on centroid proximity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distance-based iterative algorithm that partitions data into a specified number of groups using a chosen metric.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A nonparametric clustering method that partitions data into groups based on distance to centroids.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitional algorithm that groups data points into a predefined number of clusters by minimizing the distance to centroids.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitional algorithm that groups data points into k distinct clusters based on distance to a centroid.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm modified with a penalized dissimilarity measure to handle datasets with missing features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm that divides a dataset into a predefined number of clusters by minimizing intra-cluster variance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm that divides a dataset into k distinct non-overlapping clusters by minimizing the within-cluster sum of squares.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm that divides a dataset into k distinct non-overlapping subgroups based on distance to a centroid.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm that divides a dataset into k distinct non-overlapping subgroups based on feature similarity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm that divides a dataset into k distinct non-overlapping subgroups by minimizing the distance to cluster centroids.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm that divides a dataset into k distinct non-overlapping subgroups by minimizing the variance within each cluster.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm that divides a dataset into k distinct non-overlapping subgroups.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A partitioning algorithm that divides data into K clusters by minimizing the distance between points and their respective centroids.</rdfs:comment>
