  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#determinantal_point_process">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Determinantal Point Process</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework used for subset selection to balance the quality and diversity of selected items.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic measure used to model diversity and negative correlations within a subset of data to prevent mode collapse in generative models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model that characterizes the distribution of diverse sets using matrix determinants.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model that describes the distribution of subsets of elements with a preference for diversity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model that favors the selection of a diverse subset of items from a larger collection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used for discrete subset selection that captures diversity among elements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used for diverse subset selection by modeling the likelihood of subsets based on kernel matrix determinants.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used for sampling diverse subsets of data based on a many-body wavefunction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used for sampling diverse subsets of data from a larger set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used for sampling diverse subsets of elements to improve kernel method approximations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used for sampling diverse subsets of items where the probability is proportional to the volume of the spanned parallelepiped.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used for subset selection that encourages diversity among the chosen elements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used for subset selection that encourages diversity by penalizing similarity between chosen elements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to capture diversity by assigning higher probabilities to subsets of items that are less similar.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to capture diversity by modeling the repulsion between elements in a subset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to capture diversity in a set of sampled points by modeling the interaction between evaluations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to capture negative dependence or repulsion between elements in a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to capture the balance between quality and diversity in the selection of subsets from a larger set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to characterize the diversity of subsets for tasks such as product recommendation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to ensure diversity in the selection of center points for consensus clustering algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to generate sets of points that exhibit repulsion, often used for diverse subset selection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to sample diverse and fair subsets of data from a feature space.</rdfs:comment>
