    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm focused on training models to learn a distance metric that reflects the similarity between data samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that focuses on learning a similarity structure in the representation space to group similar items and separate dissimilar ones.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that optimizes a distance function to ensure similar items are closer in embedding space than dissimilar ones.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that optimizes an embedding space such that the distance between data points reflects their semantic similarity.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that trains neural networks to map data into an embedding space where similar items are close and dissimilar items are far.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning task that aims to produce a deep embedding capable of capturing the semantic similarity between data points.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns a distance function to measure the similarity between pairs of data points in a high-dimensional space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns a distance function to represent semantic similarity between data points using continuous labels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns a distance metric to classify generated images into multiple fine-grained categories.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns a distance metric to embed data into a space where similar items are close together.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns a distance metric to embed data points such that similar items are closer together in the feature space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns an embedding space where similar items are placed closer together and dissimilar items further apart.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns embedding vectors to represent the similarity between images for identification tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning task focused on learning a distance metric that minimizes intra-class distances and maximizes inter-class distances.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that learns a distance metric to embed similar data points closer together in a vector space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that learns an embedding space where semantically similar objects are placed close together and dissimilar objects are placed far apart.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning technique that learns a distance metric to embed data points in a space where similar items are closer together.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology for learning a distance function in a latent space to measure the similarity between pairs of objects.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology for learning discriminative embeddings that pull samples toward the dense regions of class clusters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that automatically extracts features to learn a non-linear transformation from input space to a semantically embedding space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that learns a distance function in a latent embedding space to capture similarities between images and labels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that learns a distance function to improve the classification of imbalanced fault data through quadruplet loss.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that learns a distance function to map data into a Euclidean space where similar samples are clustered together.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that learns a distance function to map different modalities into a joint space for tasks like zero-shot classification.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that learns a distance metric to embed data into a space where similar items are close and dissimilar items are far apart.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that learns embedding spaces where similar samples are positioned closer together than dissimilar ones.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that learns meta-features over datasets to measure similarity via Euclidean distance for warm-starting Bayesian hyperparameter optimization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network approach that learns a distance function to better separate anomalies from normal data in high-dimensional spaces.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation learning method that optimizes a distance metric to ensure similar samples are clustered closely in an embedding space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation learning task that optimizes a distance function to group similar instances and separate dissimilar ones.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation learning technique that optimizes the distance between data points to enhance retrieval accuracy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique for learning a distance function in a high-dimensional space to measure similarity between data points.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique for learning a distance metric that allows similar items to be closer together in an embedding space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that integrates deep learning with metric learning to enhance intra-class compactness and inter-class separability.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that learns a distance function to map data into an embedding space where similar items are closer together.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that learns an embedding space where similar items are closer together and dissimilar items are further apart.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that learns an embedding space where the distance between points reflects their actual semantic similarity.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that uses deep neural architectures to learn a distance metric that separates similar and dissimilar samples in an embedding space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that uses neural networks to learn an embedding space where distances reflect semantic similarity between instances.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique used to learn an embedding function that captures semantic differences within a dataset.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to learning a distance function that embeds data into a space where similar objects are close together.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#metric_learning_specializations"/>
