  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#mutual_information">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mutual Information</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another random variable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another, often approximated in high-dimensional spaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another, used here as an objective function for fitting deep nonlinear models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another, used here for feature selection in ransomware detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another, used to estimate theoretical performance limits.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through observing another random variable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information shared between two random variables to quantify their dependence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information shared between two random variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information that one random variable contains about another.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure of the mutual dependence between two variables used here to dynamically adjust the learning rate in deep neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A quantitative measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical measure that quantifies the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical measure that quantifies the stochastic dependence between discrete random variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical measure used to quantify the amount of information leakage from gradients in federated learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical measure used to quantify the amount of information shared between successive layers of a deep neural network to accelerate training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An information-theoretic measure that quantifies how much information is shared between two random variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An information-theoretic measure that quantifies the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An information-theoretic measure that quantifies the amount of information shared between two random variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An information-theoretic measure used for feature selection to quantify the dependency between input variables and model output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[estimate theoretical performance limits] estimate theoretical performance limits</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[quantify the amount of information leakage from gradients in federated learning] quantify the amount of information leakage from gradients in federated learning</rdfs:comment>
