    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another, used here for feature selection in ransomware detection.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another, used to estimate theoretical performance limits.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A measure of the amount of information obtained about one random variable through another.</skos:definition>
