  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#graph_signal_processing">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Graph Signal Processing</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of analysis that applies signal processing techniques to data defined on the vertices of a graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field that extends signal processing techniques to data defined on irregular graph structures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for analyzing and manipulating data defined on irregular graph structures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for analyzing and manipulating data defined on the vertices or edges of a network structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for analyzing and manipulating signals defined on the vertices of a graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for analyzing and processing signals defined on the vertices of a graph using adaptive estimation strategies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for analyzing signals defined on graphs to improve the representation and regularization of deep learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for analyzing signals defined on the vertices of a graph using spectral or spatial filters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for building graph-based models from classes of filtered signals by formulating modeling as a system identification problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that analyzes signals defined on the nodes of a graph to extract frequency-based features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that extends digital signal processing to data defined on graphs, utilizing spectral transforms to analyze structural information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that extends digital signal processing to data defined on irregular domains represented by graphs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that generalizes digital signal processing techniques to data residing on the vertices of a graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that generalizes digital signal processing tools to data defined on irregular graph structures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that leverages data structure priors represented as graphs to improve classification in small-sample settings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for analyzing signals defined on the vertices of a graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that uses graph theory to analyze and process signals defined on the vertices of a graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing framework that extracts features from spatiotemporal signals by mapping them onto graph vertices and edges.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing framework that leverages graph-based representations to analyze spatial dependencies in data.</rdfs:comment>
