  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#domain_randomization">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Domain Randomization</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation strategy that generates synthetic training data by randomly varying simulation parameters to improve model generalization to real-world environments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data augmentation technique that varies environment parameters to improve the generalization of agents to unseen settings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning technique that varies environment parameters during training to improve the agent's ability to generalize to new settings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sim-to-real transfer strategy that exposes a model to a wide variety of simulated environments to improve robustness in the real world.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for creating synthetic training datasets to improve the generalization of models across different environmental scenarios.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for learning robust policies by training an agent in environments with randomized dynamics to ensure successful transfer to a target system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for sim-to-real transfer that involves training an agent in simulations with randomized parameters to overcome the reality gap.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for sim-to-real transfer that involves varying simulation parameters to create policies robust to real-world environment variations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for training policies in simulation with varied environments to enable direct deployment on real-world robots.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique in simulation-to-real transfer that involves varying environment parameters to make a model robust to real-world discrepancies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique in simulation-to-real transfer that involves varying the environment's properties to make a trained policy robust to real-world variations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique in simulation-to-real transfer that varies environment parameters to make a model more robust.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that applies models trained on simulated objects to real-world objects to reduce the need for large annotated datasets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that artificially varies simulation parameters to improve the generalization of a model to real-world data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that augments synthetic data with random transformations to improve the transfer of policies from simulation to reality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that bridges the gap between simulation and reality by introducing variability in the training environment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that exposes a learning agent to a wide variety of simulated environments to bridge the gap between simulation and reality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that exposes a model to varied simulated environments to increase its generalization to the real world.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that generates diverse synthetic training data to improve the transfer of a model from simulation to reality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that synthesizes training data with varied environmental parameters to bridge the gap between simulated and real-world environments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that varies simulation parameters during training to increase the robustness of a policy when transferred to real environments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that varies simulation parameters during training to reduce the gap between simulated and real-world robot behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that varies simulation parameters to increase the robustness of policies transferred to the real world.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that varies synthetic environment parameters to improve the generalization of models to real-world data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that varies the distribution of training data through image manipulations to make models more robust against catastrophic forgetting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in reinforcement learning to enforce policy generalization by training agents in varied simulated environments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A training strategy that exposes a model to a wide variety of simulated environments to improve its transferability to the real world.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A training strategy that varies the properties of synthetic data to make a model robust to variations in real-world environments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A training technique that exposes a policy to a distribution of simulated environments to improve generalization to the real world.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A training technique that randomizes simulator rendering to enable models trained on simulated images to transfer to the real world.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[models trained on simulated objects] models trained on simulated objects</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[environment parameters] environment parameters</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[model to simulated environments, learning agent/model to varied simulated environments] model to simulated environments</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[agent in randomized environments] agent in randomized environments</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[variability in the training environment] variability in the training environment</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A data augmentation strategy that generates synthetic training data by randomly varying simulation parameters to improve model generalization to real-world environments.</skos:definition>
