    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A bijective mapping between two distributions used to perform high-dimensional numerical integration and sampling.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of generative models for continuous random variables that uses a series of invertible transformations to model complex distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of generative models that approximates probability distributions using a sequence of invertible transformations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of invertible neural networks used to map a simple distribution to a complex target distribution for efficient sampling.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of unsupervised learning algorithms based on maximum likelihood optimization with change of variables to learn complex data representations.</skos:definition>
