    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent learns optimal behavior directly from experience without constructing an explicit model of the environment's transitions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent learns to make decisions by interacting with an environment without building an internal model of the environment's dynamics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where an agent learns to make decisions through trial and error without requiring a model of the environment's dynamics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that learns an optimal policy through direct interaction with an environment without requiring a transition model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that learns optimal control policies for robotic tasks through direct interaction with the environment without a prior model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that learns optimal policies directly from environment interactions without using a model of the system dynamics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach that learns an optimal policy without requiring a model of the environment's dynamics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach that learns optimal policies or value functions without explicitly modeling the environment's transition dynamics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning strategy that learns optimal policies directly from experience without building a model of the environment's dynamics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An agent learning strategy that optimizes policies through trial-and-error without utilizing a predefined model of the environment.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An agent-based learning method that optimizes behavior through trial and error without relying on a predefined model of the environment.</skos:definition>
