    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An agent-learning strategy that optimizes policies without building an explicit internal model of the environment's dynamics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithm that learns an optimal control policy through interaction with an environment without requiring a model of the environment's dynamics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic approach to decision making that learns optimal policies without explicitly estimating the transition dynamics of the environment.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to agent training that learns planning characteristics using standard neural network components without an explicit environment model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to learning optimal control policies through interaction with an environment without requiring an explicit model of the system dynamics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach to learning optimal policies in Markov Decision Processes without explicitly modeling the environment's transitions.</skos:definition>
