  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#particle_filter">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Particle Filter</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A nonlinear estimation method that computes weighted averages of sampled trajectories from a distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A recursive Bayesian estimation technique that represents a probability distribution using a set of weighted samples to track targets in video.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A recursive Bayesian estimation technique that represents probability distributions using a set of weighted samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential Monte Carlo method that estimates the state of a system by sampling particles to represent probability distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential Monte Carlo method that uses a set of particles to represent the posterior distribution of a system's state.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential Monte Carlo method used for estimating the state of a dynamic system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential Monte Carlo method used for estimating the state of a nonlinear dynamic system from noisy observations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential Monte Carlo method used for performing Bayesian inference in non-linear state-space models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential Monte Carlo method used to combine sequence models of symbolic music with user-defined constraints in continuous time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential Monte Carlo method used to estimate the internal state of a dynamical system from noisy observations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential Monte Carlo method used to estimate the internal states of a dynamic system as it evolves over time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential Monte Carlo method used to estimate the state of a dynamic system from noisy observations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential Monte Carlo method used to estimate the state of a system by representing the probability distribution as a set of particles.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A state-space model implementation used to jointly track speaker movements and perform speaker diarisation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a set of weighted samples] set of weighted samples</rdfs:comment>
