  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#survival_analysis">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Survival Analysis</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A branch of statistics for analyzing the expected duration of time until one or more events happen, specifically handling censored data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A branch of statistics for analyzing the expected duration of time until one or more events happen.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised ranking task that predicts the time until an event occurs, often dealing with right-censored data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical approach used to map dynamic user activities to monotonically decreasing survival probabilities for early fraud detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical approach used to predict the time until a specific event occurs, often dealing with censored data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical approach used to predict the time until an event occurs and the probability of its occurrence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical framework that predicts the time until an event occurs using deep learning and piecewise exponential models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical framework used to predict the time until a specific event occurs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method for analyzing the expected duration of time until one or more events happen.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to analyze the expected duration of time until one or more events happen, such as user churn.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to analyze the expected duration of time until one or more events happen.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to analyze the expected duration of time until one or more events occur.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to evaluate survival distribution predictions through measures of discrimination and risk reduction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to model the time until a specific event occurs while handling censored data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to model the time until a specific event occurs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to model the time until a specific event of interest occurs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to model the time until an event of interest occurs, applied here to research reproducibility.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to predict the time until a specific event occurs, often applied to medical readmission risks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to predict the time until a specific event occurs, such as the discontinuation of an ad.</rdfs:comment>
