  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#contrastive_self_supervised_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Contrastive Self-Supervised Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that maximizes mutual information between different views of the same data instance to learn robust representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning method that learns representations by maximizing similarity between positive pairs and minimizing it between negative pairs without explicit labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning method that trains a model to recognize similar pairs of data representations without requiring explicit labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that extracts useful features from unlabeled data by maximizing agreement between different augmented views of the same sample.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that trains a model to distinguish between similar and dissimilar pairs of data without explicit labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that trains a model to recognize similar data points without requiring human-labeled targets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that trains an encoder to distinguish between similar and dissimilar augmented versions of the same data point without labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that trains models to distinguish between similar and dissimilar data pairs without requiring manual labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that trains models to distinguish between similar and dissimilar pairs of data without human labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses data augmentation to pretrain graph encoders on unlabeled data to alleviate overfitting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses unlabeled data and exemplars to learn representations that facilitate few-shot class incremental learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that utilizes unlabeled data by maximizing the alignment of positive samples and the divergence of class centers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning strategy that trains a model to maximize similarity between positive pairs and minimize it for negative pairs without explicit labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A pre-training approach that learns representations by contrasting similar and dissimilar unlabeled samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A pre-training strategy that learns useful features from unlabeled data by maximizing similarity between augmented views.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A representation learning approach that solves a pretext task by comparing anchor, negative, and positive features from unlabeled data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A representation learning method that trains a model to distinguish between different views of the same data point and different data points.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A representation learning strategy that learns to distinguish between similar and dissimilar data pairs without labels.</rdfs:comment>
