    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that replaces computationally expensive code regions with trained models to improve execution speed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique using deep learning models to approximate complex matrix elements in high-multiplicity scattering simulations to reduce computation time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique where deep models are used to emulate complex mathematical functions or matrix elements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The study of the ability of artificial neurons to represent complex mathematical functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The theoretical study of the ability of neural architectures to represent functions from specific mathematical spaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The theoretical study of the capacity of artificial neurons to represent a target probability distribution or function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The theoretical study of the rate at which a neural network can represent a target function given specific activation functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The use of a deep learning model to numerically estimate complex mathematical functions or metrics, such as Ricci flat metrics.</rdfs:comment>
