    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble learning algorithm where the evolution of data point weights reveals the difficulty of classification for specific samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble learning method that combines multiple weak classification rules into a single strong rule.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble learning method that combines multiple weak classifiers to create a strong classifier by focusing on previously misclassified instances.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble learning method that combines multiple weak classifiers to create a strong classifier using adaptive boosting.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble learning method that combines multiple weak learners to create a strong classifier.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble learning method that iteratively combines multiple weak classifiers to create a single strong classifier.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble learning method that iteratively trains weak learners and weights them to create a strong classifier.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An iterative ensemble technique that combines multiple weak learners to create a strong classifier.</skos:definition>
