    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A decision-making system that partitions a problem space into sub-problems solved by specialized individual learners.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A divide-and-conquer architecture where several specialized sub-models are combined by a gating network to handle different parts of the input space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that models complex data by combining multiple specialized learning modules under a gating network.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning architecture that combines multiple specialized models to handle complex or imbalanced data distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning framework that employs a gate network to assign input examples to specialized expert models for improved ranking performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that combines the outputs of several learning algorithms to improve overall performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning architecture that combines multiple specialized models to capture different patterns in the data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning architecture that combines multiple specialized models to handle different subsets of a dataset.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning architecture that combines multiple specialized models to handle time-varying statistical scenarios in decentralized cooperation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning architecture that combines multiple specialized models to perform a task by weighting their outputs based on the input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning architecture that combines multiple specialized models to track system parameters across different time-scales.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning architecture that combines multiple specialized models under a gating network to perform a task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning architecture that combines multiple specialized models, known as experts, through a gating mechanism to handle different input partitions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning architecture that combines several specialized models to perform a task by weighting their contributions based on the input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning architecture that combines several specialized sub-models, known as experts, via a gating network to handle different parts of the input space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning architecture that uses a gating network to assign inputs to specialized sub-networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning framework that employs multiple specialized models to handle diverse input distortions or tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model composed of a classifier and several regressors used to handle discontinuities in parameter-solution mappings.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model that combines multiple local experts through a routing mechanism to handle complex data distributions in regression tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that activates only a sparse subset of specialized subnetworks for any given input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that assigns a specific task to different specialized models based on the current context.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that combines multiple specialized learners through a gating network to improve modeling flexibility.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that combines multiple specialized learners to model complex data distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that combines multiple specialized learners to perform a complex task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that combines multiple specialized models to perform complex prediction tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that combines multiple specialized sub-models to approximate complex functions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that combines multiple specialized sub-models to handle diverse input contexts.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that combines multiple specialized sub-models via a gating mechanism to perform a task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that combines multiple specialized sub-networks to handle different parts of the input space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that combines several specialized models through a gating network to make a final prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture that combines several specialized networks through a gating mechanism.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular architecture where a gating network determines which specialist model is best suited for a given input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular framework that pools together multiple specialized networks to improve collective capacity and computational efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modular neural network architecture that assigns different inputs to specialized sub-networks via a gating mechanism.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that combines multiple specialized models via a gating mechanism to handle diverse data patterns.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that consists of multiple specialized sub-networks and a gating mechanism to assign inputs to the most relevant expert.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that scales parameter size independently from computational demand by activating only a subset of the network.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sparse neural network architecture that activates only a subset of its parameters for each input to improve scaling efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sparse neural network architecture that activates only a subset of specialized sub-networks for each input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sparse neural network architecture where only a subset of parameters is activated for each input, improving scalability.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sparsely activated deep learning architecture that scales model size with sublinear compute costs by using a set of specialized subnetworks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sparsely-activated model architecture that selects different parameters for each incoming example to reduce computational cost.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical framework for modeling heterogeneity in data for regression, classification, and clustering.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical model that combines multiple specialized learners to handle heterogeneous data in regression or classification tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical model that combines multiple specialized sub-models to handle heterogeneous data distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble architecture that combines multiple specialized networks via a gating mechanism to improve accuracy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble architecture that combines multiple specialized neural networks using a gating mechanism to handle diverse inputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble architecture that groups similar clients to personalize federated learning in heterogeneous data settings.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble architecture where a gating network assigns input data to specialized local classifiers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble architecture where multiple specialized models are combined via a gating mechanism to handle diverse data domains.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble learning architecture that combines multiple specialized sub-networks to improve overall performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble learning architecture where different specialized networks learn distinct sets of features to improve overall prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ensemble learning technique that trains multiple specialized sub-networks and a gating mechanism to determine which expert to use for a given input.</skos:definition>
