  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#adversarial_attack">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Adversarial Attack</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious attempt to deceive a machine learning model by providing specifically crafted adversarial inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious attempt to manipulate a machine learning model's output by providing carefully crafted input perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious attempt to mislead a machine learning model by introducing deliberately altered training or input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious influence designed to compromise the integrity or efficiency of a deep neural network during training or inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious input designed to deceive a deep learning model into making incorrect predictions or decisions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious input designed to deceive a machine learning model into making an incorrect prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious input perturbation designed to deceive a machine learning model into making an incorrect prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious manipulation of input measurements to mislead a machine learning model into producing incorrect state estimations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious manipulation of model weights or inputs intended to cause a catastrophic failure in prediction accuracy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious methodology that introduces imperceptible perturbations to input data to manipulate the output of a recommender system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious perturbation of a model's input or output designed to induce incorrect behavior in a machine learning controller.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious perturbation of input data designed to deceive a machine learning model into making incorrect predictions or estimations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious technique that introduces perturbations to input data to deceive a machine learning model into making incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A malicious technique that modifies input data to deceive a machine learning model into making incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A manipulation technique that employs maliciously crafted inputs or poisoned models to deceive deep neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method designed to evaluate the robustness of graph-based detection systems by introducing malicious perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for finding input perturbations that cause image classifiers to misclassify by searching over the latent space of a spanner network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of constructing input perturbations to force a machine learning classifier into making a misclassification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of crafting carefully designed perturbations to deceive a machine learning classifier into making an incorrect prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of crafting malicious inputs for discrete and structured code data to test the robustness of neural models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of crafting perturbed inputs to deceive a machine learning model into making incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of crafting small perturbations to input data to reduce the classification performance of deep learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of crafting small, intentional perturbations to input data to deceive a machine learning model into making incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of creating inconspicuous audio signals that fool automatic speech recognition systems using room impulse responses.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of creating modified input samples to evaluate the robustness of machine learning models against unforeseen perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of creating perturbed inputs designed to deceive a machine learning model into making an incorrect prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of creating small, intentional perturbations to input data to deceive a machine learning model into making an error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of deliberately modifying inputs to produce a desired, often incorrect, response from a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of exploiting the geometry of high-dimensional data to induce misclassification in a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
