    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Adversarial_Attacks</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious attempt to deceive a machine learning model by providing specifically crafted adversarial inputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious attempt to manipulate a machine learning model's output by providing carefully crafted input perturbations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious attempt to mislead a machine learning model by introducing deliberately altered training or input data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious influence designed to compromise the integrity or efficiency of a deep neural network during training or inference.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious input designed to deceive a deep learning model into making incorrect predictions or decisions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious input designed to deceive a machine learning model into making an incorrect prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious input perturbation designed to deceive a machine learning model into making an incorrect prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious manipulation of input measurements to mislead a machine learning model into producing incorrect state estimations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious manipulation of model weights or inputs intended to cause a catastrophic failure in prediction accuracy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious methodology that introduces imperceptible perturbations to input data to manipulate the output of a recommender system.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious perturbation of a model's input or output designed to induce incorrect behavior in a machine learning controller.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious perturbation of input data designed to deceive a machine learning model into making incorrect predictions or estimations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious technique that introduces perturbations to input data to deceive a machine learning model into making incorrect predictions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A malicious technique that modifies input data to deceive a machine learning model into making incorrect predictions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A manipulation technique that employs maliciously crafted inputs or poisoned models to deceive deep neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method designed to evaluate the robustness of graph-based detection systems by introducing malicious perturbations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method for finding input perturbations that cause image classifiers to misclassify by searching over the latent space of a spanner network.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of constructing input perturbations to force a machine learning classifier into making a misclassification.</skos:definition>
