  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#kalman_filter">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Kalman Filter</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A recursive algorithm that estimates unknown parameters from a series of noisy measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A recursive estimator that predicts the state of a linear dynamic system from a series of noisy measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A recursive estimator that provides an efficient way to track the state of a linear system over time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A recursive estimator used as a modifier for neural networks to maintain performance in non-stationary environments by adapting to data drifts.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A recursive filter that estimates the state of a linear dynamic system from a series of noisy measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A recursive mathematical algorithm used to estimate the state of a non-stationary primary user to detect emulation attacks in cognitive radio networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A state-space model that estimates the evolution of a time-varying system using a series of noisy measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithm that uses a series of measurements observed over time to produce an optimal estimate of unknown variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithm that uses a series of measurements observed over time to produce estimates of unknown variables in a linear dynamical system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithm that uses a series of measurements observed over time to produce estimates of unknown variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithm used in conjunction with a deep neural network to estimate student concentration levels from body movement data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithmic process that uses a series of measurements observed over time to produce estimates of unknown variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative algorithm that estimates the state of a linear dynamic system from a series of noisy measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative mathematical algorithm that estimates the internal state or parameters of a dynamical system from noisy measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative mathematical algorithm used to estimate the state of a dynamic system from a series of noisy measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative mathematical process that uses a series of measurements observed over time to produce estimates of unknown variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimal estimation algorithm that predicts the state of a linear system by combining noisy measurements with a mathematical model.</rdfs:comment>
