  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#metalearning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Metalearning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns how to learn by optimizing the selection of algorithms across different tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework where a model is trained to adapt quickly to new tasks with very few training examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm designed to improve the ability of a model to adapt to new tasks rapidly using very few examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that aims to design models that can adapt to new tasks quickly using a small amount of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that aims to improve the ability of a model to learn new tasks from a very small number of training examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that aims to improve the performance of a model by leveraging knowledge gained from previous learning tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that enables a model to adapt quickly to new tasks or data distributions by learning how to learn.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that enables a model to adapt to new tasks quickly by learning from a distribution of tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that extracts high-level rules or knowledge about the learning process itself to improve model performance or interpretability.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that leverages experience from multiple tasks to improve the performance of algorithms on new tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that leverages information from auxiliary tasks to improve the sample complexity of a new task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that optimizes a model's ability to adapt rapidly to new tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses a two-stage algorithm to handle user cold start problems in recommendation systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model is trained on a variety of tasks to develop a general strategy for quickly adapting to new tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model is trained to adapt quickly to new tasks by leveraging experience from previous ones.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model is trained to improve its own learning process based on a set of tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model is trained to learn how to learn, enabling fast adaptation to new tasks or subjects with minimal data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm where a model learns how to learn by optimizing for fast adaptation to new tasks or scenarios.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that aims to learn how to learn by leveraging knowledge from previous tasks to improve performance on new tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns how to learn by optimizing the learning process across multiple tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns how to learn by optimizing the process of adapting to new tasks with minimal data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns how to learn, enabling a model to adapt quickly to new tasks with minimal data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to design models capable of adapting to new tasks rapidly with minimal training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to design models capable of adapting to new tasks with very few examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to design models capable of learning how to learn from a few examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to design models capable of learning new tasks rapidly by leveraging experience from previous tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to generalize knowledge from previous tasks to improve performance on new, unseen tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to learn the general process of learning from a set of tasks to improve performance on new tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that improves data efficiency by generalizing learned concepts from a set of training tasks to new, related tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that learns how to optimize the learning process itself, such as by learning instance-specific weights for combining multiple losses.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning technique that learns how to learn by utilizing knowledge from previous tasks to optimize new ones.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A paradigm where a model learns how to learn by extracting general knowledge across multiple tasks to adapt quickly to new ones.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach that focuses on learning how to learn by leveraging prior knowledge across tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that enables a model to learn how to learn by optimizing for fast adaptation to new tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique where a model learns how to learn, allowing it to adapt to new tasks or data with very few training samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithmic framework that learns how to learn by extracting common knowledge across multiple related tasks to improve new task adaptation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An approach that learns how to learn by optimizing for fast adaptation to new tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An approach to machine learning where a model learns how to learn by optimizing the selection or combination of other learning algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
