  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#one_class_classifier">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">One Class Classifier</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A classification model that is trained using samples from only a single target class.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning algorithm trained on a single class to identify anomalies by detecting samples that deviate from the known distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning model that learns a decision boundary around a single class to identify atypical samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning model that learns to identify a single class of interest by treating all other data as outliers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained on a single class of data to identify anomalies or outliers that do not belong to that class.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained on a single class of data to identify whether new samples belong to that class or are outliers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained on a single class to detect outliers or novelties in data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained on a single class to identify anomalies as data points that do not belong to that class.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained on a single class to identify rare species or anomalies in imbalanced datasets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained to distinguish a target class from all other possible observations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained to identify a single class by recognizing patterns that deviate from a defined norm.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A novelty detection model trained on a single class to identify outliers or anomalies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised algorithm used for anomaly detection by estimating the target class density function through a reference distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning model trained on a single class to detect abnormal system conditions or anomalies.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning algorithm that identifies a target distribution by minimizing scatter along an optimal projection direction in a Hilbert space.</rdfs:comment>
