    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A classification model that is trained using samples from only a single target class.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning algorithm trained on a single class to identify anomalies by detecting samples that deviate from the known distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning model that learns a decision boundary around a single class to identify atypical samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning model that learns to identify a single class of interest by treating all other data as outliers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained on a single class of data to identify anomalies or outliers that do not belong to that class.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained on a single class of data to identify whether new samples belong to that class or are outliers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained on a single class to detect outliers or novelties in data.</skos:definition>
