    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained on a single class to identify rare species or anomalies in imbalanced datasets.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained to distinguish a target class from all other possible observations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning model trained to identify a single class by recognizing patterns that deviate from a defined norm.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A novelty detection model trained on a single class to identify outliers or anomalies.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised algorithm used for anomaly detection by estimating the target class density function through a reference distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning model trained on a single class to detect abnormal system conditions or anomalies.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning algorithm that identifies a target distribution by minimizing scatter along an optimal projection direction in a Hilbert space.</skos:definition>
