  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#hierarchical_classification">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hierarchical Classification</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A categorization process that organizes classes into a tree structure to predict the most specific leaf node.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A categorization process that organizes classes into a tree-like structure based on semantic similarity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A categorization task where classes are organized in a tree-like structure rather than a flat list.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A categorization task where objects are sorted into a nested structure of categories from general to specific.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A classification approach that organizes labels into a taxonomic structure to represent domain knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A classification approach that organizes overlapping classes into hierarchies to improve performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A classification strategy that organizes categories into a tree-like structure to reflect taxonomic relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A classification task that leverages the structured relationship between class labels to improve categorization efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning task that concurrently predicts a category and its conceptual superclasses in a structured order.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that organizes classes into a taxonomy to perform coarse-to-fine predictions for many-class few-shot problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that organizes classes into a tree-like structure to improve the classification of imbalanced datasets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning method that integrates taxonomic information to learn embeddings representative of hierarchical relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that computes label posteriors within a bottom-up inference framework to categorize data into a nested structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multi-class classification method that utilizes a structured hierarchy of classes to improve prediction performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multi-stage sorting process that groups similar classes together before refining them into specific categories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multiclass classification approach that organizes categories into a binary tree structure to decompose the problem into binary decisions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning approach that categorizes data into a nested set of classes to determine the actionability and applicability of regulatory announcements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning approach that organizes classes into a tree structure to simplify multi-class prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning approach that organizes classes into a tree-like structure to handle labels of varying levels of precision.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning approach that organizes classes into a tree-like structure to provide granular comprehension at different levels of a clinical hierarchy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning approach that organizes labels into a tree-like structure to improve classification accuracy by exploiting label relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning approach that organizes labels into a tree-like structure to predict categories at varying levels of abstraction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning approach that organizes target classes into a tree-like structure to refine prediction accuracy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that assigns data instances to categories organized in a tree-like structure of increasing specificity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that assigns instances to categories organized in a tree-like structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that organizes categories into a tree-like structure to classify documents into increasingly specific levels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that organizes classes into a tree-like structure to leverage parent-child relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that organizes labels into a tree-like structure to predict categories across multiple levels of granularity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that predicts a label from a taxonomy where classes are organized in a tree or directed acyclic graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task where class labels are organized in a tree-like structure and predictions are made across levels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task where labels are organized in a tree-like structure of categories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A task of assigning items to a structured taxonomy of classes while accounting for the parent-child relations between them.</rdfs:comment>
