  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#vertical_federated_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Vertical Federated Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative learning approach that trains models from cross-silo data with different feature spaces stored on different platforms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative learning framework where different parties hold different features for the same set of samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative learning framework where parties share different features of the same samples without exposing raw data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative learning paradigm where different organizations train a model on datasets that share the same samples but have different feature sets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative learning paradigm where participants share different features for the same set of users.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative learning paradigm where participants train models on data distributed across different sources without centralizing it.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative learning setup where different participants hold different features for the same set of samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative machine learning approach where parties build a shared model using distributed features of the same samples without exposing raw data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative machine learning framework that trains models on vertically partitioned data while preserving privacy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative training approach where multiple parties contribute different feature sets for the same set of samples while maintaining privacy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collaborative training paradigm where parties share different features for the same set of samples while keeping data private.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decentralized learning paradigm where collaborating organizations share the same users but possess disjoint feature sets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decentralized training framework where multiple agencies jointly train a model on complementary features of the same data subjects.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning approach where different parties hold different features for the same set of samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning approach where multiple parties collaborate to train a model on datasets with different features but overlapping samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning approach where participants collaborate on a shared set of samples but contribute different feature sets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning approach where participants share the same sample IDs but possess different feature sets for those samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning architecture where clients collaborate to train a model using vertically partitioned data with distinct attributes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning framework where participants with different feature sets for the same samples collaborate without sharing raw data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning framework where parties with different features of the same data entities train a joint model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning mechanism where different parties hold different features for the same set of data samples and train a model without sharing raw data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm for training models on datasets that share the same samples but possess different feature spaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm that trains a model on features partitioned across different parties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm that trains models across parties holding different features for the same set of instances.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where clients with different features for the same samples collaborate to train a predictor without sharing raw data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where different agents hold different features for the same set of data samples</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where different data sources share the same sample IDs but possess different feature spaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where different parties collaborate to train a model on datasets that share the same samples but have different feature sets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where different parties hold different feature sets for the same set of sample IDs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where different parties hold different features and labels for the same set of samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where different parties hold different features for the same set of samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where features of the same data samples are split across different participants.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where multiple parties collaborate on different feature sets for the same set of samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where parties collaborate on a model using different feature sets for the same sample IDs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning paradigm where parties share the same sample IDs but possess disjoint subsets of features for those samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed machine learning approach where data features are partitioned across different owners while maintaining data privacy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed machine learning approach where different parties hold different feature sets for the same set of users.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed machine learning approach where participants share features of the same data samples across different organizations to train a model without sharing raw data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy-preserving collaboration where parties hold different features for the same set of samples and train a shared model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy-preserving machine learning paradigm that trains models on datasets split by features across different parties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A privacy-preserving machine learning paradigm where participants share the same sample IDs but possess different feature spaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A secure learning paradigm that enables joint training on complementary user attributes owned by different agencies without sharing raw data.</rdfs:comment>
