  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#feedforwardneuralnetwork">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Feedforwardneuralnetwork</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic architectural form of artificial neural network where connections do not form a cycle.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic architecture that maps input signals to output signals through layers of interconnected neurons.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic architecture where information moves in one direction from input nodes through hidden layers to output nodes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network architecture where connections do not form cycles and information moves in one direction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, allowing information to flow in one direction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, moving information only in one direction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network where connections do not form a cycle.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network where connections do not form cycles, used here for image classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic neural network architecture where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, used here to study function approximation limits.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic neural network architecture where information moves in one direction from input to output layers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A basic neural network architecture where information moves in one direction from input to output without cycles.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational architecture with one or more hidden layers capable of approximating any continuous function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational model that approximates a function by mapping input data to output through layers of neurons without cycles.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational model that provides a piecewise constant approximation for multivariate functions using explicitly defined weights and thresholds.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model used to guide symbolic rewriting processes by learning patterns from algebraic reasoning examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A layered architecture where information moves in one direction from input to output without cycles.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multilayered architecture of artificial neurons where connections do not form a cycle.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression model used to approximate vertex centrality measures in large-scale complex networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, allowing information to move in one direction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, used here for sentiment prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, used here to approximate solutions to differential equations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, used here to approximate stabilizing feedback laws.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, used here to study approximation power.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between the nodes do not form a cycle, used here for binary classification of data distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections do not form a cycle, moving information in one direction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, propagating information in one direction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, typically used for classification or regression tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle.</rdfs:comment>
