    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic architectural form of artificial neural network where connections do not form a cycle.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic architecture that maps input signals to output signals through layers of interconnected neurons.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic architecture where information moves in one direction from input nodes through hidden layers to output nodes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network architecture where connections do not form cycles and information moves in one direction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, allowing information to flow in one direction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, moving information only in one direction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network where connections do not form a cycle.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic artificial neural network where connections do not form cycles, used here for image classification.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic neural network architecture where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, used here to study function approximation limits.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic neural network architecture where information moves in one direction from input to output layers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A basic neural network architecture where information moves in one direction from input to output without cycles.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A computational architecture with one or more hidden layers capable of approximating any continuous function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A computational model that approximates a function by mapping input data to output through layers of neurons without cycles.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A computational model that provides a piecewise constant approximation for multivariate functions using explicitly defined weights and thresholds.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning model used to guide symbolic rewriting processes by learning patterns from algebraic reasoning examples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A layered architecture where information moves in one direction from input to output without cycles.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A multilayered architecture of artificial neurons where connections do not form a cycle.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regression model used to approximate vertex centrality measures in large-scale complex networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, allowing information to move in one direction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, used here for sentiment prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, used here to approximate solutions to differential equations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, used here to approximate stabilizing feedback laws.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, used here to study approximation power.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections between the nodes do not form a cycle, used here for binary classification of data distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where connections do not form a cycle, moving information in one direction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, propagating information in one direction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An artificial neural network where connections between nodes do not form a cycle, typically used for classification or regression tasks.</skos:definition>
