    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Graph Representation Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning framework that processes structured information using local and iterative approaches to model graph data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of machine learning focused on automatically encoding graph structures into low-dimensional embeddings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of machine learning focused on learning low-dimensional embeddings for nodes and edges in a graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of machine learning that aims to learn low-dimensional vector embeddings for nodes, edges, or entire graphs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for deriving deep node and edge embeddings from large attributed graphs to enable transfer learning tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that embeds vertices of a graph into a low-dimensional vector space using a minimax game between generative and discriminative models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that leverages graph topology to embed networks into compact vector spaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that transforms graph-structured data into low-dimensional vector representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task focused on transforming graph-structured data into low-dimensional vectors while preserving topological information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that maps nodes and edges of a graph into low-dimensional vectors while preserving the graph's topology.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning technique that generates low-dimensional embeddings for nodes in a network to compute similarity and identify brain states.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning technique used to transform graph-structured data into low-dimensional vectors for classification tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for encoding nodes of a graph into low-dimensional vectors for use in downstream machine learning tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for learning low-dimensional embeddings that capture the geometric dependencies between nodes in a graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of transforming graph-structured data into continuous vector embeddings while preserving topological information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method that encodes topological and temporal correlations of incidents into vectors for aggregation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method that maps data into a weighted graph with shortest path distances to eliminate Euclidean inductive bias.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for characterizing the structure of complex networks to perform tasks like node classification and link prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for embedding nodes in large graphs as low-dimensional vectors for downstream applications.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for encoding graph-structured data into continuous vector spaces for downstream tasks.</rdfs:comment>
