    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization framework that seeks to minimize the worst-case loss over a set of probability distributions to improve model generalization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization framework that seeks to minimize the worst-case loss over a set of probability distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization paradigm used in federated learning to mitigate the negative effects of data heterogeneity among clients.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization strategy that minimizes the worst-case expected loss over a set of possible probability distributions.</skos:definition>
