  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#adversarial_machine_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Adversarial Machine Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field focused on the study of models that are manipulated by malicious inputs to expose vulnerabilities or improve robustness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on attacking and defending machine learning models against malicious inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on attacks and defenses against machine learning models to ensure robustness and security.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on attacks that deceive machine learning models and the development of defenses to ensure their robustness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on attacks that exploit the inherent logical vulnerabilities of learning algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on attacks that manipulate machine learning models by providing deceptive input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on attacks that undermine the performance of machine learning algorithms through malicious inputs or poisoning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on characterizing attacks and developing defenses to make AI systems resilient against malicious inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on creating and defending against inputs designed to deceive machine learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on creating and defending against inputs designed to deceive or misguide machine learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on creating modified inputs that cause a model to make incorrect predictions to protect facial privacy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on creating perturbed inputs to test and improve the robustness of machine learning classifiers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on manipulating input data to deceive models and developing defenses against such attacks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on protecting automated systems against security threats using game-theoretic or Bayesian risk analysis frameworks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on techniques that attempt to fool models by providing deceptive input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the design of models that can resist malicious attempts to corrupt their functionality or bypass security measures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the interaction between a machine learner and an adversary who attempts to manipulate the model's output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the robustness of models against intentionally designed malicious inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the scenarios where machine learning systems are intentionally manipulated by synthesized input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the security of machine learning models against malicious attacks and defenses in wireless domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the security of machine learning models against malicious inputs or data tampering.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the security of machine learning systems against malicious attacks and threats.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the security of machine learning systems against maliciously crafted inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the security of models against malicious attempts to manipulate their output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the security vulnerabilities of models, specifically regarding attacks that use perturbed inputs to deceive them.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the use of deceptive inputs to trick models into making incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the use of machine learning to launch attacks or develop defenses against predictive models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerabilities of ML models to deceptive inputs and the development of defenses.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerabilities of ML models to intentionally crafted perturbations designed to cause misclassification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerabilities of ML models to malicious inputs and the development of defenses against them.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerabilities of ML models to malicious inputs designed to cause misclassification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerabilities of ML models to malicious inputs designed to deceive the system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerabilities of ML systems to malicious manipulations of input or training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerabilities of machine learning models to malicious inputs and the development of defenses.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerabilities of machine learning models to malicious inputs designed to cause failure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerabilities of models to maliciously crafted input perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerabilities of models to maliciously crafted inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerability of machine learning models to malicious perturbations designed to fool them.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerability of machine learning models to maliciously crafted inputs designed to cause incorrect outputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerability of machine learning models to maliciously crafted perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the vulnerability of models to maliciously crafted inputs designed to cause misclassification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on understanding and defending against input perturbations designed to deceive machine learning classifiers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focusing on security vulnerabilities in machine learning systems, including threats during training, inferencing, and hardware implementation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focusing on the vulnerabilities of ML models to deceptive inputs and the development of defenses against them.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focusing on the vulnerabilities of ML systems to malicious manipulations such as poisoning and model stealing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study that uses deceptive inputs to analyze and explain the internal decision-making process of neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A research field focused on the study of input perturbations that subvert model predictions and the design of countermeasures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security field focused on the study of perturbations to input data that cause machine learning models to misclassify.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security-focused field that generates perturbed inputs to deceive models while adhering to specific physical or system constraints.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that employs crafted perturbations to deceive a classifier into making incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that employs deceptive inputs to deceive or evade a predictive model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that generates deceptive inputs to fool classifiers and identify vulnerabilities in machine learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that studies how malicious inputs can deceive a model to better understand its decision boundaries and vulnerabilities.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to craft inputs, such as natural makeup, to evade identification by facial recognition models.</rdfs:comment>
