  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#wasserstein_barycenter">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Wasserstein Barycenter</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Bayesian predictive posterior based on optimal transport theory used as an alternative to maximum a posteriori estimators.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A centroid distribution that minimizes the sum of squared distances to cluster members under the Kantorovich-Wasserstein metric.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generalization of the mean for probability measures defined using the optimal transport distance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generalized mean of probability distributions based on optimal transport theory.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generalized mean of probability distributions computed using the optimal transport distance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A geometric average of probability distributions defined via the optimal transport distance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A geometric center of a set of probability distributions computed using the optimal transport distance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A geometric center of a set of probability distributions defined under the optimal transport metric.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A geometric construct that represents the average or central point among a set of probability distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A geometric mean in optimal transport space used to find a consensus between multiple probability distributions or models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A geometric mean in the space of probability distributions based on optimal transport.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A geometric mean of probability distributions computed using the optimal transport metric.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical mean of probability distributions based on optimal transport distances.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A measure that represents the optimal transport average between multiple input probability distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probability distribution aggregation method based on the theory of optimal transport.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probability distribution that represents the weighted average of a set of distributions using the optimal transport metric.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probability measure that represents the average of several probability distributions under the Wasserstein metric.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A representative probability distribution that minimizes the sum of Wasserstein distances to a set of given distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single probability distribution that summarizes a collection of input measures while respecting their underlying geometry via optimal transport.</rdfs:comment>
