    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative model used to infer 3D position and pose from sensor data by combining data-driven emulation with domain expertise.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative network that learns a latent representation of data conditioned on auxiliary information for scenario generation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A latent variable model that integrates representation vectors with a transformer-based architecture to enhance controllability in neural story generation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic generative model that learns a latent representation of data conditioned on auxiliary information.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic graphical model that learns latent representations by explicitly capturing characteristics associated with provided labels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A stochastic generative model that learns a latent representation of data conditioned on specific auxiliary information.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#generative_architectures"/>
    <ml:processesData rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#structured_prediction"/>
    <ml:transforms rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#latent_space"/>
    <ml:modifies rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#latent_space"/>
    <ml:modifies rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#variational_autoencoder"/>
    <ml:learnsFrom rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#latent_space"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#generalized_additive_model">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Generalized Additive Model</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of interpretable models used to recover reward functions in reinforcement learning settings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributional regression model where probability distribution parameters depend on predictors through smooth functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible class of interpretable models that extend linear models by summing smooth functions of predictors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression framework that models a response variable as a sum of smooth functions of predictors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression framework that models a response variable as a sum of smooth functions of the predictors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression framework that models the response as a sum of smooth functions of the predictor variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression framework that models the response as a sum of smooth functions of the predictors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression framework used to model the relationship between training sample size and model performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression model that allows for non-linear relationships between predictors and the response variable via smooth functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression model that captures non-linear relationships between variables using a sum of smooth functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression model that describes a response variable as a sum of smooth functions of the predictors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression model that describes the relationship between a dependent variable and covariates as a sum of smooth functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression model that describes the relationship between a dependent variable and predictors as a sum of smooth functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression model that describes the relationship between a target and predictors as a sum of smooth functions of each predictor.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression technique that describes a response variable as a sum of smooth functions of predictors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression technique that models a response variable as a sum of smooth functions of the predictors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A flexible regression technique that models the relationship between a dependent variable and predictors using smooth functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear model that allows for non-linear relationships between the independent variables and the dependent variable via smooth functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A nonparametric regression model that represents the target function as a sum of univariate functions of the explanatory variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression model that models predictors independently in a non-linear way to maintain full interpretability while capturing arbitrary patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression model that represents the target variable as a sum of separate shape functions for each input feature.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression or classification model that fits complex nonlinear functions as a sum of univariate functions to maintain interpretability.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A white-box model class that detects anomalies using a partial identification objective to handle noisy or heterogeneous features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An intrinsically interpretable model architecture that combines main effects and interaction effects for explainable recommendations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[recover reward functions in reinforcement learning settings] recover reward functions in reinforcement learning settings</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[model the relationship between training sample size and model performance] model the relationship between training sample size and model performance</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a sum of smooth functions, smooth functions] smooth functions</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a partial identification objective] partial identification objective</rdfs:comment>
