  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#sensitivity_analysis">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sensitivity Analysis</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A diagnostic procedure that examines how changes in input instances affect the output or parameters of a classification model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for determining how different values of an input parameter impact the output of a mathematical model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for generating visual explanations from neural networks by analyzing how changes in input affect the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for identifying which input variables most significantly influence the objective function and constraints of an optimization problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of determining how the uncertainty in the output of a model can be apportioned to different sources of uncertainty in its inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology used to determine how the uncertainty in the output of a model can be apportioned to different sources of uncertainty in its inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology used to determine how the variation in the output of a model can be attributed to different variations in its inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model interpretation technique that assesses the importance of input features by measuring the change in output relative to input perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to determine how the uncertainty in the output of a model can be apportioned to different sources of uncertainty in its inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A study of how the uncertainty in the output of a model can be apportioned to different sources of uncertainty in its inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to determine how the uncertainty in the output of a model can be apportioned to different sources of uncertainty in its inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to determine how the variation in the output of a model can be attributed to different variations of its input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explanatory method that investigates the effect of input perturbations on model predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[determine how the uncertainty in the output of a model can be apportioned to different sources of uncertainty in its inputs] determine how the uncertainty in the output of a model can be apportioned to different sources of uncertainty in its inputs</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[determine how the variation in the output of a model can be attributed to different variations in its inputs, determine how the variation in the output of a model can be attributed to different variations of its input features] determine how the variation in the output of a model can be attributed to different variations in its inputs</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[how input changes affect model output] how input changes affect model output</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[influential input variables] influential input variables</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[output uncertainty to input sources] output uncertainty to input sources</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A diagnostic procedure that examines how changes in input instances affect the output or parameters of a classification model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method for determining how different values of an input parameter impact the output of a mathematical model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method for generating visual explanations from neural networks by analyzing how changes in input affect the output.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method for identifying which input variables most significantly influence the objective function and constraints of an optimization problem.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of determining how the uncertainty in the output of a model can be apportioned to different sources of uncertainty in its inputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology used to determine how the uncertainty in the output of a model can be apportioned to different sources of uncertainty in its inputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology used to determine how the variation in the output of a model can be attributed to different variations in its inputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model interpretation technique that assesses the importance of input features by measuring the change in output relative to input perturbations.</skos:definition>
