  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#distributional_regression">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Distributional Regression</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that estimates cosmological parameters directly from the volumetric representation of matter distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning problem that involves mapping an input space to a space of probability distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning task that maps a probability distribution to a real-valued response.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning technique that maps probability measures to real-valued outputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression task that aims to map probability measures to real-valued responses over a reproducing kernel Hilbert space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression task that maps probability measures to real-valued responses.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression task where the input is a probability distribution or a bag of observations and the output is a single value.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression task where the input is a probability measure and the output is a vector-valued variable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression task where the response variable depends on a covariate that is itself a probability distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regression technique that estimates the entire conditional probability distribution of a target variable rather than a single point estimate.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to estimate target variables that are only available at the group level rather than for individual observations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to map the counterfactual distribution of a system's natural regime to the distribution of a disrupted system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical modeling technique that predicts the probability distribution of a target variable rather than a single point estimate.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical problem of predicting a distribution based on the input features of a distribution of distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task where labels are associated with groups of inputs rather than individual samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[estimate target variables that are only available at the group level rather than for individual observations] estimate target variables that are only available at the group level rather than for individual observations</rdfs:comment>
