    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning problem that involves mapping an input space to a space of probability distributions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning task that maps a probability distribution to a real-valued response.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning technique that maps probability measures to real-valued outputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regression task that aims to map probability measures to real-valued responses over a reproducing kernel Hilbert space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regression task that maps probability measures to real-valued responses.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regression task where the input is a probability distribution or a bag of observations and the output is a single value.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regression task where the input is a probability measure and the output is a vector-valued variable.</skos:definition>
