    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning setting where data arrives in a sequential stream and the model is updated incrementally to minimize regret.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning setting where data arrives in a sequential stream and the model is updated incrementally.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning setting where data arrives sequentially and the model is updated incrementally.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning setting where data arrives sequentially and the model is updated iteratively to minimize regret.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning setting where data arrives sequentially and the model must update its parameters and make predictions in real-time.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A meta-algorithm that allocates a data augmentation budget on the fly during neural network training.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of learning where data arrives in a sequential stream and the model is updated incrementally.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of machine learning in which data is processed sequentially, updating the model as new instances arrive.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of machine learning where data is processed in a sequential stream and the model is updated incrementally.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of machine learning where data is processed sequentially and the model is updated in real-time.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of model training where data arrives in a sequential stream and the learner updates its hypothesis on the fly.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method where a model is updated sequentially as new data points arrive in a real-time stream.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method where a model updates its parameters sequentially as new data points arrive in real-time.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that updates a model's parameters sequentially as new data arrives to improve prediction accuracy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology where a model is updated incrementally as data arrives in a sequential stream.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A paradigm for adaptively generating adversarial disturbances to maximize the cost incurred by a controller in real-time.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A paradigm for algorithms that maintain worst-case regret guarantees while adapting to stochastic environments.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A paradigm for designing adaptive and parameter-free algorithms through black-box reductions to simplify analysis and improve regret guarantees.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A paradigm where a model is updated incrementally as new data arrives in a sequential manner.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A paradigm where a model iteratively receives data, makes a decision, and updates its parameters based on immediate reward feedback.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A predictive approach that updates its model as time passes to handle concept drift in time-series data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A runtime approach to self-adaptive systems that accumulates knowledge through exploration to address design-time uncertainty.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequence-based decision-making approach for statistical arbitrage that does not require non-stationary stochastic process assumptions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequential data processing paradigm where the model updates its parameters immediately as each new data point arrives.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequential decision process where a learner updates its strategy based on partial loss feedback.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequential decision-making framework where a model updates its parameters as data arrives in a stream.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequential learning paradigm used to optimize bidding strategies in repeated auctions to minimize regret over time.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequential learning process where a model is updated incrementally as new data arrives to forecast future outcomes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequential learning process where a model updates its parameters as data arrives in a stream.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequential learning setting where a model must predict labels or abstain as examples arrive one by one.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sequential prediction framework where an algorithm updates its strategy based on expert advice to minimize regret.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A training paradigm where a model updates its parameters sequentially as new data arrives, often implemented using recurrent neural networks for regression.</skos:definition>
