  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#xai_ml">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Xai Ml</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of AI focused on making the internal mechanisms and predictions of models understandable to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of artificial intelligence focused on creating models whose predictions and decisions can be understood by human users.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of machine learning focused on making the internal mechanisms and decisions of models transparent and understandable to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of research focused on creating models whose internal logic and decision-making processes are transparent to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on creating methods to make the decisions of black box models transparent and understandable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on creating methods to make the internal logic of black-box models transparent to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on the ability to elaborate the reasoning process by which a trained model arrives at its decision.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study that focuses on making the internal mechanisms and outputs of complex models transparent to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework combining gradient boosting and Shapley values to provide interpretable predictions for driver fatigue monitoring.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that provides justifications for the predictions made by a predictive model without reducing its accuracy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of methods and techniques designed to make the internal logic and decision-making processes of models transparent to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of methods and techniques that make the internal logic and outcomes of black-box models transparent to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques and methods designed to make the outputs of machine learning models transparent and interpretable to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques designed to make the internal logic and decision-making process of complex models transparent and understandable to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques designed to make the internal logic and predictions of complex models understandable to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques that provide feature-based explanations to guide the crafting of adversarial examples for robustness evaluation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A subfield of artificial intelligence that focuses on making the internal mechanisms and outputs of models transparent and understandable to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A subset of artificial intelligence focused on producing models whose predictions can be understood by humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A suite of methods designed to make the internal logic and decisions of a model understandable to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[make the internal logic and decision-making processes of models transparent to humans, make the internal logic and decision-making process of complex models transparent and understandable to humans, make the internal logic and predictions of complex models understandable to humans, make the internal logic and decisions of a model understandable to humans] produce models whose internal logic can be easily understood by humans</rdfs:comment>
