  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#subspace_clustering">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Subspace Clustering</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering algorithm designed to group data points that lie in disjoint low-dimensional subspaces of a higher-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering method that groups data points based on whether they lie within a union of low-dimensional subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering method that groups data points into a union of low-dimensional linear or affine subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering method that identifies low-dimensional linear subspaces in high-dimensional data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering problem that involves grouping high-dimensional data into a union of low-dimensional subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimension reduction technique that models high-dimensional data as a union of low-dimensional subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that groups data points residing in the same low-dimensional subspace.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping method that identifies a union of low-dimensional linear subspaces within a high-dimensional dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping method that identifies clusters of data points lying in different low-dimensional linear subspaces of a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping method that partitions data points into subspaces by approximating the rank of a representation matrix.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping technique that partitions data points based on the assumption that they lie in a union of low-dimensional linear subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping technique that partitions high-dimensional data into a union of low-dimensional linear subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping technique that partitions high-dimensional data into a union of several low-dimensional linear subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that involves grouping data points into multiple low-dimensional linear subspaces within a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for grouping data points that lie in a union of low-dimensional linear subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of detecting clusters of nodes that are only interesting within a specific subset of attributes in a multi-attributed network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A spectral-clustering-based method that uses a convex program for optimal direction search to group data points belonging to the same subspace.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for grouping data points that lie in the same low-dimensional linear subspace.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algebro-geometric approach that segments data points into multiple subspaces of varying dimensions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points based on the assumption that they lie in a union of low-dimensional linear subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points based on the assumption that they lie in a union of low-dimensional subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points based on the linear or affine subspaces they inhabit.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points based on the linear subspaces they inhabit.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points based on the low-dimensional subspaces they inhabit.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points based on the union of linear subspaces they originate from.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points belonging to the same linear subspace.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points belonging to the same low-dimensional linear subspace.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points by identifying the linear subspaces they belong to, often using a self-expressive property.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points lying in a union of low-dimensional subspaces into separate clusters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that groups data points supported on a union of linear subspaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that identifies low-dimensional linear structures to group data points into clusters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning method that partitions data into a set of linear subspaces to identify shared patterns.</rdfs:comment>
