  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#zeroshotlearning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Zeroshotlearning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A capability of a model to correctly recognize or adapt to novel tasks without having seen any training examples for them.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A capability of a model to perform a task or recognize a category without having seen explicit training examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A capability of large language models to perform tasks without specific training examples for that particular task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A capability of pre-trained models to solve new tasks without task-specific training data by using natural language prompts.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A classification framework that recognizes images of unseen classes using only semantic information and coupled dictionary learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A classification task where a model recognizes unseen classes using prior descriptive attributes rather than labeled training examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A classification task where the model must recognize objects from classes that were not seen during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for recognizing object categories without training images by leveraging semantic information from text corpora.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generalization task where a model must classify instances from target classes that were not seen during the training phase.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to make predictions on unseen labels by utilizing side information about semantic labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to perform a task without having seen any specific training examples for that task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to recognize classes it has never seen during training by using auxiliary information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to recognize novel categories without having seen any labeled training examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to recognize novel classes without having seen any training examples from those classes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to recognize objects from classes that were not seen during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to recognize objects or relationships not seen during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to recognize or perform tasks on classes or languages it has not seen during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to recognize or predict items from categories it has never seen during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning capability that allows a model to recognize classes it has never seen during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that enables a model to predict unseen labels by leveraging semantic relationships between classes.</rdfs:comment>
