    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A capability of a model to correctly recognize or adapt to novel tasks without having seen any training examples for them.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A capability of a model to perform a task or recognize a category without having seen explicit training examples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A capability of large language models to perform tasks without specific training examples for that particular task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A capability of pre-trained models to solve new tasks without task-specific training data by using natural language prompts.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A classification framework that recognizes images of unseen classes using only semantic information and coupled dictionary learning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A classification task where a model recognizes unseen classes using prior descriptive attributes rather than labeled training examples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A classification task where the model must recognize objects from classes that were not seen during training.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework for recognizing object categories without training images by leveraging semantic information from text corpora.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generalization task where a model must classify instances from target classes that were not seen during the training phase.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to make predictions on unseen labels by utilizing side information about semantic labels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a model to perform a task without having seen any specific training examples for that task.</skos:definition>
