  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#autoencoder">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Autoencoder</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that resembles a communication channel and is analyzed using information theoretic methodology.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning methodology that maps data structures into a continuous latent space for generative purposes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning-based architecture used for end-to-end learning of communications systems to minimize bit error rates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep neural network used to compress high-dimensional data into small latent representations for efficient policy learning in embedded systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensional reduction technique used to optimize network traffic datasets for malware detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative neural network architecture used to produce streamlines with better spatial coverage in tractography reconstructions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative neural network that learns to compress and reconstruct data to mitigate adversarial attacks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A latent model used for image generation that estimates the latent distribution explicitly using a latent density estimator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that learns efficient data codings by attempting to reconstruct its input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture consisting of an encoder and decoder used to learn efficient low-dimensional representations of input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to compress input data into a latent representation and reconstruct it.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to compress input data into a latent representation and then reconstruct the original input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn a compressed representation of input data for tasks such as reconstruction or denoising.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn disentangled latent representations of shape and pose for 3D human body models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient codings of input data by compressing it into a bottleneck layer and then reconstructing it.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient codings of input data by reconstructing the input at the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient codings of input data by training the network to reconstruct the input at the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient codings of input data for tasks such as anomaly detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient compressed representations of input data in an unsupervised manner.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient compressed representations of input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data codings and approximations for reconstructions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data codings by attempting to reconstruct its input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data codings by compressing input into a latent representation and reconstructing it.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data codings by minimizing reconstruction error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data codings in an unsupervised manner by compressing input into a latent representation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data codings in an unsupervised manner by reconstructing its input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data codings in an unsupervised manner by reproducing the input at the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data codings in an unsupervised manner for tasks like image compression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data codings in an unsupervised manner.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data encodings by reconstructing its input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data encodings for tasks such as anomaly detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient data representations by reconstructing its input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient representations of data by reconstructing the input from a latent space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture designed to learn efficient representations of input data by reconstructing the input at the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture equipped with a discriminator to recover hidden components from an invertible mixture of independent components.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that compresses input data into a discrete latent space for representation learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that jointly learns a precoder and decoder for data symbol detection in communication receivers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed latent representation of data for solving differential equations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed latent representation of input data for tasks like clustering or similarity retrieval.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed latent representation of input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation by reconstructing its own input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of data by attempting to reconstruct its input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of data by attempting to reconstruct the input at the output layer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of data by reconstructing its input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of data by reconstructing the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of data by training a decoder to approximate a physical process and an encoder to map goals to designs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that learns a compressed representation of input data by attempting to reconstruct the original input.</rdfs:comment>
