  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#weakly_supervised_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Weakly Supervised Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning approach that leverages incomplete or partial information from electronic medical records to improve object detection in medical images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that trains models using noisy or imprecise labels to estimate the target distribution of the data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that uses labels provided at a coarse level, such as image-level labels, to train a model for fine-grained tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that uses noisy, limited, or imprecise annotations to train a model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that utilizes imprecise or limited labels to train a model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that utilizes imprecise or noisy labels to guide the training of a model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that utilizes imprecise or noisy labels to train a model for a specific task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that utilizes noisy or imprecise labels to train a model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that enables models to generalize from limited, sparse, or inaccurate annotations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that leverages imprecise or noisy labels derived from expert knowledge to train models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that trains models using imprecise or incomplete labels to reduce the need for exhaustive manual annotation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that trains models using imprecise, noisy, or limited labeled data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses a small set of seed words or noisy labels to train classifiers without extensive manual annotation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses imprecise or coarse-grained labels to train a model, often guided by attention mechanisms like saliency maps.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that uses rule-based knowledge or noisy labels to train models on large unlabeled datasets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that utilizes coarse labels for entire sequences rather than precise labels for every single timestamp.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that utilizes imprecise or coarse-grained labels to train models when strong labels are unavailable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that utilizes imprecise or noisy labels to train a model for predictive tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that utilizes imprecise or noisy labels to train a model when full supervision is unavailable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that utilizes imprecise or noisy labels to train models when high-quality labeled data is scarce.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that utilizes noisy or imprecise labels to train a model for a target task.</rdfs:comment>
