  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#convex_relaxation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Convex Relaxation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational technique that approximates a hard discrete optimization problem with a continuous version to find a global optimum.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical approximation that transforms a discrete optimization problem into a continuous convex one.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to approximate non-convex optimization problems to verify the robustness of neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical optimization technique that approximates a non-convex problem with a convex one to provide provable guarantees.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical optimization technique used to approximate the NP-hard densest k-subgraph problem via nuclear norm relaxation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that approximates a combinatorial penalty function with a convex one to simplify optimization and support recovery.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that approximates a difficult non-convex optimization problem with a simpler convex one to find a global optimum.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that approximates a hard optimization problem with a simpler convex one to find a tractable solution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that approximates a non-convex optimization problem with a convex one to make it computationally tractable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that approximates a non-convex optimization problem with a convex one to provide certifiable robustness bounds.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that transforms a difficult non-convex optimization problem into a simpler convex one.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique used to analyze and find global minima in non-convex factorization problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical transformation that approximates a non-convex optimization problem with a convex surrogate to ensure global optimality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical transformation that converts a hard discrete optimization problem into a continuous convex problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that approximates a non-convex optimization problem with a convex one to make it computationally tractable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that approximates a non-convex problem with a convex one to enable provably robust model training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that transforms a non-convex optimization problem into a convex one to make it computationally tractable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization technique that approximates a computationally hard problem by replacing a non-convex constraint with a convex one.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization technique that transforms a hard discrete problem into a continuous form to provide certificates of optimality for clustering.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization technique that transforms a non-convex problem into a convex one to ensure global convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[approximate non-convex optimization problems to verify the robustness of neural networks] approximate non-convex optimization problems to verify the robustness of neural networks</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[approximate the np-hard densest k-subgraph problem via nuclear norm relaxation] approximate the np-hard densest k-subgraph problem via nuclear norm relaxation</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[analyze and find global minima in non-convex factorization problems] analyze and find global minima in non-convex factorization problems</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[hard problem via convex replacement] hard problem via convex replacement</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[hard discrete problem into a continuous form] hard discrete problem into a continuous form</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[non-convex problem into a convex one] hard problem via convex replacement</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A computational technique that approximates a hard discrete optimization problem with a continuous version to find a global optimum.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical approximation that transforms a discrete optimization problem into a continuous convex one.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to approximate non-convex optimization problems to verify the robustness of neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical optimization technique that approximates a non-convex problem with a convex one to provide provable guarantees.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical optimization technique used to approximate the NP-hard densest k-subgraph problem via nuclear norm relaxation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that approximates a combinatorial penalty function with a convex one to simplify optimization and support recovery.</skos:definition>
