    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical tool that uses historical data to forecast the likelihood of an event or the presence of a specific characteristic.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical tool that uses historical data to forecast the likelihood of specific clinical outcomes or events.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical tool that uses historical data to predict future outcomes or identify key drivers of a target variable.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical tool that uses linguistic features from disclosure texts to forecast the bankruptcy of public firms.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical tool used to forecast future outcomes based on historical patterns in data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical tool used to forecast student performance based on persistent characteristics such as study habits and social interactions.</skos:definition>
