  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#inductivebias">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Inductivebias</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions a learner uses to predict outputs for inputs it has not encountered during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions a learner uses to predict outputs for inputs it has not encountered, which influences the decision boundaries of convolutional neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions a learner uses to predict outputs for inputs it has not encountered.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions a learner uses to prioritize certain hypotheses over others during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions a learning algorithm uses to prioritize one hypothesis over another when the data is insufficient.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions used by a learner to prioritize certain hypotheses over others.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions used by a learning algorithm to prioritize certain hypotheses over others during the search for a solution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions used by a learning algorithm to prioritize certain hypotheses over others during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions used by a learning algorithm to prioritize certain hypotheses over others to improve generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions used by a learning algorithm to prioritize certain hypotheses over others when constructing a model of the environment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions used by a learning algorithm to prioritize certain patterns over others during generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of assumptions used by a learning algorithm to prioritize certain solutions over others for better generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of prior assumptions used by a learner to make inferences that go beyond the observed data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of prior assumptions used to constrain a learning algorithm to improve generalization and adherence to physical laws.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The set of assumptions a learning algorithm uses to prioritize certain hypotheses over others when presented with data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[constrain a learning algorithm to improve generalization and adherence to physical laws] constrain a learning algorithm to improve generalization and adherence to physical laws</rdfs:comment>
