    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis method used to characterize the shape of data by tracking the birth and death of topological features across scales.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis method used to measure the distribution and shape of manifolds generated by generative neural network models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis method used to quantify the strength of interactions between features by analyzing connectivity in neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis methodology that captures the shape and size of data by producing a statistical summary called a persistence diagram.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis technique that generates features from point clouds to perform dimensionality reduction and classification on images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis technique used to calculate multi-scale connectivity signatures to preserve structure in latent representations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool that computes multi-scale invariant properties of high-dimensional data to identify robust patterns.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool that computes robust features in discrete observations to identify nontrivial structures.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool that measures the evolution of geometric features across different spatial scales.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool that studies the shape of data by characterizing topological signals through a set of intervals called bar codes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool that studies the shape of datasets by tracking the evolution of features across different scales.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool that tracks the evolution of features across different spatial scales to summarize shape information.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool that tracks the evolution of features across different spatial scales.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool that tracks the evolution of geometric features across different scales.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool that tracks the evolution of homological features across different spatial scales.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool that tracks the evolution of topological features across different filtration levels of a dataset.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool used to compute graph features for representation learning on blockchain transaction networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological data analysis tool used to detect adversarial inputs by analyzing the structural persistence of subgraphs in neural network computations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological feature extraction method used to make signal detection more resilient to noise in gravitational wave data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological method that tracks the birth and death of features across different spatial scales.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A topological tool that tracks the evolution of topological features over time to analyze noisy, nonlinear, and nonstationary signals.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#mathematical_foundations"/>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">homological persistence</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">simplicial complexes and persistent homology</skos:altLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#linearcontextualbandit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Linearcontextualbandit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A bandit algorithm where rewards are modeled as linear functions of side information available at each decision point.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making algorithm that can be manipulated by malicious agents through adversarial modifications to rewards or contexts.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making framework that learns an optimal policy based on side information and rewards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making framework that selects actions based on side information to maximize rewards while adhering to resource constraints.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making framework that uses linear functions of context to estimate the expected reward of different actions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making framework where an agent chooses actions based on side information to maximize cumulative rewards over time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making model that assumes a linear relationship between context features and the expected reward of an action.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making model where the reward of each arm is a linear function of a context vector provided at each time step.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making problem where an agent chooses actions based on side information to maximize cumulative rewards in a linear reward model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making problem where an agent chooses actions based on side information to maximize cumulative rewards under a linear reward model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decision-making problem where an agent selects actions based on side information to maximize cumulative rewards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning framework for online learning that balances exploration and exploitation based on context vectors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework for sequential decision making where rewards depend on a context vector and the expected reward is linear in the context.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework used to select the most successful manipulation strategy for unseen items based on a linear relationship between context and reward.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework where an agent chooses actions based on context to maximize rewards in a linear reward function setting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework where an agent chooses actions based on side information to maximize cumulative rewards in a linear reward function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning problem where an agent chooses actions based on context to maximize rewards while dealing with unknown reward functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning problem where an agent chooses actions based on side information to maximize rewards using a linear reward model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning problem where arms are chosen based on side information to maximize relative reward rank.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning problem where the agent chooses actions based on context vectors to maximize cumulative reward.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning problem where the reward of an action depends on a side-information vector called the context.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sequential decision making framework where the reward is a linear function of the context and the chosen action.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An online learning problem where an agent chooses actions based on side information to maximize cumulative reward.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[linear functions of context] linear functions of context</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[select the most successful manipulation strategy for unseen items based on a linear relationship between context and reward] select the most successful manipulation strategy for unseen items based on a linear relationship between context and reward</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[rewards] reward</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[decision-making algorithm] decision-making algorithm</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[actions] action</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[exploration and exploitation] exploration and exploitation</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[arms] arms</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[reward] reward</rdfs:comment>
