  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#compressed_sensing">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Compressed Sensing</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A sampling theory that enables the reconstruction of sparse signals from an incomplete set of measurements using projection matrices.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing framework that reconstructs a signal from a small number of linear projections using deep learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing framework that recovers sparse physiological signals from undersampled or noisy measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing framework that recovers sparse signals from a small number of non-adaptive measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique for efficiently acquiring and reconstructing a signal by finding a sparse representation in some orthonormal basis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique for efficiently acquiring and reconstructing a signal by using fewer samples than required by the Nyquist criterion.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique for efficiently acquiring and reconstructing a signal from a small number of non-adaptive measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique for efficiently acquiring and reconstructing a signal from far fewer samples than required by the Nyquist-Shannon theorem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique for reconstructing signals from far fewer samples than required by the Nyquist criterion.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique for recovering a signal from fewer samples than required by the Nyquist-Shannon sampling theorem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique for recovering a sparse signal from a small number of linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique for recovering sparse signals from a small number of linear measurements using an optimized acquisition matrix.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique for recovering sparse signals from a small number of linear projections.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique for recovering sparse vectors from a limited number of measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that allows for the reconstruction of a signal from fewer samples than required by the Nyquist-Shannon sampling theorem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that allows for the reconstruction of a sparse signal from a small number of linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that allows the reconstruction of a signal from a number of samples significantly below the Nyquist rate.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that allows the reconstruction of a sparse signal from a small number of linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that allows the reconstruction of a sparse signal from fewer samples than required by the Nyquist-Shannon theorem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that allows the recovery of a sparse signal from fewer samples than required by the Nyquist criterion.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that allows the recovery of a sparse signal from fewer samples than required by the Nyquist-Shannon sampling theorem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that allows the recovery of sparse signals from a small number of linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that enables high subsampling factors in MRI to reduce scan durations while maintaining image quality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that enables the recovery of sparse signals from a small number of measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that enables the recovery of sparse signals from far fewer samples than required by the Nyquist criterion.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that reconstructs a high-dimensional signal from a small number of linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that reconstructs a signal from fewer samples than required by the Nyquist criterion.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that reconstructs a sparse signal from a small number of linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that reconstructs a sparse signal from a small number of non-adaptive linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that reconstructs an unknown signal from a small number of linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that reconstructs high-quality images from undersampled data below the Nyquist-Shannon rate.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that reconstructs high-resolution images from fewer samples than traditionally required.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that reconstructs images from under-sampled data by promoting sparsity in the temporal domain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that reconstructs sparse signals from a small number of linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that recovers a high-dimensional signal from a small number of linear measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A signal processing technique that recovers a sparse signal from fewer measurements than required by traditional sampling theory.</rdfs:comment>
