    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A parameter estimation method that avoids calculating the normalizing constant by matching the gradient of the log-density.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A parameter estimation tool for fitting unnormalized probability density models, specifically applied here to truncated densities.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique for estimating a probability density function by matching the score function, which is the gradient of the log-density.</skos:definition>
