    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that compresses input data into a latent representation by maximizing the mutual information between the representation and the target.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that compresses input data into a latent representation while maximizing the predictive power for a target variable.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that uses variational inference to learn a compressed representation that retains only the information relevant to a specific task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A generative framework that compresses input data into a latent representation to maximize predictive power while minimizing redundant information.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A latent representation framework that compresses input features to retain only the information most relevant for downstream tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A nonlinear compression method that retains only the information in embeddings necessary for a specific discriminative task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization framework that compresses input data into a representation that retains only the information relevant for a specific target.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization method that improves classification calibration and out-of-distribution detection by compressing input information.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that compresses an input signal to retain only the information most relevant for a specific prediction task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that compresses input data into a minimal sufficient statistic to improve generalization and reduce noise.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that learns a compressed representation of the input that retains only the information relevant for predicting the target.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that balances empirical and Bayesian objectives to minimize risks from finite sampling of targets.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that learns a compressed representation of input data that retains only the information relevant to a target task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An information theoretic framework used to extract brief and comprehensive explanations from black-box decision systems.</skos:definition>
