  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#network_representation_learning_task">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Network Representation Learning Task</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A graph analytics technique that transforms the structural characteristics of a network into low-dimensional vector embeddings.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that embeds network vertices into a low-dimensional vector space while preserving topological structure and vertex content.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that maps heterogeneous information networks into a low-dimensional space to facilitate search, classification, and prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning technique that encodes network nodes and edges into low-dimensional vectors to identify hidden relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning technique that maps network components into low-dimensional Euclidean spaces using random walks and co-occurrence patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for learning low-dimensional embeddings of vertices in homogeneous, heterogeneous, or bipartite networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for transforming graph structures into low-dimensional vector spaces while preserving structural properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that maps complex networks into a low-dimensional vector space to facilitate analysis tasks like node classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that maps nodes of a graph into a low-dimensional vector space while preserving structural properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that maps vertices of a graph into a low-dimensional vector space while preserving structural properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that maps vertices of a network into a low-dimensional space while preserving the structural information of the graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that transforms graph-based interaction data into low-dimensional vectors for downstream predictive tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of encoding network topology and attributes into low-dimensional vectors for downstream analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of identifying low-dimensional embeddings of graph-structured data for visualization and classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of learning low-dimensional embeddings for nodes in a graph to capture its structural properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of learning low-dimensional vector embeddings for nodes in a social network to capture local and global structures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of learning low-dimensional vector representations for nodes based on network structures or node attributes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of mapping graph nodes and edges into low-dimensional vectors while preserving the structural properties of the network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of mapping graph vertices into a low-dimensional vector space to facilitate downstream algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of mapping nodes in a graph to low-dimensional vectors while preserving the network structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of projecting a network's topological structure into a low-dimensional vector space for downstream analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process that transforms graph structures into low-dimensional vector spaces for downstream analysis tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for mapping nodes of a high-dimensional graph into low-dimensional vector spaces while preserving the graph's structural properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for mapping nodes or edges of a graph into low-dimensional vectors while preserving the network's structural properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that maps a real-world information network into a low-dimensional space while preserving its inherent properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that represents graph structures via low-dimension vectors to support social-oriented applications.</rdfs:comment>
