  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#semidefinite_programming_relaxation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Semidefinite Programming Relaxation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A convex optimization method that approximates a difficult discrete problem by relaxing it into a continuous form.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A convex optimization technique that approximates a hard combinatorial problem by relaxing it into a semidefinite program.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A convex optimization technique that approximates a non-convex problem by relaxing constraints into a semidefinite program.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A convex optimization technique that approximates an NP-hard discrete problem by relaxing it into a semidefinite program.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A convex optimization technique used to approximate computationally intractable non-convex problems like l0-norm penalties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A convex optimization technique used to certify the robustness of ReLU networks against adversarial perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical optimization technique used to approximate a high-dimensional subspace projection problem for compressive classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that transforms a hard combinatorial optimization problem into a convex one for easier solving.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that transforms a non-convex optimization problem into a convex one by relaxing constraints into semidefinite matrices.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization technique that transforms a difficult non-convex problem into a convex semidefinite program.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization technique that transforms a hard combinatorial problem into a convex problem over the cone of positive semidefinite matrices.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[certify the robustness of relu networks against adversarial perturbations] certify the robustness of relu networks against adversarial perturbations</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[approximate a high-dimensional subspace projection problem for compressive classification] approximate a high-dimensional subspace projection problem for compressive classification</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a difficult/hard problem] difficult/hard problem</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a hard/non-convex problem into a convex one] hard/non-convex problem into a convex one</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A convex optimization method that approximates a difficult discrete problem by relaxing it into a continuous form.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A convex optimization technique that approximates a hard combinatorial problem by relaxing it into a semidefinite program.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A convex optimization technique that approximates a non-convex problem by relaxing constraints into a semidefinite program.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A convex optimization technique that approximates an NP-hard discrete problem by relaxing it into a semidefinite program.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A convex optimization technique used to approximate computationally intractable non-convex problems like l0-norm penalties.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A convex optimization technique used to certify the robustness of ReLU networks against adversarial perturbations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical optimization technique used to approximate a high-dimensional subspace projection problem for compressive classification.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that transforms a hard combinatorial optimization problem into a convex one for easier solving.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that transforms a non-convex optimization problem into a convex one by relaxing constraints into semidefinite matrices.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization technique that transforms a difficult non-convex problem into a convex semidefinite program.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization technique that transforms a hard combinatorial problem into a convex problem over the cone of positive semidefinite matrices.</skos:definition>
