  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#domaingeneralization">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Domaingeneralization</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that aims to create a model capable of performing well on unseen target domains without having access to them during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that aims to create models capable of performing well on unseen target domains without having access to them during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that enables a classifier to generalize to unknown target domains using a heterogeneous collection of training sources.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning methodology that enables a model trained on a source domain to perform effectively in new, unseen challenging domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning objective aimed at creating a model that performs well on unseen target domains without using their data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning objective where a model is trained on multiple source domains to perform well on unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning objective where a model is trained to perform well on unseen target domains without having access to them during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm aimed at training models to maintain robustness when encountering unseen data distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that aims to build a model capable of performing well on unseen data distributions without using target-domain data during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that aims to create models capable of performing well on unseen distributions without target-domain data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that aims to train a model on multiple source domains so it can perform well on unseen target domains without further adaptation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that develops models on multi-domain source data to perform well on unknown target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning setting that aims to train a model on multiple source domains so that it performs well on unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning strategy that aims to create a model capable of performing well on unseen target domains without using data from those domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning strategy that aims to create models capable of performing well on entirely unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning strategy that aims to produce a model capable of performing well on unseen target distributions using data from multiple source domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning task where a model is trained on multiple source domains to perform well on an entirely unseen target domain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning task where a model is trained to perform accurately on unseen target domains without using domain labels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach aimed at building models that remain robust and accurate when applied to unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that aims to learn representations that are robust and invariant across multiple different domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that aims to train a model on one or more source domains so that it generalizes to unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that aims to train a model on one or more source domains so that it performs well on an unseen target domain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that aims to train models to perform well on unseen target domains without having access to data from those domains during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that learns domain-agnostic feature representations to improve model performance on unseen data distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning capability that allows a model trained on one source domain to perform accurately on unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning goal of training models to perform robustly on unseen domains without requiring data from those domains during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning goal to create models that perform well on unseen distributions without having access to them during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning goal to develop models that perform robustly across multiple unseen target domains without explicit adaptation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning goal to develop models that perform well on an unseen target domain without having accessed that domain during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning goal to develop models that perform well on unseen test distributions without access to target domain data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning goal where a model is trained on one or more source domains to perform well on an unseen target domain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning goal where a model is trained to perform well on unseen data distributions without having access to them during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning objective aimed at maintaining model performance across different but related data distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning objective that aims to build models capable of performing well on unseen distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning objective that aims to make models perform well on unseen target domains without using their data during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning objective that aims to train a model on one or more source distributions so that it performs well on unseen target distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning objective that aims to train a model to perform well on unseen distributions without having access to them during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning objective to ensure a model performs well on unseen target domains without using their data during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning objective to ensure that a model trained on one or more source domains performs well on unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning objective to train a model that performs well on unseen target domains without requiring data from those domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm aimed at training models that perform well on unseen data distributions without requiring target domain samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to apply knowledge from multiple labeled source domains to unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to learn domain-invariant features to ensure a model performs well on unseen target domains without further training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to learn models robust to domain shift using data from limited source domains without target domain access.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to learn representations from multiple source domains to ensure robust performance on an unseen target domain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to train a model on one or more source domains so that it performs well on unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to train a model on source data so that it performs well on unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to train a model to perform well on unseen target domains without using their data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to train models to perform accurately on unseen target domains without utilizing target data during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that aims to train models to perform well on data distributions that were not encountered during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that employs multiple source domains to build robust models capable of generalizing to unseen target domains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that learns from multiple source domains to generalize to unseen target domains under distribution discrepancy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that learns to generalize to unseen target domains by leveraging knowledge from multiple source domains.</rdfs:comment>
