    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning technique that iteratively assigns labels to unlabeled samples using a model trained on labeled and previously pseudo-labeled data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning technique that uses a model's own high-confidence predictions as ground truth labels for unlabeled data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning technique that uses a pre-trained model to generate labels for unlabeled data to expand the training set.</skos:definition>
