  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#projected_gradient_descent">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Projected Gradient Descent</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm that constrains the solution to a specific set by projecting the gradient step back onto that set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm that ensures the solution remains within a constrained domain by projecting updates back onto the feasible set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm that minimizes a function by taking steps in the direction of the negative gradient and projecting the result back onto a feasible set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm that projects gradient steps onto specific subspaces to estimate gradient-sparse parameter vectors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm used as a tool to analyze the region of attraction for large-scale nonlinear systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm used in adversarial testing to find norm-bounded perturbations that cause neural network misclassification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm used to generate adversarial examples by controlling the maximum perturbation of the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm used to solve nonconvex problems with rank constraints.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization method that constrains the update step to a specific feasible set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that converges to a global optimum by enforcing constraints on variables in nonconvex problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that finds the minimum of a function within a constrained set by projecting the gradient step onto that set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that iteratively updates parameters to minimize a function while ensuring the result stays within a feasible set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that iteratively updates variables and projects them onto a feasible constraint set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that minimizes a function by taking steps in the direction of the negative gradient and projecting the result onto a feasible set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that performs a gradient step followed by a projection onto a feasible set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that solves constrained convex problems by projecting the gradient step back onto the feasible region.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that solves constrained problems by projecting the gradient step back onto the feasible set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm that updates parameters using the gradient and then maps the result back onto a constrained set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm used to find low-rank tensor fits to data under generalized parametric models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization algorithm used to learn weight vectors of Rectified Linear Units in high-dimensional regimes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization-based adversarial attack method used to generate perturbations that fool object detection systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[solve nonconvex problems with rank constraints] solve nonconvex problems with rank constraints</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the gradient and then maps the result back onto a constrained set] gradient step followed by a projection onto a feasible set</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[find low-rank tensor fits to data under generalized parametric models] find low-rank tensor fits to data under generalized parametric models</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[learn weight vectors of rectified linear units in high-dimensional regimes] learn weight vectors of rectified linear units in high-dimensional regimes</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[generate perturbations that fool object detection systems] perturbations that fool object detection systems</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[perturbations that fool object detection systems] perturbations that fool object detection systems</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a gradient step followed by a projection onto a feasible set] gradient step followed by a projection onto a feasible set</rdfs:comment>
