  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#koopman_operator">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Koopman Operator</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data-driven tool that maps nonlinear systems into equivalent linear systems in an embedding space for real-time control.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear embedding of nonlinear dynamics whose eigenfunctions can be used to discover conserved quantities of a system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that describes the evolution of a dynamical system by lifting the state space into an infinite-dimensional function space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that describes the evolution of a nonlinear dynamical system by lifting the state space into an infinite-dimensional function space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that describes the evolution of functions of the state in a nonlinear dynamical system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that describes the evolution of observables in a dynamical system to simplify non-linear analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that describes the evolution of observables in a nonlinear dynamical system.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that describes the evolution of observables in the weight space of a neural network during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that maps the flow of a nonlinear dynamical system onto a space of observables to simplify analysis and control.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that represents a non-linear dynamical system in an infinite-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that represents a nonlinear dynamical system by lifting it into an infinite-dimensional function space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that represents a nonlinear dynamical system by lifting the state into an infinite-dimensional function space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that represents a nonlinear dynamical system in an infinite-dimensional function space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that represents nonlinear dynamical systems in a higher-dimensional space to facilitate linear control design.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that represents nonlinear dynamical systems in an infinite-dimensional space to enable linear analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator that transforms a nonlinear dynamical system into an infinite-dimensional linear space for easier analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear operator used in a deep learning framework to represent and predict the behavior of nonlinear dynamical systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A linear representation used to identify nonlinear dynamics from data for efficient control design.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that represents non-linear dynamical systems as linear operators in a higher-dimensional latent space.</rdfs:comment>
