  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#neural_network_pruning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Neural Network Pruning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A compression method that removes redundant weights or neurons from a model to reduce its size and computational cost.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational efficiency technique that reduces the size of a model by removing unused neurons without compromising accuracy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of reducing model complexity by removing redundant weights or connections from a trained network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression method that removes redundant weights or neurons to decrease computational overhead.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression process that removes redundant weights or connections from a network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression process that removes redundant weights or neurons to reduce computational cost.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that identifies and removes redundant components to reduce parameter count and accelerate inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that removes low-salience neurons to reduce size and improve generalization capacity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that removes parameters to prevent overfitting and improve generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that removes redundant parameters from a neural network to increase sparsity and efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that removes redundant parameters from a pre-trained network to reduce inference costs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that removes redundant parameters from a trained network to improve efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that removes redundant parameters or filters to reduce the size and computational cost of a network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression technique that removes redundant parameters through iterative training and pruning steps to improve efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
