  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#deepimageprior">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Deepimageprior</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that uses an untrained convolutional neural network as a regularization prior to perform tasks like phase unwrapping without training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that uses the structure of a neural network as a regularization prior for inverse problems like image reconstruction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that uses the structure of a neural network as a regularization prior for solving inverse problems in image processing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that uses the structure of a randomly initialized convolutional neural network as a regularization prior to solve inverse problems without training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network structure that captures low-level image statistics to enable unsupervised layer decomposition.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A phenomenon where the structure of a convolutional network acts as a regularizer for natural images without requiring training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the architecture of an untrained network as a prior to recover images from corrupted measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the structure of a convolutional network as a prior for image restoration without external training data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the structure of a convolutional network as a prior for natural images without requiring pre-training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the structure of a convolutional neural network as a prior for image recovery tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the structure of a convolutional neural network as a prior to reconstruct images without pre-training on a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the structure of a neural network as a prior to reconstruct images from corrupted data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unlearned generative model approach where the network structure itself acts as a regularizer for solving inverse problems without pre-training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised approach that leverages the architecture of a neural network as a regularizer to reconstruct images without pre-training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised approach that uses the architecture of a convolutional neural network as a regularizer for image restoration.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised framework that uses the structure of a neural network as a regularization prior for image restoration tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning approach that uses the structure of a convolutional neural network as a regularizer to recover images from corrupted or incomplete data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised method that uses the architecture of a neural network as a regularizer for inverse problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised neural network approach that uses the structure of the network itself as a regularization prior for image reconstruction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An untrained neural network approach that uses the structure of a network architecture as a regularizer for inverse problems like denoising.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[an untrained convolutional neural network as a regularization prior, the structure of a neural network as a regularization prior, the structure of a randomly initialized convolutional neural network as a regularization prior, the structure of a convolutional network as a prior, the structure of a convolutional neural network as a prior, the structure of a neural network as a prior, the structure of the network itself as a regularization prior] structure of a neural network as a prior</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the architecture of an untrained network as a prior] architecture of an untrained network as a prior</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the architecture of a convolutional neural network as a regularizer, the structure of a convolutional neural network as a regularizer, the architecture of a neural network as a regularizer, the structure of a network architecture as a regularizer] architecture of a neural network as a regularizer</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[tasks like phase unwrapping without training data] tasks like phase unwrapping without training data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[low-level image statistics] low-level image statistics</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[network structure] network structure</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that uses an untrained convolutional neural network as a regularization prior to perform tasks like phase unwrapping without training data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that uses the structure of a neural network as a regularization prior for inverse problems like image reconstruction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that uses the structure of a neural network as a regularization prior for solving inverse problems in image processing.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that uses the structure of a randomly initialized convolutional neural network as a regularization prior to solve inverse problems without training data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network structure that captures low-level image statistics to enable unsupervised layer decomposition.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A phenomenon where the structure of a convolutional network acts as a regularizer for natural images without requiring training data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the architecture of an untrained network as a prior to recover images from corrupted measurements.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the structure of a convolutional network as a prior for image restoration without external training data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the structure of a convolutional network as a prior for natural images without requiring pre-training.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the structure of a convolutional neural network as a prior for image recovery tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the structure of a convolutional neural network as a prior to reconstruct images without pre-training on a dataset.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A regularization technique that uses the structure of a neural network as a prior to reconstruct images from corrupted data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unlearned generative model approach where the network structure itself acts as a regularizer for solving inverse problems without pre-training.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised approach that leverages the architecture of a neural network as a regularizer to reconstruct images without pre-training.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised approach that uses the architecture of a convolutional neural network as a regularizer for image restoration.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised framework that uses the structure of a neural network as a regularization prior for image restoration tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning approach that uses the structure of a convolutional neural network as a regularizer to recover images from corrupted or incomplete data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised method that uses the architecture of a neural network as a regularizer for inverse problems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised neural network approach that uses the structure of the network itself as a regularization prior for image reconstruction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An untrained neural network approach that uses the structure of a network architecture as a regularizer for inverse problems like denoising.</skos:definition>
