  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#bayesian_inference">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Bayesian Inference</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational statistics method that uses manifold learning and sampling to estimate posterior distributions from small datasets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of statistical inference in which Bayes' theorem is used to update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence becomes available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of statistical inference in which Bayes' theorem is used to update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic method of updating the belief in a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic method that estimates the risk of infection based on contact lists and personal information for epidemic control.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic method that performs non-parametric conditional density estimation using a sequence of covers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic method that uses distributions in the logit layer to quantify prediction uncertainty.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical approach for estimating average treatment effects from observational data using data-driven modifications to nonparametric priors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method for estimating uncertainty in model predictions by combining prior knowledge with observed data through sampling or variational approximations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method for updating probability distributions of parameters in probabilistic programs using sampling.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method of updating the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that allows machine learning models to express uncertainty by drawing samples from a posterior distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that updates the probability distribution of a model's parameters as new data is observed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that updates the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence becomes available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that updates the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available to capture human behavioral deviations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that updates the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that uses Bayes' theorem to update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence becomes available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that uses Bayes' theorem to update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available, here used for bias correction in classification aggregates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that uses Bayes' theorem to update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that uses generative models to estimate the posterior distribution of parameters based on observed data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method that uses probability distributions to identify informative actions for learning-driven exploration.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to estimate the reliability of crowdsourced labels by updating probability distributions based on observed performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to find generating partitions and estimate entropy rates from discretized data in dynamical systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to optimize parameters and determine the mixing ratio between graph kernels and data-driven traffic models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[manifold learning and sampling] manifold learning and sampling</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence becomes available, update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available] update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence becomes available</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a sequence of covers] sequence of covers</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[distributions, probability distributions] distribution</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[data-driven modifications] data-driven modifications</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[sampling] sampling</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[bias correction in classification aggregates] bias correction in classification aggregates</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[estimate the reliability of crowdsourced labels by updating probability distributions based on observed performance] estimate the reliability of crowdsourced labels by updating probability distributions based on observed performance</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[find generating partitions and estimate entropy rates from discretized data in dynamical systems] find generating partitions and estimate entropy rates from discretized data in dynamical systems</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[optimize parameters and determine the mixing ratio between graph kernels and data-driven traffic models] optimize parameters and determine the mixing ratio between graph kernels and data-driven traffic models</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[non-parametric conditional density estimation using a sequence of covers] non-parametric conditional density estimation using a sequence of covers</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the belief/probability for a hypothesis] probability for a hypothesis</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the risk of infection] risk of infection</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[uncertainty in model predictions] uncertainty</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[uncertainty] uncertainty</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the probability distribution of a model's parameters] parameters of a probability distribution/model</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the probability for a hypothesis] probability for a hypothesis</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A computational statistics method that uses manifold learning and sampling to estimate posterior distributions from small datasets.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of statistical inference in which Bayes' theorem is used to update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence becomes available.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of statistical inference in which Bayes' theorem is used to update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic method of updating the belief in a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic method that estimates the risk of infection based on contact lists and personal information for epidemic control.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic method that performs non-parametric conditional density estimation using a sequence of covers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A probabilistic method that uses distributions in the logit layer to quantify prediction uncertainty.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical approach for estimating average treatment effects from observational data using data-driven modifications to nonparametric priors.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method for estimating uncertainty in model predictions by combining prior knowledge with observed data through sampling or variational approximations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method for updating probability distributions of parameters in probabilistic programs using sampling.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method of updating the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that allows machine learning models to express uncertainty by drawing samples from a posterior distribution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that updates the probability distribution of a model's parameters as new data is observed.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that updates the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence becomes available.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that updates the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available to capture human behavioral deviations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that updates the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that uses Bayes' theorem to update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence becomes available.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that uses Bayes' theorem to update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available, here used for bias correction in classification aggregates.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that uses Bayes' theorem to update the probability for a hypothesis as more evidence or information becomes available.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that uses generative models to estimate the posterior distribution of parameters based on observed data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that uses probability distributions to identify informative actions for learning-driven exploration.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to estimate the reliability of crowdsourced labels by updating probability distributions based on observed performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to find generating partitions and estimate entropy rates from discretized data in dynamical systems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to optimize parameters and determine the mixing ratio between graph kernels and data-driven traffic models.</skos:definition>
