    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A classification task that distinguishes between normal and adversarial input signals to defend machine learning systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A defense mechanism that identifies maliciously perturbed inputs designed to trick a classifier.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework designed to identify malicious inputs by comparing the outputs of an original model and a sanitized version.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of identifying maliciously perturbed inputs designed to mislead a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reactive defense mechanism that identifies inputs specifically crafted to fool a machine learning classifier.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security mechanism designed to identify inputs that have been intentionally perturbed to deceive a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security mechanism that identifies and rejects inputs specifically designed to fool a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security mechanism that identifies input samples specifically perturbed to cause model misclassification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security mechanism that identifies inputs specifically crafted to deceive a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security mechanism that identifies maliciously perturbed inputs designed to fool a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security method that identifies perturbed inputs designed to mislead a machine learning classifier.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security process that identifies inputs specifically crafted to fool machine learning classifiers by introducing small perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security process that identifies inputs specifically designed to trick a machine learning model into making a mistake.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security system that identifies malicious input samples in deep neural networks by analyzing the frequency domain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security task aimed at identifying inputs specifically crafted to deceive a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security task that distinguishes maliciously crafted inputs from original ones by analyzing feature attribution scores.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security task that identifies images designed to mislead deep neural network classifiers via slight perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security task that identifies inputs specifically crafted to deceive a machine learning model into making incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security task that identifies inputs specifically crafted to deceive machine learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security task that identifies samples with imperceptible perturbations designed to mislead neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
