  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#spectral_method">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Spectral Method</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A collection of algorithms that extract information from data using the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of specially designed matrices.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computationally efficient inference technique for nonparametric mixture models such as the Indian Buffet Process and Hierarchical Dirichlet Process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data analysis technique that uses eigenvectors of a matrix to detect global structures in sparse or noisy data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that utilizes the eigendecomposition of moment matrices to estimate model parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach for learning latent variable models by analyzing the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of observable operators.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach that analyzes the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a operator to derive smooth functions on manifolds.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach that decomposes temporal signals into frequency components for long-term forecasting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach that uses the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a matrix to estimate the column space of a low-rank matrix from noisy observations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach using spectral decomposition to estimate transition matrices and recover latent structures in Markov processes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A non-iterative learning approach that uses singular value decomposition or eigenvalue analysis to estimate model parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A scalable defense approach for graph neural networks that uses weighted spectral embedding to construct a robust base graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithm that analyzes the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a matrix to perform tasks like node classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithmic approach that uses the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a matrix to recover community structures in graphs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithmic approach that utilizes the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of matrices to solve systems of equations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[information] information</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of specially designed matrices, eigenvectors of a matrix, the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a matrix, the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of matrices] eigenvectors of a matrix</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[singular value decomposition or eigenvalue analysis] singular value decomposition or eigenvalue analysis</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the eigendecomposition of moment matrices] eigendecomposition of moment matrices</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[global structures in sparse or noisy data] global structures in sparse or noisy data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[tasks like node classification] node classification tasks</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[eigenvalues and eigenvectors of operators] eigenvalues and eigenvectors</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[temporal signals] temporal signals</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A collection of algorithms that extract information from data using the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of specially designed matrices.</skos:definition>
