    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A data analysis technique that uses eigenvectors of a matrix to detect global structures in sparse or noisy data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A learning approach that utilizes the eigendecomposition of moment matrices to estimate model parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach for learning latent variable models by analyzing the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of observable operators.</skos:definition>
