    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach that decomposes temporal signals into frequency components for long-term forecasting.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach that uses the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a matrix to estimate the column space of a low-rank matrix from noisy observations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach using spectral decomposition to estimate transition matrices and recover latent structures in Markov processes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A non-iterative learning approach that uses singular value decomposition or eigenvalue analysis to estimate model parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A scalable defense approach for graph neural networks that uses weighted spectral embedding to construct a robust base graph.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithm that analyzes the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a matrix to perform tasks like node classification.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An algorithmic approach that uses the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a matrix to recover community structures in graphs.</skos:definition>
