  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#stochastic_approximation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Stochastic Approximation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of iterative procedures used to find the roots of a function or the maximum of a system under stochastic noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning scheme used by recommendation systems to determine an optimal strategy when user profiles are unknown.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to analyze the convergence of iterative algorithms subject to random noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for finding the roots of a function or optimizing a parameter when the available observations are noisy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A recursive algorithm that seeks to find the root of a function when only noisy observations are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical learning method used to minimize objective functions through iterative updates based on noisy estimates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative algorithm used to evaluate the tradeoff between robustness to outliers and adaptivity to changes in non-stationary data streams.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the minimum of a convex objective using noisy gradient estimates from data streams.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root of a function or the extremum of a cost function when only noisy observations are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root of a function or the maximum of a parameter when only noisy observations are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root of a function or the maximum of a reward when only noisy observations are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root of a function or the minimum of a cost function when only noisy observations are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root of a function or the optimum of a parameter when the function is observed with noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root of a function when only noisy measurements are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root of a function when only noisy observations of the function are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root of a function when the available information is subject to noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root of an operator when only noisy observations of the operator are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root or extremum of a function when only noisy observations are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root or fixed point of a function when only noisy evaluations are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the root or optimum of a function when only noisy measurements are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the roots of a function or optimizing a parameter when the available information is noisy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the roots of a function or optimizing a parameter when the observations are subject to noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the roots of a function or optimizing parameters when the available information is noisy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the roots of a function or the maximum of a function when only noisy observations are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the roots of a function or the maximum of a function when the observations are subject to noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the roots of a function when the observations are subject to noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for finding the roots of functions or maximizing likelihoods when only noisy observations are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for solving fixed-point equations where the available information is corrupted by noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method for stochastic convex optimization that uses gradient estimates to find the minimum of a risk function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative method used to find the roots of a function when only noisy observations of the function are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative numerical procedure used to find the root of a function when the available measurements are noisy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization algorithm used to find the extremum of a function when only noisy observations are available.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An iterative optimization scheme used to find the roots of functions or optima in the presence of noise.</rdfs:comment>
