  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#layerwiserelevancepropagation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Layerwiserelevancepropagation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A decompositional attribution method that explains neural network decisions by redistributing the output prediction back through the layers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A post-hoc attribution method that decomposes the prediction of a neural network into the contributions of its individual input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A post-hoc interpretability method that explains the decisions of a neural network by backpropagating the output to the input layer.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for explaining deep learning model predictions by attributing the output to specific input pixels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for explaining predictions of complex non-linear classifiers by tracing decisions back to individual input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for explaining the decisions of deep neural networks by attributing the output to specific input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for explaining the predictions of a neural network by decomposing the output score and redistributing it back through the layers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for explaining the predictions of neural networks by propagating relevance scores back through the architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that attributes model predictions back to input variables to interpret the decisions of deep neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that explains the predictions of a neural network by attributing the output to specific input pixels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A visual interpretability method that explains neural network predictions by propagating relevance scores back through the layers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A visualization technique that explains the decisions of a neural network by redistributing the output prediction back through the layers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability method that attributes the output of a neural network to its input pixels and words.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability method that attributes the prediction of a deep network to its input features by propagating relevance scores backward.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability method that decomposes the output of a neural network back into the input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability method that decomposes the output of a neural network to attribute importance to input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability method that decomposes the output of a neural network to attribute the contribution of each input feature to the prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability method that decomposes the output of a neural network to identify the input variables most responsible for a prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability method that redistributes the prediction output backward through the network to identify influential inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique for deep models that produces human-readable heat maps to indicate the importance of input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that attributes the prediction of a neural network to its input pixels by propagating relevance scores backward.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes a model's prediction by redistributing the output value back through the network layers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes a neural network's output into contributions from individual input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network into contributions from each input feature.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to attribute importance to individual input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to attribute importance to specific input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to identify the contribution of individual input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to identify the contributions of input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to identify which input features were most influential.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output prediction of a neural network back to its input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique used to reverse engineer black-box neural networks by decomposing the output prediction back through the layers to the input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability technique used to understand the classification decisions of deep networks by identifying the importance of input frames.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainable AI technique that decomposes the prediction of a neural network into contributions of individual input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainable artificial intelligence method that quantifies the contribution of individual neurons to a model's prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An interpretability method that decomposes a neural network's prediction to attribute importance to specific input pixels.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An interpretability method that decomposes the prediction of a neural network by propagating relevance scores backward from the output to the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An interpretability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to attribute the prediction to specific input features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[reverse engineer black-box neural networks by decomposing the output prediction back through the layers to the input features] reverse engineer black-box neural networks by decomposing the output prediction back through the layers to the input features</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[understand the classification decisions of deep networks by identifying the importance of input frames] understand the classification decisions of deep networks by identifying the importance of input frames</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[neural network decisions/predictions, neural network predictions/decisions] neural network prediction</rdfs:comment>
