    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[prediction output] model predictions</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[human-readable heat maps] human-readable heat maps</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A decompositional attribution method that explains neural network decisions by redistributing the output prediction back through the layers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A post-hoc attribution method that decomposes the prediction of a neural network into the contributions of its individual input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A post-hoc interpretability method that explains the decisions of a neural network by backpropagating the output to the input layer.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique for explaining deep learning model predictions by attributing the output to specific input pixels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique for explaining predictions of complex non-linear classifiers by tracing decisions back to individual input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique for explaining the decisions of deep neural networks by attributing the output to specific input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique for explaining the predictions of a neural network by decomposing the output score and redistributing it back through the layers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique for explaining the predictions of neural networks by propagating relevance scores back through the architecture.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that attributes model predictions back to input variables to interpret the decisions of deep neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that explains the predictions of a neural network by attributing the output to specific input pixels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A visual interpretability method that explains neural network predictions by propagating relevance scores back through the layers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A visualization technique that explains the decisions of a neural network by redistributing the output prediction back through the layers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability method that attributes the output of a neural network to its input pixels and words.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability method that attributes the prediction of a deep network to its input features by propagating relevance scores backward.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability method that decomposes the output of a neural network back into the input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability method that decomposes the output of a neural network to attribute importance to input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability method that decomposes the output of a neural network to attribute the contribution of each input feature to the prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability method that decomposes the output of a neural network to identify the input variables most responsible for a prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability method that redistributes the prediction output backward through the network to identify influential inputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique for deep models that produces human-readable heat maps to indicate the importance of input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that attributes the prediction of a neural network to its input pixels by propagating relevance scores backward.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes a model's prediction by redistributing the output value back through the network layers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes a neural network's output into contributions from individual input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network into contributions from each input feature.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to attribute importance to individual input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to attribute importance to specific input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to identify the contribution of individual input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to identify the contributions of input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to identify which input features were most influential.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique that decomposes the output prediction of a neural network back to its input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique used to reverse engineer black-box neural networks by decomposing the output prediction back through the layers to the input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainability technique used to understand the classification decisions of deep networks by identifying the importance of input frames.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainable AI technique that decomposes the prediction of a neural network into contributions of individual input features.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An explainable artificial intelligence method that quantifies the contribution of individual neurons to a model's prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An interpretability method that decomposes a neural network's prediction to attribute importance to specific input pixels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An interpretability method that decomposes the prediction of a neural network by propagating relevance scores backward from the output to the input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An interpretability technique that decomposes the output of a neural network to attribute the prediction to specific input features.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#explainability_algorithm"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#learning_from_demonstration">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Learning From Demonstration</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach where an agent acquires a new skill by observing and imitating a human expert's behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach where an agent acquires a skill by observing and mimicking expert trajectories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm where an agent acquires a new skill by observing and imitating the behavior of a tutor.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm where an agent learns a behavior or policy by observing expert examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm where an agent learns a task by observing and imitating a teacher's behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm where an agent learns a task by observing and mimicking expert behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that extracts task constraints and control policies from a set of expert examples to guide autonomous systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology where a robot acquires a new skill by observing and mimicking expert examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology where a robot learns a nominal task plan by observing or being guided by a human operator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology where a system acquires a task policy by observing and imitating expert behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology where an agent acquires new skills by observing and imitating a teacher's behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A paradigm where a robot extracts control policies by observing and evaluating demonstrated behaviors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A paradigm where a system acquires a new skill or constraint by observing examples provided by an expert.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A paradigm where an agent acquires a behavior by observing and imitating a teacher's expert trajectories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A paradigm where an agent learns to perform a task by observing and imitating expert behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process where an agent acquires a behavioral policy by observing a teacher perform a task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach that learns a policy from expert or suboptimal demonstrations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach that leverages expert data to improve sample efficiency and convergence speed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach where an agent learns a policy by mapping visual demonstrations to its own state representation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotic learning approach where a model is acquired by observing a human teacher showing the robot how to perform a task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotic learning approach where a model is trained to perform a task by imitating examples provided by a human expert.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotic learning paradigm that enables an agent to acquire new skills by observing and imitating expert behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotic training approach where an agent acquires a skill by observing or being guided through a task by an expert.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotic training approach where an agent learns optimal policies by imitating expert human behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotic training method where an agent learns a desired behavior by observing a human expert's actions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotics approach where a system acquires new skills by observing and mimicking the behavior of a human teacher.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotics framework that enables agents to acquire new skills by observing demonstrations provided by human users.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotics methodology that derives control policies by imitating human-provided examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotics paradigm where an agent acquires a policy by imitating the behavior shown by a human expert.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotics paradigm where an agent learns to perform a task by observing human examples rather than through a reward function alone.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robotics training paradigm that enables agents to acquire new skills by imitating expert behaviors.</rdfs:comment>
