  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#adversarial_robustness">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Adversarial Robustness</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model property that ensures a system remains accurate when subjected to perturbed input samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model property that ensures consistent predictions despite the presence of small, malicious perturbations in input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A network design property that forces a model to reconstruct relevant image parts as proof of an object's presence to resist adversarial attacks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning model that describes its ability to maintain performance when faced with maliciously constructed inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning model that describes its ability to resist perturbations designed to cause incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning model that describes its ability to resist small, intentional perturbations to the input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning model that describes its resilience against small, intentional perturbations of input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning model that ensures its predictions remain stable despite the presence of realistic evasion attacks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning model that measures its resistance to small, intentional perturbations of input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning system that ensures it remains accurate and stable when facing unconstrained malicious inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model describing its ability to maintain performance when faced with intentionally perturbed inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that allows it to resist perturbations designed to cause incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that describes its ability to maintain performance when subjected to malicious input perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that describes its ability to resist malicious corruptions designed to cause misclassification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that describes its ability to resist perturbations in the input designed to cause incorrect classifications.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that describes its resistance to being fooled by adversarial examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that ensures consistent performance despite the presence of intentionally perturbed inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that ensures it maintains correct behavior when faced with maliciously perturbed input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that ensures it remains invariant to small, purposely designed perturbations of input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that ensures its output remains stable despite small, intentional perturbations to the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that ensures its prediction remains stable when subjected to intentionally perturbed inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that ensures its predictions remain stable in the presence of malicious perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that ensures stability and correct classification when inputs are subject to small perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that ensures stability of predictions against small, malicious perturbations of the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that ensures stable predictions when faced with maliciously crafted input perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that maintains accuracy when subjected to small, intentional perturbations of the input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a model that maintains correct predictions despite the presence of localized pixel perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a neural network that describes its ability to resist perturbations in input data to maintain correct predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a neural network that ensures it remains accurate and stable when subjected to intentionally perturbed input examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a neural network that ensures its predictions remain stable when subjected to small, intentionally crafted perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a neural network that measures its resistance to perturbations designed to cause misclassification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of deep neural networks that measures their ability to maintain performance when subjected to different types of perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A security property that ensures a model remains accurate despite the presence of intentionally crafted perturbations in the input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a classifier to maintain its performance when subjected to small, worst-case perturbations of the input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a classifier to maintain its prediction accuracy when subjected to small, intentional perturbations of the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a classifier to maintain its predictive accuracy when subjected to small, intentional perturbations of the input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a deep neural network to maintain correct predictions despite the presence of imperceptible adversarial perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain accurate predictions when subjected to intentional malicious perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain correct predictions despite small, intentionally malicious perturbations to the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain correct predictions when subjected to intentionally crafted malicious perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain correct predictions when subjected to intentionally perturbed inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain correct predictions when subjected to malicious input perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain its performance and correctness when subjected to intentionally perturbed inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain its performance and correctness when subjected to small, malicious perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain its performance when subjected to adversarial examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain its performance when subjected to adversarial perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain its performance when subjected to realistic or unrealistic adversarial examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain its performance when subjected to small, intentional perturbations of the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain its performance when subjected to small, intentionally crafted perturbations to the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain its performance when subjected to small, intentionally malicious perturbations of the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain its performance when subjected to small, intentionally perturbed inputs designed to cause misclassification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain performance when subjected to intentionally chosen input perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain performance when subjected to intentionally perturbed input instances.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to maintain performance when subjected to intentionally perturbed inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning model to resist perturbations in input data designed to cause incorrect predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning system to maintain its performance and resist manipulation when subjected to adversarial attacks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a machine learning system to maintain performance when subjected to malicious inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a model to maintain correct predictions when subjected to intentionally perturbed input examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a neural network to maintain correct classification when presented with perturbed inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability of a neural network to maintain correct predictions despite the presence of small, malicious input perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The capacity of a machine learning model to maintain correct predictions despite the presence of intentionally crafted perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The capacity of a model to maintain a consistent prediction despite small, intentional perturbations added to the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The capacity of a model to maintain correct predictions despite the presence of intentionally perturbed input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The capacity of a model to maintain correct predictions despite the presence of small, intentional perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The intrinsic property of a neural network to maintain stable predictions when subjected to adversarial perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The property of a classifier to remain accurate despite malicious perturbations to its input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The property of a machine learning model to maintain correct predictions when subjected to small, intentional perturbations of the input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The property of a machine learning model to maintain its performance when subjected to small, intentional perturbations of the input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The property of a machine learning model to maintain performance when subjected to intentionally perturbed input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The property of a model to maintain correct predictions despite the presence of imperceptible input perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The property of a model to maintain correct predictions despite the presence of intentionally perturbed input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The property of a model to maintain correct predictions when subjected to small, intentional perturbations in the input data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The property of a model to maintain correct predictions when subjected to small, intentional perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The property of a model to maintain its performance when subjected to small, intentionally perturbed inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[cause incorrect predictions] cause incorrect predictions</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[cause misclassification, cause incorrect classifications] misclassification</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[perturbations/malicious inputs] perturbations/malicious inputs</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[relevant image parts] relevant image parts</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[input data] input data</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[output/predictions] output/predictions</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model property that ensures a system remains accurate when subjected to perturbed input samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model property that ensures consistent predictions despite the presence of small, malicious perturbations in input data.</skos:definition>
