  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#model_interpretability">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Model Interpretability</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of machine learning focused on making the internal logic and decision-making process of a model transparent to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study aimed at creating tools and methods that make the internal decision-making processes of neural networks understandable to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on making the internal logic and predictions of black-box machine learning models understandable to humans.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on techniques that explain the reasoning behind the predictions made by a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for unraveling the black-box nature of neural networks by identifying the specific components of input data that drive predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of explaining the internal mechanisms of black-box models to identify the most influential features for a prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning system that allows humans to understand and explain the reasoning behind its predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning system that allows humans to understand the reasoning behind its predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of a system that allows humans to understand the cause of a decision made by a model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of machine learning models that allows humans to understand and assess the reasoning behind a prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A property of machine learning models that allows humans to understand the reasoning behind a prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A research area focused on developing tools and metrics to explain the decision-making process of black-box models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of methods used to explain the decisions and internal logic of complex predictive algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to explain the predictions of black-box machine learning models, specifically in the context of malware detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A strategy for querying black box models to understand behavior regarding robustness, fairness, and bias through input space pruning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The ability to explain and understand the internal mechanisms and decision-making processes of a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The degree to which a human can understand the cause of a decision made by a machine learning algorithm.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The degree to which a human can understand the cause of a decision made by a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[explain the decisions and internal logic of complex predictive algorithms] explain the decisions and internal logic of complex predictive algorithms</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[explain the predictions of black-box machine learning models] explain the predictions of black-box machine learning models</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[internal logic/decision-making process of models] internal logic/decision-making process of models</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[reasoning behind predictions] reasoning behind predictions</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the decision-making process] cause of a decision</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[black-box nature of neural networks] black-box nature of neural networks</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[cause of a decision, the reasoning/cause of a decision] cause of a decision</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A field of machine learning focused on making the internal logic and decision-making process of a model transparent to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A field of study aimed at creating tools and methods that make the internal decision-making processes of neural networks understandable to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on making the internal logic and predictions of black-box machine learning models understandable to humans.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A field of study focused on techniques that explain the reasoning behind the predictions made by a machine learning model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology for unraveling the black-box nature of neural networks by identifying the specific components of input data that drive predictions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of explaining the internal mechanisms of black-box models to identify the most influential features for a prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning system that allows humans to understand and explain the reasoning behind its predictions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A property of a machine learning system that allows humans to understand the reasoning behind its predictions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A property of a system that allows humans to understand the cause of a decision made by a model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A property of machine learning models that allows humans to understand and assess the reasoning behind a prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A property of machine learning models that allows humans to understand the reasoning behind a prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A research area focused on developing tools and metrics to explain the decision-making process of black-box models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of methods used to explain the decisions and internal logic of complex predictive algorithms.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to explain the predictions of black-box machine learning models, specifically in the context of malware detection.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A strategy for querying black box models to understand behavior regarding robustness, fairness, and bias through input space pruning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The ability to explain and understand the internal mechanisms and decision-making processes of a machine learning model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The degree to which a human can understand the cause of a decision made by a machine learning algorithm.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The degree to which a human can understand the cause of a decision made by a machine learning model.</skos:definition>
