  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#robust_principal_component_analysis">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Robust Principal Component Analysis</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimension reduction method that decomposes a matrix into a low-rank component and a sparse error component.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction algorithm designed to find the top eigenvector of a covariance matrix from corrupted data samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction method that decomposes a matrix into a low-rank component and a sparse noise component.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique designed to recover a low-rank matrix from data contaminated by outliers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique designed to recover a low-rank subspace from data containing outliers or contamination.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique designed to recover the low-rank structure of data in the presence of outliers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that decomposes a data matrix into a low-rank component and a sparse component to handle outliers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that decomposes a data matrix into low-rank and sparse components to handle outliers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that decomposes a data matrix into low-rank and sparse components to handle various types of corruption.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that identifies the low-rank subspace of a dataset while isolating column-sparse outliers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that recovers a low-rank matrix from data containing sparse corruptions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A low rank subspace recovery model designed to handle corrupted data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition method that separates a data matrix into a low-rank component and a sparse noise component.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition method that separates a data matrix into low-rank and sparse components while incorporating feature information for improved recovery.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition method that separates a low-rank representation from sparse noise to handle outliers in data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition method used to separate a low-rank component from a sparse component for denoising purposes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition technique that recovers a low-rank matrix from data corrupted by sparse noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition technique that recovers a low-rank matrix from data corrupted by sparse outliers and noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition technique that separates a data matrix into a low-rank component and a sparse component.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition technique that separates a data matrix into a low-rank component and a sparse error component.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition technique that separates a data matrix into low-rank and sparse components.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition technique that separates a low-rank matrix from a sparse error matrix.</rdfs:comment>
