  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#image_inpainting">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Image Inpainting</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computer vision process that reconstructs missing or corrupted regions of an image.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computer vision task that fills in missing or corrupted regions of an image to restore its original appearance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computer vision task that involves filling in missing or corrupted parts of an image.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computer vision task that involves reconstructing missing or corrupted regions of an image.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computer vision task that plausibly fills in missing regions of an image to estimate uncertainty or complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computer vision task that reconstructs missing or corrupted parts of an image based on the surrounding context.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computer vision task that reconstructs missing or removed parts of an image to create a seamless output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computer vision technique that reconstructs missing or corrupted parts of an image.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative task that uses deep learning models to predict and fill in missing or damaged regions of an image.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of reconstructing missing or masked regions of an image to create a realistic and consistent visual result.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to recover missing or corrupted parts of an image, applied here to handle errors in DNA-based data storage.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[recover missing or corrupted parts of an image] recover missing or corrupted parts of an image</rdfs:comment>
