  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#kernel_method">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Kernel Method</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms for analyzing data by mapping it into a high-dimensional feature space to find non-linear patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that map input data into high-dimensional feature spaces to perform linear operations on non-linear data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that maps data into high-dimensional spaces to perform non-linear analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that maps data into high-dimensional spaces to solve non-linear modeling problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that maps input data into high-dimensional feature spaces to enable linear separation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that project data into a higher-dimensional space to find a linear separation or regression surface.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that project data into higher-dimensional spaces to perform linear operations on non-linear patterns</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that project data into higher-dimensional spaces to perform linear operations on non-linear patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that project data into higher-dimensional spaces to perform linear operations on nonlinear data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that project data into higher-dimensional spaces to perform linear regression or classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that transforms data into a high-dimensional feature space to perform linear operations on non-linear patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that transforms input data into a higher-dimensional space to make non-linear patterns linearly separable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use a function to map data into a high-dimensional feature space for linear analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use a kernel function to map data into a high-dimensional space for linear separation or regression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use a kernel function to map data into a high-dimensional space for linear separation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use a kernel function to map data into a high-dimensional space for non-linear learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use a kernel function to map data into a high-dimensional space for tasks like classification and manifold learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use a kernel function to map data into a higher-dimensional space to perform linear separation or regression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use kernel functions to map data into high-dimensional spaces to perform regression or classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use kernel functions to map data into high-dimensional spaces, scaled here via doubly stochastic optimization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use kernel functions to map data into higher-dimensional spaces for easier pattern analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use kernel functions to operate in a high-dimensional feature space without explicitly computing the coordinates of the data in that space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use positive definite kernels to map data into high-dimensional feature spaces for linear analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that use pre-image decomposition in the original data space to achieve sparsity and scalability.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that uses a function to map data into high-dimensional spaces to facilitate linear separation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that uses a kernel function to map data into a higher-dimensional space for nonlinear estimation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that uses a kernel function to map input data into a high-dimensional feature space for non-linear analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of learning algorithms that use kernel functions to yield nonparametric estimators for high-dimensional data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning framework that uses Gram matrices and mean embeddings to handle partial rankings data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning framework that uses kernel functions to map data into high-dimensional spaces for linear separation or representation learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A nonparametric estimation technique that operates in a reproducing kernel hilbert space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A nonparametric learning algorithm that approximates continuous functions by mapping data into high-dimensional feature spaces.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique for on-line learning that maps data into a high-dimensional feature space to handle memory constraints in graph streams.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that embeds data into a high-dimensional Hilbert space to enable linear algorithms to solve non-linear problems.</rdfs:comment>
