    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method that predicts a target variable consisting of ordered categories.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that classifies instances into categories with a predefined natural order by projecting inputs onto a score scale.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that models the ordering information between different data categories.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that predicts a categorical variable with a natural ordering among its classes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that predicts a target variable consisting of ordered categories.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that predicts a target variable with a natural ordered relationship between categories.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that predicts a target variable with a predefined ordered set of categories.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that predicts a target variable with a predefined ranking or order.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that predicts a target variable with a predefined set of ordered categories.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that predicts an ordered category for a given input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A supervised learning task that predicts an ordered category for an instance, often optimized using concordance index or AUC.</skos:definition>
