  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#semi_supervised_clustering">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Semi-Supervised Clustering</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering approach that incorporates a small amount of labeled data or constraints to guide the grouping of unlabeled instances.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering approach that integrates a small amount of prior knowledge, such as constraints, to guide the grouping process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering approach that utilizes a small amount of labeled data or human queries to guide the grouping of unlabeled data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering method that incorporates a limited amount of user-provided pairwise constraints to guide the grouping process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A clustering method that incorporates a small amount of labeled data or constraints to guide the partitioning of a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A data-driven method that combines labeled and unlabeled data to uncover heterogeneous subtypes of a disease.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping method that combines unsupervised feature selection with a small amount of labeled data to refine cluster assignments.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping method that uses a small amount of labeled data to guide the partitioning of an unlabeled dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping task that utilizes a small amount of labeled data to improve the partition of unlabeled points.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping technique that leverages both unlabeled data and partial cluster information to partition a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A grouping technique that utilizes a small amount of labeled data alongside a large amount of unlabeled data to discover natural subgroups.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning approach that utilizes both labeled and unlabeled data to group similar objects.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning task that combines deep generative models and statistical relational models to group data using noisy pairwise comparisons from crowdsourcing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning method used to identify disease subtypes from heterogeneous imaging data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning task that performs multiclass labeling of unlabeled elements using a limited set of oracle queries.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised grouping task that utilizes a small amount of side information to guide the formation of clusters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning approach that utilizes a small amount of labeled data to guide the grouping of similar instances.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning task augmented with a small amount of prior knowledge in the form of pairwise constraints.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An unsupervised learning task that incorporates a small amount of labeled data or constraints to guide the grouping of similar objects.</rdfs:comment>
