  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#wasserstein_gan">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Wasserstein Gan</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial framework that uses a critic to measure the distance between real and fake distributions to improve convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that aims to minimize the Wasserstein distance between a real and a generated distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that minimizes the Earth Mover's distance to improve training convergence via a Lipschitz constraint.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that minimizes the Wasserstein distance between the real and generated data distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that uses a smooth metric to measure the distance between probability distributions for more stable training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that uses the Earth Mover's distance to improve training stability and convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that uses the Earth Mover's distance to provide more stable training and better convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that uses the Earth-Mover distance to improve training stability and image quality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that uses the Wasserstein distance as a metric between probability distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that uses the Wasserstein distance to improve training stability and convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that uses the Wasserstein distance to train a generator and detect overfitting via an independent critic.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that utilizes the 1-Lipschitz continuity of the discriminator to improve training stability and sample quality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network that utilizes the Earth Mover's distance to improve training stability and sample quality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network variant that uses the Earth Mover's distance to improve training stability and convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative adversarial network variant used for inverse problems to preserve image texture and pixel fidelity in medical imaging.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A variant of generative adversarial networks that uses the Earth Mover's distance to improve training stability and convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A variant of the generative adversarial network that uses the Earth Mover's distance to improve training stability and sample quality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a critic] critic</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a smooth metric] smooth metric</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[the earth-mover distance, Earth Mover's distance] earth-mover distance</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[inverse problems to preserve image texture and pixel fidelity in medical imaging] inverse problems to preserve image texture and pixel fidelity in medical imaging</rdfs:comment>
