    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A decision-making framework that seeks a policy that performs well under the worst-case scenario within an uncertainty set.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework for solving optimization problems where parameters are uncertain and an adversary chooses the least favorable values within a confidence set.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach to decision-making that accounts for uncertainty in the input data to ensure stability.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach to decision-making that seeks a solution that remains effective under worst-case uncertainty.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach to model uncertainty by ensuring that the solution remains effective under the worst-case scenario.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach used to ensure fairness criteria are satisfied even when protected group labels are noisy or biased.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for decision-making under uncertainty that uses predictive models to weight data-driven uncertainty sets.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for optimizing a function under uncertainty, ensuring the solution remains effective across a a range of possible values.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for optimizing a system while accounting for uncertainty in the input data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for optimizing a system while accounting for uncertainty in the input parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for solving optimization problems where some of the input data is uncertain or unreliable.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for solving optimization problems where the parameters are subject to uncertainty or adversarial perturbations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for training classifiers to be resilient against worst-case adversarial perturbations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that aims to improve the worst-case performance of a model across different data groups.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that aims to learn a model optimized for the worst-case adversarial distribution across multiple domains.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that incorporates uncertainty into a model by optimizing against the worst-case perturbation of input data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that optimizes for the worst-case scenario given uncertainty in the constraints.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that seeks an optimal solution while accounting for uncertainty in the input data to ensure a guaranteed performance level.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that seeks optimal solutions that remain effective despite uncertainty or variability in input parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to train neural networks to be resistant to adversarial examples by optimizing for the worst-case perturbation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical optimization framework that accounts for uncertainty in data to provide reliable bounds on causal effects.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology for solving optimization problems that account for uncertainty in the input parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A tool for enforcing priors on learned features in deep neural networks to improve representation invertibility and visualization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A training approach that favors flat areas of the loss landscape to improve generalization and robustness against adversarial perturbations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization approach that seeks to find a solution that performs well under the worst-case scenario within a class of objective functions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization framework that builds models resistant to misclassification caused by small perturbations or adversarial attacks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization framework that incorporates uncertainty sets to ensure the solution remains feasible or optimal under worst-case scenarios.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization strategy that seeks a solution performing well against the worst-case realization of uncertain parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An optimization strategy that seeks a solution that remains effective under the worst-case scenario of parameter uncertainty.</skos:definition>
