    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A self-exciting point process where the occurrence of an event increases the probability of future events occurring.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A self-exciting point process where the occurrence of an event increases the probability of future events.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A stochastic point process model that explicitly captures self- and mutually-triggering patterns between events in sequences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A stochastic point process used to model self-exciting temporal events, such as pandemic-related social unrest.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A stochastic point process used to model the spatiotemporal risk of disease transmission based on high-resolution mobility data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A stochastic point process where the occurrence of an event increases the probability of future events occurring.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A stochastic point process where the occurrence of an event increases the probability of future events.</rdfs:comment>
