  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#adversarial_imitation_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Adversarial Imitation Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for generating high-dimensional event sequences by training a generator to imitate a process and a discriminator to distinguish real from fake sequences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for learning a policy from expert demonstrations by treating the problem as a GAN-like competition between a generator and a discriminator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for learning a policy from expert demonstrations by using a discriminator to distinguish between expert and agent behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for training an agent to mimic an expert's behavior by using a discriminator to distinguish agent and expert trajectories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that alternates between a discriminator and a generator to produce trajectories that mimic expert behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for learning a policy from expert demonstrations using a discriminator to distinguish between expert and agent behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of learning a policy from expert demonstrations by using a discriminator to distinguish between agent and expert behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that trains an agent to mimic expert behavior by using a discriminator as a reward signal.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that trains an agent to mimic expert behavior by using an adversarial framework to distinguish between agent and expert trajectories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that uses a discriminator to learn a reward function from expert demonstrations for reinforcement learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that uses generative adversarial networks to learn control policies by mimicking expert demonstrations from raw video data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach that uses expert demonstrations to replace dense reward functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning approach where a policy is trained to mimic expert behavior by fooling a discriminator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that learns a policy by training a discriminator to distinguish between expert and agent behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that uses a discriminator to minimize the divergence between expert trajectories and agent behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning method that learns a policy by training a discriminator to distinguish between expert and agent behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning technique that learns adaptive policies by imitating expert demonstrations using a discriminator to distinguish between agent and expert behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning technique where an agent learns a policy by trying to fool a discriminator into thinking its behavior is from an expert.</rdfs:comment>
