    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of learning low-dimensional features from high-dimensional environment observations to facilitate agent control and policy learning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of mapping raw observations into a lower-dimensional latent space to facilitate robotic planning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process that encodes raw sensory input into a compact latent space to facilitate the learning of complex skills in reinforcement learning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The process of discovering a compact and efficient latent encoding of raw sensory inputs to facilitate downstream task learning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The process of extracting a concise, latent description of an environment from high-dimensional raw observations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The process of learning a compact and useful latent space from raw sensory observations to facilitate agent exploration and task performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The process of learning a compact embedding of an environment's state space to improve the efficiency of reinforcement learning agents.</skos:definition>
