  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#statistical_learning_theory">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Statistical Learning Theory</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for analyzing the performance and generalization of machine learning algorithms based on probability and statistics.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that analyzes the performance and generalization capabilities of learning algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that provides the basis for decision making and model construction from data sets.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework for analyzing the generalization of algorithms when data dependency is characterized by a graph.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework providing guarantees for supervised machine learning based on the empirical risk minimization principle.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that analyzes the conditions under which learning algorithms achieve fast rates of convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that analyzes the excess risk and generalization properties of learning algorithms using probability distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that analyzes the generalization performance of learning algorithms based on data distributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that provides mathematical guarantees on the generalization ability of learning machines, including compressed predictors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that provides principles for generalizing from a finite set of training data to unseen examples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that provides the mathematical foundations for analyzing the generalization ability of supervised learning algorithms.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework used to build predictive models for coupled demand nexus based on climate-sensitive variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework used to study the convergence and complexity of classification algorithms through shattering coefficients.</rdfs:comment>
