    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that provides mathematical guarantees on the generalization ability of learning machines, including compressed predictors.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that provides principles for generalizing from a finite set of training data to unseen examples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework that provides the mathematical foundations for analyzing the generalization ability of supervised learning algorithms.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework used to build predictive models for coupled demand nexus based on climate-sensitive variables.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A theoretical framework used to study the convergence and complexity of classification algorithms through shattering coefficients.</skos:definition>
