    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical model that represents observed data through unobserved variables to account for hidden variations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical model that represents observed variables as functions of a set of hidden variables to capture underlying data structures.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical representation that explains observed data through the influence of hidden, unmeasured causes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical tool for analyzing neural activity that infers hidden states without depending on known relationships between activity and external variables.</skos:definition>
