  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#reproducing_kernel_hilbert_space">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Reproducing Kernel Hilbert Space</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Hilbert space of functions in which point evaluation is a continuous linear functional.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Hilbert space of functions in which the evaluation functional is continuous and represented by a kernel.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Hilbert space of functions in which the evaluation functional is continuous for every point in the domain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Hilbert space of functions in which the evaluation functional is continuous, used for nonparametric representation of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A complete inner product space of functions where point evaluation is a continuous linear functional.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A complete inner product space of functions where the evaluation functional is continuous.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A functional analysis framework that enables the mapping of data into high-dimensional spaces to find linear solutions to nonlinear problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A functional analysis framework that enables the mapping of non-linear data into a high-dimensional space for linear processing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A functional space associated with a positive definite kernel used for generating multiscale approximations and sparse representations of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A functional space associated with a positive definite kernel where point evaluation is a continuous linear functional.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A functional space characterized by kernels that allow the evaluation of linear functionals via inner products.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A functional space in one-to-one correspondence with positive semidefinite kernels used for linear system identification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A functional space of inner product kernels where the evaluation functional is continuous.</rdfs:comment>
