  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#sparse_neural_network">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sparse Neural Network</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that leverages activation sparsity to reduce energy consumption and execution cycles.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning model where a significant portion of the weights are set to zero to reduce storage and computational requirements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model architecture designed to utilize actual sparse matrix operations to improve training efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model architecture that utilizes a predefined graph topology to reduce the number of active connections between neurons.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model architecture that utilizes sparse computations and parameter selection to reduce the number of active weights for efficiency and compression.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model architecture where a significant portion of the weights are set to zero to improve efficiency and generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model architecture where a significant portion of the weights or connections are set to zero to improve generalization and efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model architecture where a significant portion of weights are zero to reduce computational cost.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model architecture where many weights or activations are zero to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model architecture where most of the weights are zeroed to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model where a significant portion of the weights are set to zero to reduce memory and computational costs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model where a significant portion of the weights are zero, reducing resource requirements for deployment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A network architecture that reduces computational cost by activating only a small subset of its parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A network architecture that utilizes a limited number of active connections to reduce memory requirements while maintaining performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A network architecture where most of the weights are zero, reducing computational complexity and memory usage.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A network architecture where only a subset of weights are non-zero to improve efficiency and reduce parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where a significant portion of the parameters are set to zero to reduce model size and computational cost.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where a significant portion of the weights are set to zero to reduce complexity and computational cost.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where a significant portion of the weights are zero to reduce computational and memory requirements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where a significant portion of the weights are zero, reducing computational complexity and memory usage.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where a significant portion of the weights are zero, reducing compute and storage requirements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture where a significant portion of the weights are zero, reducing memory and computational requirements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network topology where many edges are removed to reduce storage and runtime costs while maintaining precision.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network where a significant portion of the weights are zero, reducing the number of parameters and computational requirements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of artificial neural network where a significant portion of the weights are set to zero to reduce model size.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An artificial network architecture where a significant portion of the weights are zero to increase efficiency and generalization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[utilize actual sparse matrix operations to improve training efficiency] utilize actual sparse matrix operations to improve training efficiency</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a predefined graph topology] graph topology</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[sparse computations and parameter selection] sparse computations and parameter selection</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a limited number of active connections] limited number of active connections</rdfs:comment>
