  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#uncertaintyquantification">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Uncertaintyquantification</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational process that assesses the reliability and potential error of predictions made by machine learning models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational process that characterizes the amount of uncertainty in the outputs of a mathematical model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational process that characterizes the confidence levels of predictions made by a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A computational process used to characterize the uncertainty in the predictions of a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach to characterize the amount of uncertainty in the output of a predictive model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical process of characterizing the amount of uncertainty in a model's estimates or predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical process that characterizes the likelihood and magnitude of errors in predictive models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for estimating the error of machine learning predictions in phase space to support active learning and resilient simulations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodological process that characterizes the degree of confidence or doubt associated with a model's prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for characterizing the amount of doubt or variability associated with a model's prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for measuring the confidence or reliability of a model's prediction to identify potential errors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that characterizes the reliability or confidence levels associated with a model's prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that distinguishes and measures aleatoric and epistemic randomness in model predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that measures the confidence or reliability of a model's predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology used to characterize the confidence or reliability of a model's predictions, especially under distribution shift.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology used to characterize the confidence or reliability of a model's predictive output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A modeling process that distinguishes between aleatoric and epistemic uncertainty to identify out-of-distribution samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process for assessing the predictive ability of AI algorithms by describing the entire predictive distribution of a target variable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process in machine learning that estimates the confidence or reliability of a model's predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the amount of doubt or confidence associated with a predictive model's output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the amount of uncertainty in the predictions made by a statistical or machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the confidence levels of a model's predictions to identify when it encounters unfamiliar data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the confidence levels of a model's predictions to improve safety and reliability.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the confidence of a model's prediction to detect adversarial perturbations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the confidence or variance associated with the predictions of a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the degree of confidence or potential error associated with a model's prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the different sources of error or unpredictability in the output of a predictive model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the level of confidence or doubt associated with a model's prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the reliability of a model's prediction by estimating the probability distribution of the output.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the reliability of a model's predictions by estimating the confidence levels of its outputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of characterizing the total error and confidence levels in neural network-based inference.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of estimating the confidence levels associated with a model's point predictions to improve reliability and fairness.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of estimating the confidence of a model's prediction by sampling from stochastic discrete state transitions over recurrent timesteps.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of estimating the confidence of model predictions using functional operators over the projection of weights in a reproducing kernel Hilbert space.</rdfs:comment>
