    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation of a high-dimensional object used to capture semantic similarities.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation of discrete entities like users and items in a shared space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation of discrete entities that captures semantic relationships between them in a continuous space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation of discrete entities that captures semantic relationships between them.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation of high-dimensional data that maps similar items to nearby points in a vector space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation of high-dimensional data that preserves semantic or syntactic similarities.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation of high-dimensional data used to capture semantic relationships.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation of high-dimensional discrete data that captures semantic similarity.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation of high-dimensional discrete data that preserves semantic relationships.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation that captures the semantic characteristics of a high-dimensional object.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation that captures the semantic meaning of discrete data entities.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A low-dimensional vector representation that captures the semantic meaning of discrete entities based on their context.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A real-valued vector representation of discrete entities used to capture latent structures in large datasets.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation of discrete entities as continuous low-dimensional vectors in a latent space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation of high-dimensional discrete data as dense vectors of real numbers.</skos:definition>
