    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A population-based metaheuristic optimization method inspired by biological evolution, involving mutation, crossover, and selection.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A population-based metaheuristic optimization method inspired by biological evolution.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A population-based metaheuristic optimization technique used for estimating hyperparameters of a kernel-based model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A population-based optimization method inspired by biological evolution that uses mutation, crossover, and selection to find optimal solutions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A population-based optimization method inspired by biological evolution used to find optimal solutions in complex search spaces.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A population-based optimization method inspired by biological evolution used to search for optimal parameters or architectures.</skos:definition>
