    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning algorithm used to train controllers by reducing overestimation bias in Q-value updates.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning architecture that reduces overestimation bias by using two separate networks to select and evaluate actions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning architecture that reduces overestimation bias of action values by using two separate neural networks to select and evaluate actions.</skos:definition>
