  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#gradient_compression">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Gradient Compression</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A communication-efficiency technique in distributed deep learning that reduces the volume of gradient updates sent between workers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A communication-efficiency technique that reduces the size of gradient updates transmitted during distributed training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A communication-efficient method that reduces the amount of data transmitted during distributed training of neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A communication-efficient technique that reduces the precision or volume of gradient updates sent between distributed computing nodes.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A communication-reduction method that reduces the size of gradient updates transmitted during distributed training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A communication-reduction technique in distributed training that uses sparsification or quantization to reduce the size of model updates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distributed learning technique that reduces the communication overhead by compressing model updates during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for reducing the amount of data transferred between learners in distributed deep learning.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method used in distributed training to reduce the amount of data transmitted between nodes by approximating the gradient updates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method used in distributed training to reduce the amount of data transmitted between workers and parameter servers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method used in distributed training to reduce the communication overhead by reducing the size of gradient vectors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method used in distributed training to reduce the communication overhead by shrinking the volume of gradient data transmitted.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique in distributed learning that reduces the amount of data transmitted between nodes to alleviate communication bottlenecks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique in distributed learning that reduces the communication overhead by quantizing or sparsifying gradients transmitted between workers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique in distributed learning used to reduce the communication overhead of stochastic gradient descent.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that reduces the amount of data transmitted during distributed training of deep neural networks to overcome communication bottlenecks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in distributed learning to reduce communication overhead by reducing the size of gradients transmitted between workers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in distributed learning to reduce the amount of data transmitted between nodes during model updates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in distributed learning to reduce the amount of data transmitted between workers and a server by selecting or modulating gradients.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in distributed optimization to reduce the amount of data transmitted between nodes by compressing the gradient vectors.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in distributed training to reduce communication costs by sparsifying or quantizing stochastic gradients.</rdfs:comment>
