  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#residual_neural_network">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Residual Neural Network</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of neural networks that can be interpreted as a time-discretized ordinary differential equation for processing large amounts of data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep architecture that uses shortcut connections to bypass one or more layers to mitigate the vanishing gradient problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep architecture that utilizes shortcut connections to enable the training of very deep networks for signal classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that employs shortcut connections to allow gradients to flow through the network more easily, mitigating the vanishing gradient problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that employs shortcut connections to allow gradients to flow through the network more easily.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that employs skip connections to alleviate the vanishing gradient problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses residual convolutional units to model temporal properties of time series data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses shortcut connections to facilitate the training of very deep models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses skip connections to allow gradients to flow more easily through the network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses skip connections to allow gradients to flow more easily through very deep networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses skip connections to allow gradients to flow through very deep networks more easily.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses skip connections to allow gradients to flow through very deep networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses skip connections to allow the training of very deep networks by mitigating the vanishing gradient problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses skip connections to allow the training of very deep networks for signal classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses skip connections to facilitate the training of very deep networks for image classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses skip connections to mitigate the vanishing gradient problem during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that uses skip connections to model temporal and spatial properties of crowd traffic flows.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that utilizes shortcut connections to enable the training of very deep networks by learning residual functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture that utilizes shortcut connections to enable the universal approximation of continuous functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture using skip connections to detect and classify malware traffic from visual representations of network packets.</rdfs:comment>
