  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#generative_adversarial_imitation_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Generative Adversarial Imitation Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for learning sequential decision-making policies by utilizing expert demonstration data to learn both the policy and reward function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework for text generation that uses pre-trained language models to provide reward guidance for a discriminator.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that combines adversarial training with imitation learning to model agent behavior from observed trajectories.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns a policy and a reward function simultaneously from expert demonstrations using an adversarial structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns a policy by imitating expert behavior using a generative adversarial network structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns a policy by matching the distribution of state-action trajectories from expert demonstrations using a GAN-like structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns a policy by matching the occupancy measure of an expert using a GAN-like structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns a policy by matching the occupancy measure of an expert using a generative adversarial network structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns a policy by matching the occupancy measure of an expert's state-action distribution using a GAN-like structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns a policy from expert demonstrations by recovering a cost function using an adversarial process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns a policy from expert demonstrations by using a generative adversarial network to match the expert's state-action distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns model parameters for generative processes by imitating expert behavior through an adversarial game.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that learns to predict complex trajectories by imitating the behavior of human experts.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that mimics expert behavior by training a generator to produce trajectories indistinguishable from expert demonstrations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that trains a policy to mimic expert demonstrations by using a GAN-like structure to distinguish between expert and agent behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that uses a generative adversarial network to recover an expert policy from demonstrations by matching the occupancy measure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that uses adversarial optimization to recover a policy from expert demonstrations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that learns a control policy from expert demonstrations by matching the occupancy measure of the agent to the expert.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A minimax optimization framework used to recover an optimal policy and reward function from expert demonstrations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that enables the training of policies to mimic human-like behavior from limited demonstrations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that learns a policy by mimicking expert demonstrations using an adversarial objective.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that learns a policy by recovering a reward function from expert demonstrations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A reinforcement learning framework that trains policies to mimic expert trajectories without an explicit reward function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A robot learning framework that enables an agent to learn a policy and a reward function from expert demonstrations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An approach to policy learning that uses a GAN-like framework to make agent behavior indistinguishable from expert demonstrations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An imitation learning framework that uses a GAN-like structure to match the state distribution of an expert.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An imitation learning framework that uses adversarial training to recover a reward function from expert demonstrations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An inverse reinforcement learning method that recovers a reward function and policy by matching expert trajectory distributions.</rdfs:comment>
