    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural representation used to synthesize photorealistic novel views of real-world 3D scenes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural scene representation that learns geometry and appearance from 2D images to synthesize high-fidelity dynamic humans from arbitrary viewpoints.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation method that uses a neural network to map 3D coordinates and viewing directions to color and density for scene reconstruction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation of a 3D scene that uses a neural network to map coordinates and viewing directions to color and density.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation technique that uses a neural network to encode 3D scenes as a continuous volumetric function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation that uses a multilayer perceptron to model the volumetric density and color of a 3D scene.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation that uses a neural network to encode a 3D scene as a continuous volumetric function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A scene representation that uses a neural network to support high-quality view synthesis and 3D editing.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A volume-rendering technique that uses a neural network to synthesize novel views of 3D scenes.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A volumetric representation that synthesizes 3D object geometry and color from 2D images.</skos:definition>
