    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that uses parameterized quantum gates to approximate functions for machine learning tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical architecture used to optimize parameters for solving complex physical Hamiltonians.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical model that optimizes parameters of a gate-based circuit to solve combinatorial problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical neural network that optimizes parameters within a quantum circuit to perform learning tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A parameterized quantum algorithm that is optimized using classical gradient-based techniques.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A parameterized quantum circuit that can be optimized using classical gradients to perform machine learning tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A parameterized quantum circuit used as a trainable component within a quantum neural network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A quantum computing architecture that uses parameterized circuits to approximate functions for deep learning tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A quantum computing architecture that uses parameterized circuits to approximate functions or optimize objectives.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A quantum computing architecture that uses parameterized circuits to perform supervised learning tasks through simultaneous training with classical components.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A quantum computing architecture that uses parameterized gates and is trained using classical optimization to perform machine learning tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A quantum computing architecture that uses parameterized gates to be optimized via classical gradient-based techniques.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A quantum computing architecture that uses parameterized layers to approximate the ground states of Hamiltonians through optimization.</rdfs:comment>
