    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for solving inverse problems where one optimization problem is nested within another to learn regularization parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework for solving optimization problems where one optimization problem is nested within another.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that optimizes a higher-level objective function subject to the constraint that a lower-level optimization problem must be solved.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that optimizes a primary objective function subject to an optimization problem as a constraint.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that solves two nested optimization problems where the upper-level objective depends on the solution of the lower-level problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework used to learn data augmentation strategies by optimizing a base model's performance on a validation set.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework where one optimization problem is embedded as a constraint within another optimization problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework where one optimization problem is nested as a constraint within another optimization problem.</rdfs:comment>
