  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#item_response_theory">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Item Response Theory</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generative probabilistic paradigm used to quantify latent traits of individuals based on their responses to test items.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic framework used to estimate the latent traits of an individual based on their responses to test items.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to design and analyze tests by relating the observed performance of a person to their latent trait.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A probabilistic model used to estimate the latent ability of a person and the difficulty of a test item.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A psychometric framework that estimates examinee and item logits using maximum likelihood methods and probabilities of matrix elements.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A psychometric framework that estimates the ability of a classifier based on its performance on test instances of varying difficulty.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A psychometric framework that estimates the latent traits of a person based on their performance on test items of varying difficulty.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A psychometric framework that models the relationship between a person's latent traits and their responses to test items.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A psychometric framework that uses mathematical models to estimate the latent abilities of examinees and the difficulty of test items.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A psychometric framework used to estimate dataset difficulty and classifier ability to evaluate the quality of machine learning benchmarks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A psychometric framework used to estimate latent traits or scores based on the patterns of binary responses.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A psychometric framework used to estimate the difficulty and discrimination parameters of test questions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A psychometric model that relates the ability of an examinee to the difficulty and discrimination of a test item.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A psychometric modeling framework used to estimate latent traits to weight and combine multiple unsupervised anomaly detection methods.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[quantify latent traits of individuals based on their responses to test items, estimate the latent traits of an individual based on their responses to test items, design and analyze tests by relating the observed performance of a person to their latent trait, estimate the latent ability of a person and the difficulty of a test item] estimate the latent ability of a person and the difficulty of a test item</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[maximum likelihood methods and probabilities of matrix elements] maximum likelihood methods and probabilities of matrix elements</rdfs:comment>
