  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#reinforcement_learning_environment">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Reinforcement Learning Environment</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A simulated framework that allows an agent to interact and learn through trial and error within a specific domain.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A simulated framework that provides observations, actions, and rewards for training autonomous agents.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A simulated framework where an agent learns to make decisions by interacting with a dynamic system to maximize rewards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A simulated platform that allows agents to interact with a system to learn optimal behaviors through trial and error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A simulated setting that provides a framework for building and evaluating agents through interaction and reward.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A simulated setting that provides a framework for training agents through interaction and photorealistic rendering.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A simulated setting that provides a task and feedback mechanism for training autonomous agents to maximize rewards.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A simulated setting that provides observations, actions, and rewards to train agents to solve complex tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A simulated setting where agents learn optimal behaviors through trial and error and reward signals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A simulated testbed used to train autonomous cyber agents by balancing fidelity and simplicity within a specific action space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A software toolkit that provides simulated settings for training agents through trial and error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[train autonomous cyber agents by balancing fidelity and simplicity within a specific action space] train autonomous cyber agents by balancing fidelity and simplicity within a specific action space</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[agent] agent</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[framework/observations/rewards] framework/observations/rewards</rdfs:comment>
