  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#multiviewlearning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Multiviewlearning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning framework that leverages multiple distinct sets of feature representations to improve predictive performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning paradigm that integrates complementary information from multiple distinct data sources or representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning problem that utilizes various representations of an object to mine valuable knowledge and improve algorithm performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A learning task that integrates multiple different representations of the same data to improve model performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that acquires information from multiple feature sets to improve classification accuracy and efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that improves performance by utilizing diversity from different data views, such as amplitude and phase features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that integrates complementary information from multiple different data sources or perspectives.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that integrates information from multiple different perspectives or sensors to improve task performance.</rdfs:comment>
