  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#lineardynamicalsystem">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Lineardynamicalsystem</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical framework that models the evolution of a system's state over time using linear transformations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model that describes a system's evolution over time using linear differential or difference equations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model that describes the evolution of a state over time using linear equations and Gaussian noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model that describes the evolution of a state over time using linear equations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model that describes the evolution of a state over time using linear transformations and additive noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model that describes the evolution of a state over time using linear transformations and stochastic noise.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model that describes the evolution of a state over time using linear transformations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model used for time-series forecasting that describes the evolution of a state over time using linear equations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical model where the state evolves according to linear transformations of the current state and input.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A parametric model class used to identify the eigenspectrum of unknown dynamics for time series clustering.</rdfs:comment>
