    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dynamic Time Warping</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A comparison measure used to calculate the similarity between two temporal sequences that may vary in speed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dissimilarity measure that aligns two time series by stretching or compressing them in time to find an optimal match.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A distance function used to compare and measure similarity between two time series sequences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A similarity measure used to find the optimal alignment between two time-series sequences.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that aligns two time-series sequences by stretching or compressing them to find an optimal match.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that dynamically aligns two sequences by finding the minimal distance matching under constraints to overcome temporal distortion.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to classify different types of artifacts in EEG signals to enable brain-computer interface control for persons with motor disabilities.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A time series alignment technique that finds an optimal match between two sequences by stretching or shrinking them in time.</rdfs:comment>
