  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#shap_shapley_additive_explanations">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Shap (Shapley Additive Explanations)</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A game theoretic approach used to explain the output of any machine learning model by assigning importance values to each feature.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A game theory-based framework used to explain the output of any supervised learning model by assigning importance values to each feature.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A game theory-based framework used to explain the output of machine learning models by attributing feature contributions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A game-theoretic approach to explain the output of any machine learning model by assigning each feature an importance value.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A game-theoretic approach to explain the output of any machine learning model by assigning importance values to each feature.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A game-theoretic approach used to explain the output of any machine learning model by attributing importance to each feature.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A game-theoretic approach used to explain the output of any machine learning model by attributing importance to features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A game-theoretic framework that assigns each feature a value representing its contribution to a model's prediction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A game-theoretic method used for the local explanation of a black-box model's predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A post-hoc interpretability method that assigns each feature an importance value for a particular prediction based on cooperative game theory.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A unified framework for interpreting model predictions by assigning each feature an importance value based on additive feature importance measures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An explainability method that assigns each feature an importance value based on cooperative game theory.</rdfs:comment>
