  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#graph_pooling">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Graph Pooling</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction operation for graph neural networks that aggregates nodes into a coarser representation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction operation in graph neural networks that coarsens the graph structure to extract higher-level features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction process in graph neural networks that aggregates node features to construct a coarser graph topology.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction process that aggregates node and edge information into a fixed-size representation for graph-level tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction process that aggregates nodes in a graph to create a hierarchical representation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that aggregates local substructures to learn graph-level representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A downsampling methodology used in graph neural networks to generate a graph-level representation by summarizing node features.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A downsampling operation for graph data that uses self-attention to consider both node features and graph topology.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A graph machine learning operator used to reduce the size of graphs through selection, reduction, and connection operations.</rdfs:comment>
