    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture used to learn efficient codings of input data for tasks like vector reconstruction and retrieval.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture used to learn the optimal mapping between all-atom and reduced representations in coarse-graining simulations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network designed to learn a compressed representation of input data by attempting to reconstruct the original input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network designed to learn a compressed representation of input data for reconstruction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network designed to learn a compressed, disentangled representation of input data, such as timbre, for synthesis.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network designed to learn efficient codings of input data by reconstructing the input at the output layer.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network designed to learn efficient data codings by attempting to reconstruct its input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network designed to learn efficient data codings in an unsupervised manner by reconstructing its input.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network designed to learn efficient data codings in an unsupervised manner by reconstructing the input at the output.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network designed to learn efficient data codings in an unsupervised manner.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network framework used to design channel encoders and decoders for reliable data transmission over noisy channels.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network structure designed to define a conservative vector field associated with an energy function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network used for non-linear feature reduction to compress information into a smaller feature space for price trend prediction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network used for unsupervised representation learning that is regularized here using a clustering algorithm.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network used to learn efficient codings of input data by attempting to reconstruct the original input from a reduced representation.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A representation learning tool that maps data from a high-dimensional space to a latent space while preserving specific properties like local distances.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of neural network used to learn efficient codings of input data by reconstructing the input at its output layer.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of neural network used to learn efficient codings of input data by training the network to ignore signal noise.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A type of neural network used to learn efficient data codings in an unsupervised manner.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An unsupervised neural network that learns a compressed representation of input data through an encoding and decoding process.</skos:definition>
