  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#zeroth_order_optimization">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Zeroth-Order Optimization</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of algorithms that optimize a function using only its value rather than its gradient information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of optimization algorithms that estimate gradients using only function evaluations rather than explicit derivative information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A derivative-free method that estimates gradients using only function evaluations rather than explicit backpropagation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A derivative-free method that minimizes objective functions using only function evaluations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A derivative-free optimization method that estimates the objective function's gradient using only function evaluations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A derivative-free optimization method used to optimize photonic circuit configurations under resource and power constraints.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A derivative-free optimization technique that estimates gradients using only function evaluations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A global optimization method for non-convex smooth functions that relies solely on noisy evaluations of function values without gradient information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gradient-free algorithm that estimates objective function derivatives using only function value evaluations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gradient-free optimization method that optimizes a function using only its value outputs, enabling the use of black-box knowledge sources.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gradient-free optimization method that relies exclusively on function evaluations to find a solution.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gradient-free optimization method that relies solely on function evaluations to find the minimum of a target objective.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gradient-free optimization technique that estimates derivatives using only function evaluations through parameter perturbation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach for minimizing a function using only function evaluations rather than gradient information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach to finding a function's extremum using only function values without calculating derivatives.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical approach to finding the minimum of a function using only function evaluations rather than gradient information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical process for minimizing an objective function using only evaluations of the function without access to gradient information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization method that estimates the gradient of an objective function using only function value queries.</rdfs:comment>
