  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#network_compression">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Network Compression</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method to reduce the size and computational requirements of deep learning models through iterative pruning and simulation of the reduced network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that reduces the number of parameters in a deep neural network to decrease memory usage and latency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that reduces the size and complexity of deep learning models to improve efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of reducing the number of parameters and computational requirements of a neural network while maintaining its performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of reducing the size and complexity of a neural network while maintaining its original functionality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of reducing the size and complexity of a neural network while maintaining its performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of reducing the size or complexity of a network while attempting to maintain its original functional properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process that reduces the complexity and memory footprint of a deep learning model through quantization and sparsity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process that reduces the size of a neural network by removing redundant units or layers while maintaining its output behavior.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques including matrix factorization and tensor decomposition used to reduce the size and runtime of deep models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to reduce the memory footprint and computational requirements of a deep neural network while maintaining accuracy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to reduce the size and computational cost of neural networks while maintaining accuracy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to reduce the size and computational requirements of deep neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to reduce the size and parameter count of a neural network while maintaining its predictive power.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques, including pruning and quantization, used to reduce the size and energy consumption of deep learning models for edge deployment.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques, such as pruning and quantization, used to reduce the memory and computational requirements of deep neural networks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that reduces the memory and computational requirements of neural networks without sacrificing accuracy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[reduce the size and runtime of deep models, reduce the memory footprint and computational requirements of a deep neural network while maintaining accuracy, reduce the size and computational cost of neural networks while maintaining accuracy, reduce the size and computational requirements of deep neural networks, reduce the memory and computational requirements of deep neural networks] reduce the size and runtime of deep models</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[reduce the size and parameter count of a neural network while maintaining its predictive power] reduce the size and parameter count of a neural network while maintaining its predictive power</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[reduce the size and energy consumption of deep learning models for edge deployment] reduce the size and energy consumption of deep learning models for edge deployment</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[deep learning models/neural networks] deep learning models/neural networks</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method to reduce the size and computational requirements of deep learning models through iterative pruning and simulation of the reduced network.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that reduces the number of parameters in a deep neural network to decrease memory usage and latency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology that reduces the size and complexity of deep learning models to improve efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of reducing the number of parameters and computational requirements of a neural network while maintaining its performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of reducing the size and complexity of a neural network while maintaining its original functionality.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of reducing the size and complexity of a neural network while maintaining its performance.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process of reducing the size or complexity of a network while attempting to maintain its original functional properties.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process that reduces the complexity and memory footprint of a deep learning model through quantization and sparsity.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A process that reduces the size of a neural network by removing redundant units or layers while maintaining its output behavior.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of techniques including matrix factorization and tensor decomposition used to reduce the size and runtime of deep models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to reduce the memory footprint and computational requirements of a deep neural network while maintaining accuracy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to reduce the size and computational cost of neural networks while maintaining accuracy.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to reduce the size and computational requirements of deep neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to reduce the size and parameter count of a neural network while maintaining its predictive power.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of techniques, including pruning and quantization, used to reduce the size and energy consumption of deep learning models for edge deployment.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of techniques, such as pruning and quantization, used to reduce the memory and computational requirements of deep neural networks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A technique that reduces the memory and computational requirements of neural networks without sacrificing accuracy.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#ml_training_and_optimization_protocol"/>
  </rdf:Description>
