  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#variance_reduction">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Variance Reduction</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of optimization techniques designed to accelerate the convergence of stochastic gradient methods.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of optimization techniques used to reduce the noise in stochastic gradient estimates to accelerate convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class of stochastic optimization techniques designed to accelerate convergence by reducing the noise of gradient estimates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A family of optimization techniques designed to decrease the noise in stochastic gradient estimates to accelerate convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of optimization techniques used to accelerate the convergence of stochastic gradient descent by reducing the noise in gradient estimates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to decrease the noise in gradient estimators for models with discrete latent variables to speed up convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to decrease the finite sample variance of additive functionals of Markov chains.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical technique used in Monte Carlo synthesis to decrease the noise and improve the accuracy of pixel estimates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical technique used in gradient estimation to reduce the noise of stochastic approximations for more stable training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical technique used to decrease the noise in gradient estimations for more stable model training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A statistical technique used to decrease the variability of an estimator to improve the accuracy of stochastic simulations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A stochastic optimization strategy that reduces the noise in gradient estimates to accelerate convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A stochastic optimization technique that stabilizes gradient estimates to accelerate convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique applied to stochastic optimization algorithms to decrease the noise in gradient estimates and improve convergence speed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique applied to stochastic optimization to accelerate convergence by reducing the noise in gradient estimates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique in stochastic optimization used to decrease the noise of gradient estimates to accelerate convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in stochastic gradient descent to accelerate convergence by reducing the noise associated with stochastic gradient estimates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in stochastic optimization to decrease the noise of gradient estimates and accelerate convergence rates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in stochastic optimization to decrease the noise of gradient estimates and accelerate convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used in stochastic optimization to lower the noise of gradient estimates for faster convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization strategy designed to decrease the noise in stochastic gradient estimates to accelerate convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization technique that accelerates convergence by reducing the noise in gradient estimates.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An optimization technique that reduces the noise in stochastic gradients to accelerate convergence.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[accelerate the convergence of stochastic gradient methods, accelerate convergence by reducing the noise of gradient estimates, decrease the noise in stochastic gradient estimates to accelerate convergence] accelerate the convergence of stochastic gradient methods</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[reduce the noise in stochastic gradient estimates to accelerate convergence, accelerate the convergence of stochastic gradient descent by reducing the noise in gradient estimates, decrease the noise in gradient estimators for models with discrete latent variables to speed up convergence, decrease the noise in gradient estimations for more stable model training, decrease the noise of gradient estimates to accelerate convergence, stochastic optimization algorithms to decrease the noise in gradient estimates and improve convergence speed, stochastic optimization to accelerate convergence by reducing the noise in gradient estimates] accelerate the convergence of stochastic gradient methods</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[decrease the finite sample variance of additive functionals of markov chains] decrease the finite sample variance of additive functionals of markov chains</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[decrease the variability of an estimator to improve the accuracy of stochastic simulations] decrease the variability of an estimator to improve the accuracy of stochastic simulations</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[noise of pixel estimates] noise of pixel estimates</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[noise of gradient estimates] gradient estimates</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[gradient estimates] gradient estimates</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of optimization techniques designed to accelerate the convergence of stochastic gradient methods.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of optimization techniques used to reduce the noise in stochastic gradient estimates to accelerate convergence.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A class of stochastic optimization techniques designed to accelerate convergence by reducing the noise of gradient estimates.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A family of optimization techniques designed to decrease the noise in stochastic gradient estimates to accelerate convergence.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of optimization techniques used to accelerate the convergence of stochastic gradient descent by reducing the noise in gradient estimates.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of techniques used to decrease the noise in gradient estimators for models with discrete latent variables to speed up convergence.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical method used to decrease the finite sample variance of additive functionals of Markov chains.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical technique used in Monte Carlo synthesis to decrease the noise and improve the accuracy of pixel estimates.</skos:definition>
