    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A statistical technique used to decrease the variability of an estimator to improve the accuracy of stochastic simulations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A stochastic optimization strategy that reduces the noise in gradient estimates to accelerate convergence.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A stochastic optimization technique that stabilizes gradient estimates to accelerate convergence.</skos:definition>
