    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning architecture suitable for long memory length channels used for symbol detection in mmWave systems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that processes sequential data in both forward and backward directions to capture full context.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture that processes sequential data in both forward and backward directions to capture global context.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural architecture trained to predict sequences in both positive and negative time directions simultaneously.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that jointly generates part-of-speech tags and lemmas using character-level and word-level embeddings.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that processes data in both forward and backward directions to capture temporal dependencies.</skos:definition>
