    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that trains a binary classifier using only positive examples and a set of unlabeled data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that trains a model using a set of confirmed positive examples and a set of unlabeled data containing both positive and negative instances.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning paradigm that trains a model using a set of confirmed positive examples and a set of unlabeled examples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning approach for training a binary classifier using only positive and unlabeled data samples.</skos:definition>
