    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning approach that trains a model using a set of confirmed positive examples and a set of unlabeled data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning setting where only positive and unlabeled examples are available for training.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning setting where only positive examples are labeled and the remaining data is treated as unlabeled.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning task where the model is trained using only confirmed positive examples and an unlabeled set.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A semi-supervised learning task where the training set contains only confirmed positive examples and a set of unlabeled data.</skos:definition>
