  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#universaladversarialperturbation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Universaladversarialperturbation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single adversarial noise pattern that can be added to any input from a dataset to cause a model to misclassify it.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single input modification designed to compromise a model's availability by increasing processing latency across various frames.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single input modification that can cause a deep neural network to misclassify a wide variety of different images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single input noise pattern capable of causing a neural network to misclassify a wide range of different images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single input-agnostic noise pattern that can cause a deep learning model to misclassify most input samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single input-independent noise pattern that can cause a deep neural network to misclassify a wide range of different images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single input-independent noise pattern that can cause a machine learning model to misclassify a wide range of inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single input-independent noise pattern that can mislead a reinforcement learning policy across multiple instances.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single input-independent noise pattern that causes a machine learning model to misclassify a wide range of images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single input-independent noise pattern that successfully fools a neural network across a wide variety of images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single input-independent perturbation that can cause misclassification across a large fraction of images within a specific class.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single noise pattern added to input data that causes a machine learning model to misclassify a wide range of inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single noise pattern that can be added to any image within a broad class to change its predicted label.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single noise pattern that can be added to any input instance to mislead a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single noise pattern that can be applied to multiple images to cause a deep neural network to misclassify them.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single noise pattern that, when added to any input image, causes a neural network to consistently misclassify it.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single set of noise patterns that can fool multiple models or images across a dataset to alter perceived geometry.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single, image-agnostic noise pattern that can cause misclassification across multiple different inputs in a neural network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single, image-agnostic noise vector that causes a machine learning classifier to misclassify a wide range of inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single, input-agnostic noise pattern added to images or signals to mislead a machine learning model.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single, input-agnostic noise pattern that can cause a target model to misclassify a wide range of different input samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single, input-agnostic noise pattern that causes a model to misclassify a wide range of different inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single, input-independent noise pattern that can cause a deep neural network to misclassify a wide range of images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single, input-independent noise pattern that can cause a machine learning model to misclassify a wide range of images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single, input-independent perturbation that can cause a machine learning model to misclassify a wide range of images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A single, small-magnitude noise pattern that causes misclassification across a wide range of different input images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A small, data-free noise pattern that can be added to any input image to cause a neural network to make a prediction error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A small, example-independent noise pattern that degrades the performance of a machine learning model across multiple inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A small, token-agnostic vector added to input embeddings that causes a text classifier to misclassify inputs with high probability.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of adversarial attack that employs a single input-independent noise pattern to deceive deep neural networks across multiple different images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of image-agnostic noise that can mislead deep convolutional neural networks into making incorrect predictions regardless of the input image.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of input noise that contains dominant features capable of causing misclassification across a wide range of images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A type of input-agnostic noise that is designed to fool deep learning models across a wide range of data samples.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An image-agnostic noise pattern applied to sequential frames to induce failures in embodied vision navigation agents.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An image-agnostic noise pattern that causes a high probability of misclassification across a wide range of natural images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An input-agnostic noise pattern that can fool a deep convolutional network across a large portion of a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[multiple images to cause a deep neural network to misclassify them] multiple images to cause a deep neural network to misclassify them</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[sequential frames to induce failures in embodied vision navigation agents] sequential frames to induce failures in embodied vision navigation agents</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a single input-independent noise pattern] single input-independent noise pattern</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[dominant features capable of causing misclassification across a wide range of images] multiple images to cause a deep neural network to misclassify them</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[fool deep learning models across a wide range of data samples] fool deep learning models</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[model] model</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[model's availability] model's availability</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[multiple models or images] multiple models or images</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single adversarial noise pattern that can be added to any input from a dataset to cause a model to misclassify it.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single input modification designed to compromise a model's availability by increasing processing latency across various frames.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single input modification that can cause a deep neural network to misclassify a wide variety of different images.</skos:definition>
