    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single input-agnostic noise pattern that can cause a deep learning model to misclassify most input samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single input-independent noise pattern that can cause a deep neural network to misclassify a wide range of different images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single input-independent noise pattern that can cause a machine learning model to misclassify a wide range of inputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single input-independent noise pattern that can mislead a reinforcement learning policy across multiple instances.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single input-independent noise pattern that causes a machine learning model to misclassify a wide range of images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single input-independent noise pattern that successfully fools a neural network across a wide variety of images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single input-independent perturbation that can cause misclassification across a large fraction of images within a specific class.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single noise pattern added to input data that causes a machine learning model to misclassify a wide range of inputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single noise pattern that can be added to any image within a broad class to change its predicted label.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single noise pattern that can be added to any input instance to mislead a machine learning model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single noise pattern that can be applied to multiple images to cause a deep neural network to misclassify them.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single noise pattern that, when added to any input image, causes a neural network to consistently misclassify it.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single set of noise patterns that can fool multiple models or images across a dataset to alter perceived geometry.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single, image-agnostic noise pattern that can cause misclassification across multiple different inputs in a neural network.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single, image-agnostic noise vector that causes a machine learning classifier to misclassify a wide range of inputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single, input-agnostic noise pattern added to images or signals to mislead a machine learning model.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single, input-agnostic noise pattern that can cause a target model to misclassify a wide range of different input samples.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single, input-agnostic noise pattern that causes a model to misclassify a wide range of different inputs.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single, input-independent noise pattern that can cause a deep neural network to misclassify a wide range of images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single, input-independent noise pattern that can cause a machine learning model to misclassify a wide range of images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single, input-independent perturbation that can cause a machine learning model to misclassify a wide range of images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A single, small-magnitude noise pattern that causes misclassification across a wide range of different input images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A small, data-free noise pattern that can be added to any input image to cause a neural network to make a prediction error.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A small, example-independent noise pattern that degrades the performance of a machine learning model across multiple inputs.</skos:definition>
