  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#variationalquantumalgorithm">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Variationalquantumalgorithm</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid method that merges quantum simulation and quantum machine learning to classify phases of matter.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that optimizes a set of parameters in a quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that optimizes the parameters of a quantum circuit to solve a specific task.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that uses a classical optimizer to train a parameterized quantum circuit.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that uses a classical optimizer to tune the parameters of a quantum circuit.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that uses a parameterized quantum circuit to optimize a cost function on noisy quantum hardware.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that uses a parameterized quantum circuit to optimize a cost function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical approach that uses parameterized quantum circuits to optimize a cost function for tasks like matrix decomposition.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical method that optimizes parameters of a quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical method that optimizes parameters of a quantum circuit to simulate physical systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical method that uses a classical optimizer to train the parameters of a quantum circuit.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical method used to find the minimum of a cost function on near-term quantum devices.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical optimization method that tunes parameters of a quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical optimization method that uses parameterized quantum circuits to solve computational problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical optimization procedure that optimizes parameters within a quantum circuit to solve a specific problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical optimization procedure that updates the parameters of a quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical optimization routine that uses a parameterized quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical procedure that optimizes the parameters of a quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[phases of matter] phases of matter</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a classical optimizer] classical optimizer</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[find the minimum of a cost function on near-term quantum devices] find the minimum of a cost function on near-term quantum devices</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid method that merges quantum simulation and quantum machine learning to classify phases of matter.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that optimizes a set of parameters in a quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that optimizes the parameters of a quantum circuit to solve a specific task.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that uses a classical optimizer to train a parameterized quantum circuit.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that uses a classical optimizer to tune the parameters of a quantum circuit.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that uses a parameterized quantum circuit to optimize a cost function on noisy quantum hardware.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical algorithm that uses a parameterized quantum circuit to optimize a cost function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical approach that uses parameterized quantum circuits to optimize a cost function for tasks like matrix decomposition.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical method that optimizes parameters of a quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical method that optimizes parameters of a quantum circuit to simulate physical systems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical method that uses a classical optimizer to train the parameters of a quantum circuit.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical method used to find the minimum of a cost function on near-term quantum devices.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical optimization method that tunes parameters of a quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical optimization method that uses parameterized quantum circuits to solve computational problems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical optimization procedure that optimizes parameters within a quantum circuit to solve a specific problem.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical optimization procedure that updates the parameters of a quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical optimization routine that uses a parameterized quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid quantum-classical procedure that optimizes the parameters of a quantum circuit to minimize a cost function.</skos:definition>
