  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#deep_residual_network">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Deep Residual Network</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture composed of near-identity mappings that can represent smooth bi-Lipschitz functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs shortcut connections to allow gradients to flow through the network more easily, mitigating the vanishing gradient problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs shortcut connections to allow gradients to flow through very deep layers without vanishing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs shortcut connections to facilitate the training of very deep models for tasks like image denoising.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs shortcut connections to mitigate the vanishing gradient problem during training.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs skip connections to allow the training of extremely deep layers by mitigating the vanishing gradient problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs skip connections to facilitate the training of very deep models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to allow gradients to flow through very deep layers without vanishing.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to allow the training of very deep layers.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to approximate high-dimensional random partial differential equations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to facilitate the training of very deep models for analyzing fermionic systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to facilitate the training of very deep models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to improve the accuracy and generalization of short-term power load forecasting.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to train very deep models for classifying the severity of autoimmune diseases from histological images.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An ultra-deep neural network architecture used to predict protein contacts by integrating evolutionary coupling and sequence conservation information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[predict protein contacts by integrating evolutionary coupling and sequence conservation information] predict protein contacts by integrating evolutionary coupling and sequence conservation information</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[smooth bi-Lipschitz functions] smooth bi-lipschitz functions</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture composed of near-identity mappings that can represent smooth bi-Lipschitz functions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs shortcut connections to allow gradients to flow through the network more easily, mitigating the vanishing gradient problem.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs shortcut connections to allow gradients to flow through very deep layers without vanishing.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs shortcut connections to facilitate the training of very deep models for tasks like image denoising.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs shortcut connections to mitigate the vanishing gradient problem during training.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs skip connections to allow the training of extremely deep layers by mitigating the vanishing gradient problem.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that employs skip connections to facilitate the training of very deep models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to allow gradients to flow through very deep layers without vanishing.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to allow the training of very deep layers.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to approximate high-dimensional random partial differential equations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to facilitate the training of very deep models for analyzing fermionic systems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to facilitate the training of very deep models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to improve the accuracy and generalization of short-term power load forecasting.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that uses skip connections to train very deep models for classifying the severity of autoimmune diseases from histological images.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An ultra-deep neural network architecture used to predict protein contacts by integrating evolutionary coupling and sequence conservation information.</skos:definition>
