    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method for autonomously developing pixel-wise representations in video streams using a human-like attention mechanism and contrastive learning.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method for learning generic and transferable features from large-scale unlabeled data across different modalities.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of extracting meaningful features from unlabeled data using local learning rules inspired by the neocortex.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of extracting meaningful features from unlabeled data without the need for explicit ground-truth targets.</skos:definition>
