  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#kernel_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Kernel Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that uses kernel functions to map data into high-dimensional feature spaces to perform linear separation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that uses similarity functions to map data into high-dimensional feature spaces for analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning method that uses kernel functions to map data into high-dimensional spaces to perform non-linear regression or classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for adaptively selecting an optimal reproducing kernel Hilbert space to minimize regularized risk.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for approximating high-dimensional feature spaces using fast basis function expansions for better scalability.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for automatically selecting or constructing the most appropriate kernel function for a dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for computing similarity matrices between data points to facilitate tasks like clustering.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for constructing a similarity matrix between data points to enable linear algorithms to operate in a high-dimensional feature space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for estimating a positive semidefinite matrix that defines the similarity between objects.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for optimizing the kernel function used in machine learning algorithms to better capture data similarities.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for optimizing the parameters of a kernel function to improve the performance of a learning algorithm.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method that uses kernel functions to map data into high-dimensional spaces to perform non-linear regression or classification.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for automatically discovering an optimal similarity function to be used within a support vector machine.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for optimizing similarity functions using centered alignment to improve classification and regression performance.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for producing feature maps to refine the margin of a support vector machine using Fourier-analytic characterization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process of estimating a similarity function that defines the distance between objects in a high-dimensional space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique that optimizes the choice of a kernel function to improve the performance of a machine learning model in tasks like change-point detection.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A technique used to optimize the similarity function that maps input data into a high-dimensional feature space.</rdfs:comment>
