  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#physics_informed_deep_learning">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Physics-Informed Deep Learning</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A deep learning approach that incorporates physical priors and domain knowledge into the model architecture or loss function to solve scientific problems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that incorporates physical constraints, such as governing equations, into neural network predictions to calibrate constitutive models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that integrates known physical laws or constraints into a neural network's architecture or loss function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that integrates physical laws and differential equations into neural network architectures to discover governing equations from data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A framework that integrates physical laws, often expressed as partial differential equations, into the loss function of a neural network to constrain its predictions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid framework that integrates known physical models and constraints into neural networks for image reconstruction.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid framework that integrates physical traffic flow models with data-driven neural networks to improve state estimation with limited data.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid modeling approach that integrates physical laws or constraints into the architecture and loss functions of a neural network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A hybrid paradigm that integrates physical laws and model-driven components into deep learning architectures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that incorporates physical laws and governing equations into the training process to improve model accuracy and data efficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that incorporates physical laws and theories into the neural network architecture or loss function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that integrates physical laws, such as partial differential equations, into the neural network's loss function or architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A machine learning framework that incorporates physical laws or constraints into the loss function or architecture.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A modeling framework that integrates physical laws and mathematical constraints into neural network architectures to guide the learning process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that integrates physics-based models to improve data efficiency and interpretability in predictive tasks.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural network framework that integrates physical laws or constraints into the learning process.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An approach that uses background knowledge from physical laws as a guideline for designing efficient neural network models.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[physical priors and domain knowledge] physical priors and domain knowledge</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[physical constraints] physical constraints</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[physical laws and governing equations] physical laws and governing equations</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[physical laws or constraints] physical constraints</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[physical traffic flow models] physical traffic flow models</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[physical laws/constraints into neural network architecture or loss function] physical laws/constraints into neural network architecture or loss function</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A deep learning approach that incorporates physical priors and domain knowledge into the model architecture or loss function to solve scientific problems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that incorporates physical constraints, such as governing equations, into neural network predictions to calibrate constitutive models.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that integrates known physical laws or constraints into a neural network's architecture or loss function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that integrates physical laws and differential equations into neural network architectures to discover governing equations from data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A framework that integrates physical laws, often expressed as partial differential equations, into the loss function of a neural network to constrain its predictions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid framework that integrates known physical models and constraints into neural networks for image reconstruction.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid framework that integrates physical traffic flow models with data-driven neural networks to improve state estimation with limited data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid modeling approach that integrates physical laws or constraints into the architecture and loss functions of a neural network.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A hybrid paradigm that integrates physical laws and model-driven components into deep learning architectures.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that incorporates physical laws and governing equations into the training process to improve model accuracy and data efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that incorporates physical laws and theories into the neural network architecture or loss function.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning approach that integrates physical laws, such as partial differential equations, into the neural network's loss function or architecture.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A machine learning framework that incorporates physical laws or constraints into the loss function or architecture.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A modeling framework that integrates physical laws and mathematical constraints into neural network architectures to guide the learning process.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network architecture that integrates physics-based models to improve data efficiency and interpretability in predictive tasks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A neural network framework that integrates physical laws or constraints into the learning process.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An approach that uses background knowledge from physical laws as a guideline for designing efficient neural network models.</skos:definition>
