    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal method used to determine the set of all possible states a system can reach from an initial set of conditions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification approach used to compute interval over-approximations of the output set of neural networks given input uncertainty.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification method that computes an over-approximation of all possible states a dynamical system can reach over a time horizon.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification method that computes the set of all possible states a dynamic system can reach from a given set of initial conditions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification method that computes the set of all possible states a system can reach from a given set of initial conditions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification method used to determine all possible states a system can reach from a given set of initial conditions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification method used to determine if a system can enter a specific set of unsafe states from a given set of initial conditions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification method used to determine the set of all possible states a system can reach given a set of initial conditions and inputs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification method used to encapsulate safety constraints in the training of neural network controllers for robotic systems.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification method used to estimate the set of states a closed-loop system with a neural network controller can reach over time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification technique that computes the set of all possible states a system can reach from a given set of initial conditions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A formal verification technique used to determine if a system can enter a specific set of unsafe states.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for determining whether a neural network can produce a specific arbitrary output given its activation functions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A verification method for neural networks that uses MILP encodings to determine if a system is locally robust under specific transformations.</rdfs:comment>
