  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#counterfactual_fairness">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Counterfactual Fairness</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fairness criterion based on causal inference that ensures a decision remains the same in both the actual and a counterfactual world.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fairness criterion in machine learning that ensures a decision remains the same in a world where a sensitive attribute was changed.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fairness criterion requiring that a model's prediction remains unchanged if a sensitive attribute is altered in a counterfactual scenario.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fairness criterion stating that a prediction is fair if it remains unchanged when a protected attribute is counterfactually altered.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fairness criterion that ensures a decision remains the same in a world where a sensitive attribute of an individual was different.</rdfs:comment>
