  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#differentiable_architecture_search">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Differentiable Architecture Search</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for automating neural network design that uses continuous relaxation of the architecture representation to enable gradient descent optimization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for automating the design of neural network architectures by optimizing a continuous relaxation of the search space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method for automating the design of neural network architectures by optimizing continuous parameters.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A method of optimizing neural network topologies by treating the search space as a continuous, differentiable objective.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology for automating the design of neural network architectures by optimizing a continuous relaxation of the search space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that optimizes a neural network's topology by treating the search space as a continuous, differentiable function.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A methodology that uses gradient-based optimization to automatically discover the optimal structure of a neural network.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture search method that optimizes the network structure using gradient-based optimization on a continuous relaxation of the search space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture search method that uses a differentiable relaxation to optimize the network structure.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture search method that uses continuous relaxation of the search space to identify optimal network structures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A neural architecture search method that uses continuous relaxation to optimize the network structure via gradient descent.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An AutoML technique that optimizes a neural network's structure by treating the architecture parameters as continuous variables.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An algorithm for neural architecture search that optimizes the network structure using gradient-based methods.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An automated machine learning method that optimizes the network structure by treating the architecture as a continuous differentiable variable.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An automated method for designing neural network architectures by optimizing a continuous relaxation of the search space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An automated method for discovering optimal neural network topologies by optimizing architecture parameters via gradient descent.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An automated method for finding optimal neural network structures using gradient-based optimization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An automated method for finding the optimal neural network structure by optimizing a continuous relaxation of the architecture space.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An automated method for optimizing neural network structures by treating the architecture search space as a continuous optimization problem.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An automated process for designing neural network architectures by optimizing the structure using gradient descent.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An automated process that optimizes the structure of a neural network using gradient-based methods.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[continuous relaxation of the architecture representation] continuous relaxation of the architecture representation</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[gradient-based optimization on a continuous relaxation of the search space, continuous relaxation of the search space] continuous relaxation of the search space</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[neural network architectures, neural network topologies, neural network structure, neural network structures] neural network structure</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method for automating neural network design that uses continuous relaxation of the architecture representation to enable gradient descent optimization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method for automating the design of neural network architectures by optimizing a continuous relaxation of the search space.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method for automating the design of neural network architectures by optimizing continuous parameters.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of optimizing neural network topologies by treating the search space as a continuous, differentiable objective.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A methodology for automating the design of neural network architectures by optimizing a continuous relaxation of the search space.</skos:definition>
