  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#low_rank_approximation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Low-Rank Approximation</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction process that approximates a high-order tensor with a simpler structure to reduce computational cost.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that approximates a high-dimensional matrix with a matrix of lower rank.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that approximates a matrix using a smaller number of singular values.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that represents a matrix as a product of smaller matrices to capture primary structures.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique used to approximate a large matrix with a product of smaller matrices to reduce computational cost.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical process of finding a matrix or operator of lower rank that closely approximates a given high-rank matrix.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that approximates a positive semidefinite matrix from partial entries using nonconvex optimization.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that computes a relative-error approximation of a positive semidefinite matrix in sublinear time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that finds a matrix or quantum state of limited rank that best approximates a given high-rank object.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique used to approximate a high-dimensional kernel by a matrix of lower rank to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix compression technique that approximates a high-dimensional matrix with one of lower rank to reduce memory usage.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition technique that reduces the computational complexity and memory footprint of a model by approximating large matrices with lower-dimensional representations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix factorization method that represents a high-dimensional matrix with a simpler version of reduced rank.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix factorization technique that approximates a large matrix with one of significantly lower rank to reduce dimensionality.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix factorization technique that finds a lower-dimensional representation of a matrix to minimize the error under a specific norm.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix factorization technique that produces a simplified version of a large matrix to minimize spectral or Frobenius error.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A matrix factorization technique used to reduce the dimensionality of large kernel matrices while preserving essential information.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model compression method that reduces the number of parameters by approximating matrices with lower-rank versions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A numerical method for approximating a large matrix with a matrix of significantly lower rank to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A numerical method that approximates a high-dimensional matrix with a matrix of lower rank to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A numerical method that simplifies a large matrix by approximating it with a matrix of significantly lower rank.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A numerical method used to approximate a high-dimensional covariance operator with a simpler, lower-dimensional representation for efficient sampling.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A numerical technique that approximates a large matrix with one of lower rank to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A numerical technique that simplifies a large matrix by representing it as a product of smaller matrices to reduce computational complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A numerical technique used to approximate a high-dimensional matrix with a matrix of lower rank to reduce complexity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a smaller number of singular values] smaller number of singular values</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[approximate a large matrix with a product of smaller matrices to reduce computational cost, approximate a high-dimensional kernel by a matrix of lower rank to reduce computational complexity, reduce the dimensionality of large kernel matrices while preserving essential information, approximate a high-dimensional matrix with a matrix of lower rank to reduce complexity] approximate a high-dimensional matrix with a matrix of lower rank to reduce complexity</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[approximate a high-dimensional covariance operator with a simpler] approximate a high-dimensional covariance operator with a simpler</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[high-dimensional matrix, a large matrix with a lower-rank matrix] high-dimensional matrix</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[matrix] matrix</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[a large matrix as a product of smaller matrices] high-dimensional matrix</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">[relative-error approximation] relative-error approximation</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction process that approximates a high-order tensor with a simpler structure to reduce computational cost.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that approximates a high-dimensional matrix with a matrix of lower rank.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that approximates a matrix using a smaller number of singular values.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique that represents a matrix as a product of smaller matrices to capture primary structures.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A dimensionality reduction technique used to approximate a large matrix with a product of smaller matrices to reduce computational cost.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical process of finding a matrix or operator of lower rank that closely approximates a given high-rank matrix.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that approximates a positive semidefinite matrix from partial entries using nonconvex optimization.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that computes a relative-error approximation of a positive semidefinite matrix in sublinear time.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique that finds a matrix or quantum state of limited rank that best approximates a given high-rank object.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A mathematical technique used to approximate a high-dimensional kernel by a matrix of lower rank to reduce computational complexity.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A matrix compression technique that approximates a high-dimensional matrix with one of lower rank to reduce memory usage.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A matrix decomposition technique that reduces the computational complexity and memory footprint of a model by approximating large matrices with lower-dimensional representations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A matrix factorization method that represents a high-dimensional matrix with a simpler version of reduced rank.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A matrix factorization technique that approximates a large matrix with one of significantly lower rank to reduce dimensionality.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A matrix factorization technique that finds a lower-dimensional representation of a matrix to minimize the error under a specific norm.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A matrix factorization technique that produces a simplified version of a large matrix to minimize spectral or Frobenius error.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A matrix factorization technique used to reduce the dimensionality of large kernel matrices while preserving essential information.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A model compression method that reduces the number of parameters by approximating matrices with lower-rank versions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A numerical method for approximating a large matrix with a matrix of significantly lower rank to reduce computational complexity.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A numerical method that approximates a high-dimensional matrix with a matrix of lower rank to reduce computational complexity.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A numerical method that simplifies a large matrix by approximating it with a matrix of significantly lower rank.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A numerical method used to approximate a high-dimensional covariance operator with a simpler, lower-dimensional representation for efficient sampling.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A numerical technique that approximates a large matrix with one of lower rank to reduce computational complexity.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A numerical technique that simplifies a large matrix by representing it as a product of smaller matrices to reduce computational complexity.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A numerical technique used to approximate a high-dimensional matrix with a matrix of lower rank to reduce complexity.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#optimization_and_compression_algorithm"/>
    <ml:hasComponent rdf:resource="http://linqubit.co/ontology/ml_concepts#nonconvex_optimization"/>
